  {"a":"ksante","b":"aatrox","win":["Skill","Skill","Aatrox","Aatrox","Skill","Aatrox","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online — W an Aatrox who steps in for a sweetspot Q and Q3 knock him up before his drain kicks in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His All Out / Aatrox's R: his combat-stat ult turns extended trades lethal — your R strips your own tankiness, so do not flip the duel here unless your W is up to blank his Q knockups."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Aatrox with Eclipse/first item + R uptime owns the side lane — your Iceborn/tank piece keeps you alive but you out-DPS nothing here, you survive and farm."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your second tank item plus W-unstoppable lets you eat his full Q-W-R rotation and peel him off — the lane swings back to you as a teamfight tank."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and W a committed Aatrox so his sweetspot Q whiffs, then Q3 knock-up","Sidestep Infernal Chains, then trade while Deathbringer Stance is down — Bramble blunts the rest","Survive his Level 6-to-1-item window and scale into a 2-item tank who out-peels his all-in"],"foe":["Land all three sweetspot Q knockups to stack his passive heal and win the extended trade","Hit his W chain-pull to drag you back into Q range and deny your W disengage","Pop R at 6 for the combat-stat all-in while you have no second item to absorb it"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are even scuffle territory — I only have Q and no engage, and Aatrox is just as weak before his sweetspots are reliable, so I farm with the tip of Q and respect his W chain-pull. At 3 I get my real window: my full Q-W is online, so if he walks up to land his Q edges I W to become unstoppable, eat the knockup, and Q3 him up before his drain passive heals him back. Do not stand on the inner sweetspot of his Q — that is the part that knocks up and feeds his sustain.","mid":"Levels 4-5 I can still bank small trades with my bulk, but from 6 this is his lane. His R gives combat stats and turns every extended fight into a drain-tank duel he wins, and if I flip my own R I throw away the tankiness that is my whole answer to him. So I hold R, use W purely to dodge his Q knockups and his W chain-pull, and refuse the long trade — I trade the first two hits and walk, never the drawn-out fight where his passive heal out-paces me.","late":"This is where I reclaim it. With two tank items my W-unstoppable lets me absorb his full Q-W-R combo, and my R becomes a peel tool — I dash through him, knock him off my carry, and recast to drag him out when he dives. His drain all-in needs a target to sustain on; deny him a clean 1v1 and bring him into my team, where his single-target damage gets eaten while I stay durable. Close fights around my second item, not on a side-lane duel he is built to win.","whys":["I only have Q with no engage and he has no reliable sweetspot yet — we both just farm, so last-hit at Q range and do not flip a fight neither of us controls.","He picks up his second ability and so do I; trades stay even because his drain heal and my bulk cancel out before our combos come fully online.","The Darkin Blade sweetspots knock me up and Infernal Chains drags me back in; Deathbringer Stance heals him off my max health through all my chip.","With R up and his sustain rolling he owns the drawn-out fight; my bulk banks nothing if I stand in his drain, so I only short-trade and walk.","All Out gives him combat stats for a lethal all-in, and if I flip my own R I lose the tankiness that is my only answer — the duel is his.","His first item plus R uptime out-DPS my tank piece in the side lane; I survive and farm but I win no straight trade here.","Two tank items plus W's charge-up damage reduction let me eat The Darkin Blade and R-peel him off my carry — his single-target drain fades on my durability."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"akali","win":["K'Sante","Skill","Akali","Akali","Akali","Akali","Akali"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"My full Q-W combo comes online — if Akali walks up to last-hit I can W-charge into her, Q3 the knock-up-and-pull, but she just E-dashes or Shrouds out of the lockup."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Akali's spike, not mine — All Out strips my tankiness while her R two-part dash plus shuriken execute can chunk my now-squishy duelist profile before I land a Q3."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Her threat peak: with her first AP item her shuriken-into-R burst beats my Iceborn-Gauntlet bulk because magic damage and her untargetable Shroud ignore my armor stacking."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"My reclaim window — two tank items and R let me survive her full combo through W's damage resist and recall-peel her out of the fight with R's second cast."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her W Twilight Shroud and E dash early, then W-charge unstoppable into her and Q3 knock-up-pull the instant her escapes are down","Drag the lane to 2+ tank items where I survive her burst through W's damage resist and R-peel her instead of dueling her squishy-vs-squishy at 6","Keep a control ward for her Shroud so my Q stacks and W stun actually land instead of hitting an empty cloud"],"foe":["Drop W Twilight Shroud to go untargetable, dodge my Q3 and W charge, and reset her assassin combo for free","Hit level 6 and use All Out's stat-strip against me — burst my duelist-profile body with R dash-execute before I peel","Scale to her first AP item where shuriken poke and reset burst ignore my armor and punish every cooldown I whiff"]},"early":"Level 1 is mine for once — I only have Q but so does Akali, and she has no Shroud yet, so I can W-bump her off a cautious last-hit and Q-poke without eating a real answer. By level 2-3 it evens out and then tips: once she has W Twilight Shroud and E shuriken-dash, my whole combo gets blanked — I W-charge in unstoppable, she Shrouds untargetable and my Q3 pull grabs nothing. Never blow my full Q-W on a target who can vanish; bait the Shroud first, farm safe, and only commit when her cloud is on cooldown.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are Akali's. My tank trading pattern wants to bank small leads around her cooldowns, but she refuses the extended fight — she pokes with shuriken, E-dashes out, and Shrouds whenever I W-charge in. At 6 it gets worse, not better: All Out strips my bulk to turn me into a duelist, but against an assassin that just hands her a squishy target for her R two-part dash and execute. Don't ult to fight her at 6 — my R is for surviving and peeling, not for racing burst with Akali. Hold W to eat her R recast damage and look to land Q3-into-wall stun the moment she lands next to me out of Shroud.","late":"This is where I claw it back. By 2+ items I'm stacking armor and HP, and even though her magic burst ignores armor, W's flat damage resist plus the sheer health pool let me survive her full combo where a squishy couldn't. More importantly the game stops being a 1v1 — All Out's recall second-cast lets me dive past her Shroud, peel her off my carry, and drag her into my team. I don't win the isolated sidelane duel against a fed Akali, so I group: my job is to eat her engage with W, then R her out of the fight so my team kills her while she's stripped of escape.","whys":["I'm weak at level 1 but so is Akali, and she has no W Shroud yet — I can W-bump her off a last-hit and Q-poke with no clean answer coming back.","Even — my Q out-cleaves her early but she can E-dash the W charge and trade shuriken poke back, so neither of us lands a committed hit.","Her W Twilight Shroud and E dash come online and blank my combo — I W in unstoppable but she goes untargetable and my Q3 pull grabs an empty cloud.","She refuses my extended tank trade, poking with shuriken and Shrouding every time I charge, so I can't bank the lane leads my bulk usually wins.","All Out strips my tankiness into a duelist profile, which only feeds her assassin pattern — her R two-part dash and execute beat my now-squishy body before I land Q3.","Her first AP item makes shuriken-and-reset burst lethal, and magic damage plus untargetable Shroud ignore the armor stacking that's supposed to be my answer.","By 2+ items W's damage resist and my health pool let me survive her full combo, and R's recall second-cast peels her out of the fight where a squishy can't follow."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"akshan","win":["Akshan","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Akshan","K'Sante","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Ntofo Strikes plus Path Maker combo comes online — if he steps in to Q-poke, charge W into him and land Q3's knock-up-and-pull before his E swing can reset the gap."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Akshan's poke window: his Q Avengerang and E swing-shot let him chip your low-econ tank body from a range your short Q can't answer until you have W up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out flips you to a duelist profile with bonus range — you survive Avengerang poke through the dash and out-DPS a squishy Akshan whose only cushion is his three-hit shield."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet plus your W stun pins him; once he can't kite on his E swing your sustained tank DPS through Dauntless Instinct marks runs him down."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach level 3 and bank the Path Maker (W) charge into a terrain stun so Q3's knock-up-and-pull lands before his E swing resets","Use All Out (R) to dash through him and convert to the duelist profile, surviving his Q/W poke and running him down with Dauntless Instinct move speed","Buy Iceborn Gauntlet and force side-lane fights where his E grapple has no terrain to swing off and escape your W stun"],"foe":["Kite-skirmish with E swing-shots, staying outside your short Ntofo Strikes (Q) range so he pokes your tank body for free","Chip you down with Avengerang and his double-shot passive before you bank a lead, then roam off Heroic Swing","Stall lane and abuse his camouflage passive plus revive to snowball other lanes while you can't catch him"]},"early":"Level 1 is mine to take — Akshan has no engage and I farm safely, but the instant I have my Ntofo Strikes Q stacks and a point in Path Maker W at level 2-3, his Q Avengerang and E swing-shot poke start chipping my low-econ tank body from outside my short range. Don't chase his swing with a raw Q he'll just kite; hold the wave and bait him into Q-range to last-hit. The trick is my W: charge it when he steps up and the unstoppable dash slams him into terrain for a stun he can't grapple out of, then Q3 knock-up-and-pulls him for a real trade.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a coin-flip — he has full E swing mobility and Q/W poke to kite my cooldown-reliant pattern, so I respect the skirmish, farm with Q's cleave, and only commit W when I can pin him to a wall. Then level 6 flips it my way: All Out dashes me through him, gives me bonus range, and converts my tank stats into a duelist profile, so I survive his poke through the dash and out-DPS a squishy who has no burst to punish a tank. Bait his E swing first, then R through him onto terrain — once he's stunned and can't kite, my Dauntless Instinct marks and move speed run him down.","late":"This is my window, not his. With Iceborn Gauntlet and a tank-engage item I'm durable and my W stun plus Q slow shut down his only out — the E grapple swing — so I force side-lane fights where there's a wall to pin him against. His Q/W poke does nothing meaningful to my HP pool late, and his armor-shredding skirmisher damage can't out-trade my sustained tank DPS once I'm on top of him. Just don't let him farm free and roam: his camouflage passive and revive make him a map threat, so close the side lane on top of him and use R to recall him out of position into my team.","whys":["Akshan has no engage at level 1 and you concede nothing — farm safely with Ntofo Strikes (Q) while his lone Q Avengerang can't punish a tank yet.","He picks up his E swing-shot and Q poke and starts chipping your low-econ body from outside your short Q range, so the level-2 window is his.","His full kite kit is online — E swing mobility plus Q/W poke lets him skirmish your cooldown-reliant pattern and dodge your short Path Maker (W) charge.","It's even — you can bank a W terrain stun into Q3's knock-up-and-pull if he oversteps, but his E swing resets the gap if he plays it clean.","All Out converts you to a duelist with bonus range and dashes you through his poke — a squishy Akshan has no burst to punish a tank and you out-DPS him here.","Iceborn Gauntlet plus your W stun pins him off his E swing, and your sustained tank DPS through Dauntless Instinct marks out-trades his skirmisher poke.","Late, Avengerang and his Dirty Fighting shield do nothing to your HP pool while your W stun denies the grapple — force side-lane fights and R him out of position."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"ambessa","win":["Skill","Skill","Ambessa","K'Sante","Ambessa","Ambessa","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online — W her against the wave to wall-stun, then two Ntofo stacks to pull her in, the one melee trade she cannot dash out of at 3."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ambessa's window: All Out strips your tankiness for a duelist profile, but her chain-CC plus W damage out-trades that squishier form unless you W her burst first and bait her dashes."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Her threat peak: Ambessa's first bruiser item plus her dash-reset combo lets her chain-CC and W-burst you faster than your Iceborn slow can lock her down."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your spike at last: a two-item control-tank K'Sante eats her sustained DPS, peels with R All Out, and out-survives the extended fight she relied on winning."}],"wants":{"you":["Land W Path Maker against the wave to wall-stun her, then two Ntofo stacks to pull her into your marked attack","Hold E Footwork as a disengage to escape her dash-in chain-CC rather than spending it to chase","Drag the lane to two items, with a Grievous Wounds component so her R healing cannot out-pace your bulk"],"foe":["Weave her dashes around your short Q and the wind-up on W so both whiff and she takes no CC","Land her chain-CC to lock you through your W charge and W-burst your duelist form during All Out","Snowball her first-item dash-reset combo before your two-item tank bulk comes online"]},"early":"Ambessa has no ranged poke, so levels 1-2 are a farm standoff — I have only Q with no engage threat at 1 and can't punish her dash mobility yet, so I last-hit with the tip of Ntofo Strikes and concede nothing. The danger is her dash-heavy combo closing on me against the wave, so I never shove blind into a spot where she can W-burst me. My one window is level 3 when the full Q-W combo lands: I charge W Path Maker into her to wall-stun, then Q3 to knock up and pull — that's the one melee trade she can't dash out of, so I only commit it when she oversteps.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are mine to control as a tank — I trade around her cooldowns, bank small leads with my bulk, and hold E Footwork as my escape instead of burning it to engage, because she will dash in and chain-CC me the instant I commit. Level 6 flips to her: All Out converts my tank stats into a squishier duelist profile, and that's exactly the form her W damage and CC chain out-trade, so I don't pop R hoping to 1v1 a full-health Ambessa with her dashes up. I bait her dash-chain and her ult out first, then either W her burst as a non-ulted tank or save All Out to peel, never to open.","late":"Her first-item dash-reset combo is the scariest stretch — she chains CC and W-bursts me before my Iceborn slow can lock her down, so I play for scaling, not a coin-flip duel. At two-plus items the lane finally turns back to me: a full control-tank K'Sante eats her sustained DPS, my armor and HP stacking survive the extended fight she needs to win, and R All Out lets me dash through her, knock her back, and recall-peel her off my carries in any 5v5. I stop trying to solo-duel a fed Ambessa in the sidelane and bring my W lockdown and R peel to the teamfight where my bulk, not her burst, decides it.","whys":["She has no ranged tool and I have no engage at level 1, so this opens as a pure farm standoff — last-hit with Q range and don't get caught against the wave.","It stays even — my W-Q combo isn't fully online and her dashes let her sidestep a lone Q, so neither of us can commit a clean trade yet.","Her level-3 dash-chain and W damage out-trade my full combo if she dodges the wind-up on W Path Maker, so she edges the early skirmish window.","I reclaim lane control as a tank — I trade around her cooldowns and bank small leads with my bulk, holding E to disengage her dash-in.","All Out strips my tankiness for a duelist profile, and her chain-CC plus W-burst beats that squishier form — she owns the level-6 all-in.","Her first bruiser item powers a dash-reset combo that chain-CCs and bursts me before my Iceborn slow locks her down — this is her snowball peak.","Two-item control-tank K'Sante out-survives her sustained DPS and R All Out peels her off my carries, so the extended fight she needed finally swings to me."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"aurora","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q3 knock-up + pull lands once you have the full Q-W combo, but Aurora's E blink dodges the W charge if you telegraph it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out gives you a duelist 1v1, yet it strips your tankiness right as Between Worlds (140s) drops a slow zone she teleports across to burst you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Even durable on Iceborn Gauntlet, you eat Twofold Hex walking up — she owns the side lane whenever Across the Veil is off cooldown."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Teamfights flip to you: R All Out yanks Aurora out of her backline poke and your bulk soaks her single rotation."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Across the Veil, its 22s, then commit W so the charge is not simply blinked","Use E over the wall or to minions to close her Q poke gap and force a Q3 pull","Survive lane EVEN and reach 2+ items where R drags her out of teamfights"],"foe":["Poke you down with Q every time you walk up to last-hit","Hold Across the Veil (22s) to blink your W charge and Q3 pull","Drop Between Worlds so its slow zone traps your stripped-down All Out"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — you only have Q and no engage, she only has Q poke, so trade short and farm. The moment she hits 2-3 she starts winning: her Q chips you every time you step to a minion, and your only answer is the short Q cleave she just walks out of. Don't throw W blind — she holds E blink for exactly that, and a dodged W is a free poke window for her. Bank CS, eat the chip, and accept she controls the tempo here.","mid":"This is her peak and your hardest stretch. At 6 your R is a trap: it gives you a duelist 1v1 but converts your tank stats into a squishier profile, and that's precisely when her W exile + root-burst can actually kill you. Only ult if you've already baited E and have her pinned against terrain with W. Otherwise hold defensive — use E over a wall to dodge her root, walk her down only when her blink is on cooldown, and force a Q3 pull-in the instant she's out of position. If you can't pin her, just farm even and don't feed the ulting form.","late":"Now it tilts to you. Once you have 2+ items the lane becomes a teamfight, and that's your kit's whole point — R All Out lets you dash through Aurora and recall her out of her backline, dragging her off her poke perch and into your team. Your bulk soaks one of her rotations where a squishy can't, and your W peel shields a carry through her burst. Don't try to solo-kill her in a sidelane where she kites with E and Q; group, find the R pick on her, and let your durability win the 5v5 her poke can't.","whys":["Level 1 is even — you have only Q with no engage and she has only Q poke, so trade short and farm the wave.","At 2 her Q poke starts chipping you every walk-up while your short Q cleave can't punish her back — she owns the tempo.","She holds Across the Veil (W, 22s) to blink your charge, the two-stack pull, so she pokes safely and you cannot commit.","Levels 4-5 are her control window — she kites your short-range combo with E and bleeds you with Q while you just farm.","At 6 your All Out strips your tankiness, and Between Worlds slows you in its zone while she teleports across it to burst you.","On her first item she pokes you out of the sidelane and blinks any all-in — durable or not, you can't pin her down.","From 2+ items it flips to you: R All Out drags her out of the backline and your bulk soaks her single rotation in the 5v5."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"camille","win":["Skill","Camille","Camille","Camille","Camille","Camille","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online: W-charge into a committed Camille, then two Ntofo stacks pull her in — your first real trading window against her 325-range Q."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"The Hextech Ultimatum (140s at rank 1) anchors you into the isolated 1v1 her kit is built for, and All Out strips your bulk right when her Hookshot stun lands."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Her Sheen/Trinity spike: Hookshot stun into a Tactical Sweep that heals off its outer half, plus a Q proc, out-trades your single tank item."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your threat window flips here for once: full tank build with Iceborn and a second armor item, you become an unkillable R-peel that her true damage chips but never kills."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold W (Path Maker) unstoppable for her E hookshot engage, then release the wall-stun to interrupt her W cone and Q true-damage burst","Land the two-stack Ntofo Strikes pull when she dashes in so she cannot reposition with her Hookshot second cast","Build early armor and tenacity so her Q true-damage proc and W cone don't delete your stacks, and stay near walls so her E dash is predictable"],"foe":["Engage with E hookshot stun, then weave Q true-damage procs and W cone heal to out-sustain your trades in melee","Use R (Hextech Ultimatum) to isolate you in a 1v1 where her items beat your stripped-down All Out duelist form","Dodge your short Q and W with E wall-dash and second-cast reposition, then scale to two items where her percent-true damage ignores your armor"]},"early":"Level 1 I have only Ntofo Strikes and no engage, so I concede the first level and just farm at Q range — Camille has no reason to commit either with just her Q proc up. By level 2 I take W or E and get safer, and at 3 my Q-W combo is online for my first real trade: if she steps in to last-hit, I can W-charge unstoppable through her poke and Q3 her for the knock-up and pull. The thing to never do is eat her E hookshot stun into the wall — that stun into her Q true-damage proc and W cone is what flips a trade against my low-econ early, so I hold W to answer her engage, not to start one.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a respect stretch — her Q stacks true damage that ignores my armor and her W cone heals her through my Q poke, so I trade around her cooldowns and bank small leads with my bulk rather than dueling her toe-to-toe. At 6 the lane tilts to her: her R isolates me into the exact 1v1 her kit is built for, and the moment I pop All Out to win that duel I strip my own tankiness right as her E stun combo lands hardest. So I don't gamble All Out into a healthy Camille with R up — I bait her E hookshot, W-stun her into the wall to interrupt the W cone, and only commit when her dash is on cooldown and she can't second-cast away.","late":"Her first item is her takeover: Sheen/Trinity turns the E-stun-into-W-cone-and-Q-proc rotation into a trade that out-sustains my tank build, and Hextech Ultimatum walls me into the duel her stats now win. I stop trying to sidelane her one-for-one here — she's the scaler and I'm the peeler. But once I reach two-plus items the matchup is genuinely mine again in the only way that matters: full tank with Iceborn and a second armor piece, I become an unkillable R-peel that pulls her off my carry, and while her percent-HP and true damage shred me, they can't one-shot a stacked K'Sante. I win by grouping and using All Out to recall her out of my backline, never by feeding her an isolated sidelane kill.","whys":["Even at level 1 — you have only Ntofo Strikes and no engage, but so does she with just her Q proc, so you both just farm and set up the wave.","She picks up her dash tools before your Q-W combo fully matters, and her E hookshot plus Q true-damage proc out-threatens your bare Q at level 2.","Her full Q-W-E combo out-trades you in melee — one E hookshot stun into her cone and true-damage proc beats your unitemized tank trade.","She owns the lane-control window: a Camille with Q true damage and W cone heal grinds down your stacks faster than your bulk banks a lead.","Her R (Hextech Ultimatum) isolates you into a 1v1, and your All Out strips the very tankiness you need to survive her E-stun burst — this window is hers.","Her Sheen/Trinity spike lands E stun into W cone heal and Q proc, out-trading your single tank item before your W-peel comes back up.","Genuinely yours late: full tank with Iceborn and armor, you become an unkillable R-peel her true damage chips but can never one-shot."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"cassiopeia","win":["Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Cassio is poison-only and slow to ramp early, so this is the one stretch where you can walk up and Q3 her before her sustained DPS spins up."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Once her Twin Fang is online she kites your short Q and grounds your W mid-charge, so every step into her range costs more HP than your Q poke returns."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Petrifying Gaze (120s) only stuns you if you face her — turn away and it is a slow, so landing a wall-stun W is still your kill condition."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Full poison Cassio melts your armor stacks with magic DPS, but a fed All-Out duelist profile with magic pen can still dash on top of her and recall-peel her in fights — your one reclaim window."}],"wants":{"you":["Land W into a wall or minion to stun her long enough to Q3 and close the gap before she kites","Save E to dash past her grounding window, not to engage into it","Buy Mercury's Treads and Grievous Wounds early — Twin Fang heals her off every poison tick you eat"],"foe":["Hold W (Miasma) to ground your W dash and your E so your engage just dies on the cast","Stack poison with Q then spam Twin Fang to out-DPS your sustain while move speed keeps her at range","Land Petrifying Gaze while you face her, so it stuns instead of slowing, then re-poison"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are the only stretch that is mine. Cassio is poison-only and ramps slowly, so I can walk up, eat one Q, and threaten the two-stack pull before her DPS exists. The moment Twin Fang is online at 3, that flips: she shreds me at range and my Q barely reaches. Last-hit at the tip of Q, do not chase a Q she can just kite, and never step over her Miasma — grounded, my W dash and E do not fire and I am stuck in her poison.","mid":"From 4 through 6 she owns the tempo. My W is my whole kill threat and her W (Miasma) grounds it on cast, so I have to bait that cooldown or land W into terrain for the long stun, then Q3-pull and All-Out her before she can re-poison. At 6 her R face-stun catches me the instant I commit the charge, and All-Out strips my tankiness right when her sustained magic DPS is highest. Only go in when her Miasma is down and I have a wall behind her.","late":"Past two items full-poison Cassio out-DPSes my armor stacks — magic damage and percent ticks ignore everything I build, so I cannot just sit in her face. But this is the one window I can reclaim: a fed All-Out converts me into a magic-pen duelist who can dash on top of her, and the R recast lets me yank her out of her team's backline. I do not win the standstill poke war; I win by using E and W to close the gap she relies on and deleting her before she resets.","whys":["Cassio's poison ramps slowly and I have nothing but Q at 1 either, so neither of us threatens a kill — I just farm and set up my level 2-3 walk-up.","She picks up Twin Fang and starts out-DPSing my poke; her passive move speed keeps her at range where my short Q whiffs.","Her full poison plus Miasma grounding is online — she cancels my W charge on cast and kites my Q3, so every trade bleeds me.","Levels 4-5 are her control peak here: she pokes me off the wave with stacked poison while her move speed dodges my only engage tools.","At 6 her R face-stun catches me mid-W and All-Out strips my bulk into her highest DPS window, so committing usually feeds.","Her first AP item spikes her sustained poison damage past my first tank piece, and Miasma still grounds every gap-close I try.","Late, a fed All-Out turns me into a magic-pen duelist who can finally dash onto her and recall-peel her out before she kites — my only reclaim window."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"chogath","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W combo comes online — W (Path Maker) the moment he winds up Rupture, then two stacks to pull him in. This is your first real window to chunk him before Feast stacks."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R (Feast) is the threat to respect — it's flat true damage that ignores your armor stacking, and All Out strips your tankiness, so don't 1v1 him under turret when Feast is up and you're low."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His Feast HP stacks plus a first tank item out-bulk you — your armor does nothing against a true-damage Feast, and Feral Scream silences you out of the trade."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet plus your peel kit flips it: you survive his slow Q-W-Feast combo with Path Maker's unstoppable charge and R him off your carry in fights."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold W (Path Maker) to eat his Rupture knockup, then pull him in at two stacks and trade hard","Own Levels 3-5 before Feast stacks make him impossible to chunk","Reach 2 items so Iceborn Gauntlet bulk and R peel beat his slow point-and-click combo in teamfights"],"foe":["Land Rupture (Q) into Feral Scream (W) silence to lock you for the full knockup-silence combo","Stack Feast every kill and CS so his HP pool and true-damage R outscale your armor","Drag the game late where true-damage Feast and his silence ignore everything you build"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are an even farm — Cho'Gath has no engage and just wants to last-hit and stack, and I only have Q so I'm not threatening a kill either. The thing I'm fishing for is his Rupture (Q): it's a telegraphed delayed knockup, so I hold W (Path Maker) to charge through it unstoppable rather than eating it. Once I hit 3 and my Q-W combo is online I can W his wind-up, Q3 to knock him up, and win the short trade before he has the HP to shrug it off.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are mine. He's a slow, immobile target who has to walk up to farm, and that's exactly the melee profile I beat — I W through his Rupture, Q3 for the knockup, and bank small leads while he has no way to punish my cooldowns. The turn is Level 6: his Feast is flat true damage that ignores all the armor I stack, and if I pop All Out I trade away the bulk that lets me survive his combo. So I keep using R as a tool for trades, not a desperate 1v1, and I never all-in him low when Feast is up.","late":"This is where I have to respect him as a scaler — but it doesn't fully run away from me like Vayne or Fiora does. His Feast true damage and Feral Scream silence beat my armor, so I can't bet on out-tanking him in a straight duel. What I can do is play the teamfight: with Iceborn Gauntlet and two items I have the bulk to charge through his slow Q-W-Feast combo with Path Maker's unstoppable window, then R their carry out of the fight. Don't sit in lane trying to solo a fat Cho'Gath — group, peel, and let my R win the 5v5 instead of his stacks winning the 1v1.","whys":["He has no engage and you only have Q — neither side threatens a kill, so deny his stacks and last-hit even.","You pick up W or E and get safer, but your full combo isn't online yet — set up the wave and hold Path Maker for his Rupture.","Your Q-W combo is online: W through his Rupture knockup, then two Ntofo stacks to pull him in and chunk him before Feast bulks him out.","You own the short trades as a tank, but his Feast stacking is creeping up — bank your lead now because it stops working soon.","His R Feast is flat true damage that ignores your armor and All Out strips your bulk — don't 1v1 him low when Feast is up.","Feast HP plus his first tank item out-bulk you, and Feast's true damage ignores armor stacking — stop dueling and play the wave.","Iceborn bulk lets you survive his slow combo and R peels their carry — win the teamfight instead of his stacks winning the 1v1."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"darius","win":["Darius","Darius","Darius","Darius","Darius","Darius","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Darius owns this — his E pull into empowered Q bleed beats you before your Q-W combo is online, so just farm and eat minimal poke."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online, but a level-3 Darius all-in still out-trades you raw; W his E pull to stay unstoppable rather than dueling him head-on."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out gives you a real 1v1 — W-block his E, R-knock him out of his 5-stack bleed, but it strips your tankiness right as his R execute threatens, so it's a coinflip skill window."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your first tank-engage item plus sustained DPS finally outscales his all-in — you survive Noxian Guillotine and peel him with R recall while he falls off."}],"wants":{"you":["Use W's unstoppable charge to eat his E pull so he can't chain you into empowered Q bleed","Survive his levels 1-9 all-in windows and farm to your first tank item where you out-sustain him","At 6, R-knock him out of his Hemorrhage stacks before they ramp his Q and Guillotine damage"],"foe":["Land E to pull you in and chain empowered Q + Hemorrhage stacks for a level 1-3 all-in","Stack 5 bleeds to maximize his passive AD and the true-damage threshold on Noxian Guillotine R","Win the all-in before your first item, since he loses the lane once you out-scale his early bully window"]},"early":"Darius owns levels 1-3 and you cannot pretend otherwise — at level 1 you only have Q with no engage, and his E pull into an empowered Q outer-blade will out-trade anything you can do back. Do not stand in E range to throw a Q; last-hit at the tip and concede the poke. Your one defensive tool is W: if he commits an E, charging W makes you unstoppable so the pull can't chain you into his full combo. Otherwise just farm — your payoff is later, not here.","mid":"Levels 4-6 even out into a skill matchup. You finally have the Q-W combo and your tank bulk lets you trade around his cooldowns, but a fed Darius still all-ins hard, so pick fights when his E is down. At 6 it's a genuine coinflip: All Out gives you the duelist profile to win the 1v1 and your R can knock him out of his Hemorrhage stacks, but it strips your tankiness exactly when his Noxian Guillotine execute comes online — block his E with W before you ever commit R.","late":"This is where you reclaim the matchup. Darius is an early bully who falls off, and once you hit your first tank-engage item your sustained DPS and bulk out-trade his all-in — you eat the Guillotine and keep swinging while he can't kill you fast enough. In teamfights your R recall peels him off your carries entirely, turning his single-target dive into wasted cooldowns. Close on these windows; don't let a snowballing Darius end before you get there.","whys":["You have only Q and no engage threat, while his E pull into empowered Q outer-blade out-trades anything you can answer at level 1.","He picks up his combo a beat before you do — a level-2 Darius E-Q all-in still beats your half-online kit, so just farm.","Your Q-W combo is online but a level-3 Darius all-in out-trades you raw; use W only to dodge his E pull, not to duel him.","It's a true skill window — your tank bulk lets you trade around his E cooldown, but a fed Darius still wins the committed all-in.","All Out wins you the 1v1 and R knocks him out of his bleed stacks, but it strips your tankiness right as his Guillotine execute threatens — a coinflip.","Your first tank-engage item makes the trades skill-dependent again as your sustain starts to match his falling-off all-in.","You out-scale him here: your bulk and DPS survive Noxian Guillotine while R recall peels him off your team and his early-bully power is gone."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"drmundo","win":["K'Sante","K'Sante","Dr. Mundo","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online — W a committed Mundo and pull him in at two stacks, your first real trade window before his sustain snowballs."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Mundo's cleaver hits off your current health and Heart Zapper heals him back — every chunk you take off him is undone, so don't trade for nothing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet online: you out-disrupt him, slow him with the proc and force side-lane fights he can't kite away from."},{"when":"Late","text":"R All Out turns you into a duelist with bonus damage and healing — the one profile that threatens to kill a Maximum-Dosage Mundo instead of chipping at him."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach your Level 3 Q-W combo and W-stun a committed Mundo into a Q3 knock-up","Stack tank items and use Iceborn slows to lock him in side-lane fights he can't kite","Use R All Out's bonus damage and healing to fight through Maximum Dosage, not chip it"],"foe":["Cleaver (Q) your HP bar from range and heal back every chip with his passive","Dodge your short Q and W by walking out — he wants distance, not a brawl","Reach 2-3 items where his R drain-heal makes him impossible to kill in a sustained fight"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are a farm fest — you only have Q and no engage, and his cleaver (Q) chips you for percent-HP while his passive heals him back, so don't try to out-poke a drain tank. The trade pattern flips at Level 3: once you have the full Q-W combo you can W-charge into a committed Mundo, stun him, and land Q3 for the knock-up. Bait his Q cleaver first — when it's on cooldown his only damage is autos and E, and that's your window to step up. Don't throw a Q into max range and walk into his cleaver for nothing; every HP point you spend that he just heals back is value lost.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your tank lane-control peak — you trade around his Q cooldown and bank small leads with your bulk while his early kit is weak. At 6 his R is a double-edged thing for both of you: his Maximum Dosage is a huge heal that makes all-ins messy, but your R All Out converts you into a penetration duelist who can actually fight through it rather than chip at it. Look for the all-in when his cleaver is down: W-stun, Q3 knock-up, R through him. The longer the fight, the more his passive and R drain back — so commit hard and fast, don't drag it out into his sustain.","late":"Mundo scales forever — his R Maximum Dosage plus percent-HP cleaver means in a slow brawl he simply out-heals your damage, and your armor stacking does nothing against a drain tank you can't burst. The answer is your R All Out: it strips your tankiness but gives you range and penetration, the one profile that puts real damage through his heal instead of tickling it. Catch him in side lane with Iceborn slows so he can't kite, blow R when his Maximum Dosage is on cooldown, and use your knock-up to peel him off your carries in teamfights rather than dueling a fully-itemized Mundo head-on.","whys":["You only have Q and no engage, and his cleaver pokes you for percent-HP — but Mundo's level 1 is weak too, so just farm and deny.","His cleaver is a 4s current-health chip while you still have no combo to punish it — neither of you wins this level.","Mundo's cleaver chunks you off current health and Heart Zapper heals him back before your combo can answer — he edges the level before your trading arrives.","Your full Q-W combo lets you W-stun and Q3 around his cleaver cooldown, but his sustain claws it back — even trades, small leads.","Your R All Out's penetration duelist profile fights through his Maximum Dosage heal as well as his R answers your all-in — it's a coin-flip 6.","Iceborn Gauntlet lets you slow and lock him for side-lane fights he cannot walk out of — with Grievous Wounds up, the grind is yours.","R All Out's damage and healing are the only thing that out-paces a full Mundo — with anti-heal up, you reclaim the late game his sustain would own."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"fiora","win":["Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Fiora's Q dash and Vitals dictate the opener — she pokes your single Q before your W-pull is online, so just farm and don't lever-step into auto range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is your one honest 1v1 button, but it strips your tank stats — only commit it when her parry and Q dash are both down or she riposte-stuns the W and deletes you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Fiora's Hydra/Eclipse spike with percent-HP Vitals shreds your early armor — your Iceborn frostfield slows her dash but does not stop her proccing four Vitals on you."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your peel window: Iceborn slow plus R recall lets you yank her off your carries — you stop owning the 1v1 but win by making her a non-factor in 5v5."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her parry onto a throwaway Q, then land the W stun and the two-stack pull while Riposte's 24s cooldown runs","Stack tank items and fight near your team where R recall peels her off a carry instead of dueling her straight","Take short trades with Q poke and back off before her Vitals and Q dash let her reset spacing on you"],"foe":["Riposte your W stun or your pull — both immobilize, so her parry stuns back, then Vital you down","Space with Q dashes to proc Vitals on your flanks while dodging your short-range Q and W","Scale to 2-3 items where her true-damage Vitals laugh at your armor stacking and out-splitpush you"]},"early":"Level 1 you only have Q and no engage, and Fiora pokes with a Q dash plus a Vital proc before your W-pull exists, so concede the level and last-hit at the tip of Q. Do not lever into auto range chasing a single Q — she just Q-dashes a Vital onto your side and resets. The trap is throwing your big W charge early: if she riposte-stuns it she turns the whole trade, so keep W as a defensive disengage this stage, not an engage.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are normally my lane-control peak, but Fiora's parry breaks the pattern — every W charge and two-stack pull is bait for her riposte stun, and a parried W is a death sentence. Trade in short bursts: poke Q, threaten the pull to make her hold parry, then back off before her Vitals stack. At 6 my All Out gives a real 1v1, but it sheds my tankiness exactly when she ignores armor with percent-HP true damage, so only flip it when her W and Q dash are both down.","late":"This is the one window the matchup turns my way, and only in 5v5 — never the side-lane 1v1. Her Vitals do percent-max-HP true damage that my armor stacking does nothing about, so I lose the straight duel forever. Instead I build full tank, use Iceborn's frostfield to slow her dash, and save R to recall and yank her off my carry mid-commit. Win by making her splitpush irrelevant; do not get caught alone or she carves through me.","whys":["I have only Q and no engage threat, while Fiora Q-dashes in, procs a Vital and pokes me before my W-pull combo exists.","She picks up her Q dash for free spacing and Vital uptime; my W or E only makes me safer, it does not let me catch her.","My Q-W combo comes online but she riposte-stuns the W charge or Q3 and flips the trade with percent-HP Vitals.","My usual tank lane-control peak is neutered because every W-pull and Q3 is bait for her parry stun.","All Out gives a real 1v1 but strips my tankiness right when her true-damage Vitals ignore armor — she edges the duel.","Her Hydra/Eclipse spike and stacked Vitals shred my early armor faster than my first tank item can hold.","My armor finally matters in teamfights: I go full tank and R-recall her off a carry, so I win 5v5 even though I lose the 1v1."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"galio","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Galio","K'Sante","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"With Ntofo Strikes and Path Maker both online, you charge W into a wall-stun and Q3 knock-up him before his Q wind-shred and W taunt can punish a melee like you in return."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Galio's biggest window: his global Hero's Entrance and his W damage-reduction taunt mean if you blow All Out he can flip the duel and bring help, so don't gamble your tank stats into a stacked-MR target you can't shred."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet online — your slow-and-stick durability lets you W-charge into Q3 and hold him in your range, where his immobile body can't kite your knock-up combo."},{"when":"Late","text":"Galio is an AP tank stacking magic resist, but your armor/HP and R's terrain-shred peel still win the bruiser side-skirmish; his real threat is roaming off ult, not 1v1ing you."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach level 3 and W-charge into a wall to stun him, then Q3 knock-up and pull while his Q-W cooldowns are down","Bait his W taunt before you commit Path Maker so its damage reduction and lock don't blank your engage","Use Iceborn slow plus E Footwork to stick to his immobile frame where he can't dodge your short Q and W"],"foe":["Poke you with Q wind-shred and passive magic autos so your low-econ early stays poor","Land his W taunt to soak your combo behind damage reduction, then walk off with no follow-up cost","Use his global R Hero's Entrance to roam and snowball other lanes rather than lose the 1v1 to you"]},"early":"Galio is an immobile AP tank with no dash, which is exactly the kind of melee I out-position once my combo comes online. Level 1 I just farm with Ntofo Strikes and eat a little Q wind-shred and passive-auto poke. By level 2 I pick up Path Maker or Footwork and stop conceding; by level 3 I have the full Q-W combo and own the trade — if he steps up to last-hit, I W-charge into the wall to stun him, then Q3 to knock up and pull. The one thing to respect is his W taunt: if I dump Path Maker while it's available he soaks it behind damage reduction, so bait it first.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are my lane-control peak. He can't kite a knock-up he has no dash to dodge, so I trade around his Q and W cooldowns, W-charge into terrain for the long stun, and bank small leads with my bulk. Level 6 is the one window I give him: All Out strips my tank stats, and against a champ stacking magic resist with a damage-reduction taunt and a global R, gambling my durability is a bad bet — he can survive the flip and Hero's Entrance a teammate in. So I keep R for peel, not for a greedy duel here, and bait his taunt before any hard commit.","late":"This stays an even, grindy lane that I edge on the side. Galio's magic-resist stacking does nothing against my armor and HP, and his immobile body can't escape my Iceborn slow into Q3 knock-up, so the bruiser skirmish is mine. His real threat isn't 1v1ing me — it's the global Hero's Entrance roam, so I track his ult and ping it the second he disappears. In teamfights I don't try to out-damage an AP tank; I W-charge through his line and use All Out to peel his engage off my carries, which is where my kit actually wins.","whys":["You concede nothing real here — both of you are weak at level 1, you just farm with Ntofo Strikes and take minor Q and passive-auto poke from an immobile laner you'll out-trade soon.","At level 2 you add Path Maker or Footwork and become safe, and his Q wind-shred poke can't punish a tank who simply farms toward his level-3 spike.","Your full Q-W combo is online — W-charge into the wall to stun him and Q3 to knock up and pull, and his dash-less frame can't dodge or answer it.","This is your tank lane-control peak: you trade around his Q and W cooldowns and bank leads with your bulk while his immobile body eats every W-charge stun.","Galio owns level 6 — All Out strips your tankiness, and against his MR stacking, W taunt damage reduction, and global R, flipping the duel and bringing help beats your stripped-down profile.","Iceborn Gauntlet lets you slow and stick to his immobile body, holding him in Q3 knock-up range where his taunt-and-poke kit can't out-trade your durable first-item spike.","His magic resist does nothing to your armor and HP, so you win the side-skirmish and peel him in fights; his only edge is roaming off Hero's Entrance, not the 1v1."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"gangplank","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Gangplank","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online — W a committed GP and Q3 him for the knock-up, your one window before barrels stack."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out turns you into a duelist who can dash through GP and shred — but it strips your tank stats right when his barrel-crit burst spikes, so only ult if you survive the chain."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet makes you sticky and disruptive — slow him and force a side-lane fight before his barrels and trinity come online."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Full barrel chains, crit and global R make him the threat — your armor stacking does nothing against his crit DPS and he kites your short Q/W."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach your Level 3 Q-W combo and W-Q3 him whenever he steps up to last-hit or place a barrel","Use E to dodge his barrel-detonation chains and close the gap his poke wants to keep open","Force side-lane all-ins on your Iceborn spike before his crit and global R make the map his"],"foe":["Place barrels at max range and chain-detonate them to poke you out before your Q-W lands","Use W (Remove Scurvy) to cleanse your Q slow and Q3 pull, then kite back with the heal","Stall lane and scale into barrel crit + Trinity while threatening cross-map with his R"]},"early":"At Level 1 he just barrel-pokes and you just farm — you have only Q and no engage, so don't walk into a barrel for a single cleave. Once you hit Level 3 your Q-W combo is online and this becomes your window: when he steps up to detonate a barrel or last-hit, charge W to eat the hit unstoppable, knock him into terrain, and Q3 for the pull. Bait his W (Remove Scurvy) — if he burns it to cleanse your slow, your next Q3 lands clean.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your tank lane-control peak: trade around his barrel cooldown, eat poke you out-sustain, and bank small leads with your bulk. At 6, All Out is a coin-flip — it lets you dash through him and duel, but it strips the tankiness that survives his barrel-crit burst, so only commit R if his combo is on cooldown. Don't blow W on a barrel he can pre-detonate to knock you off; save it for when he's committed.","late":"This is where you lose the lever. Once GP stacks barrel crit and Trinity, his DPS is crit and percent-pressure that your armor stacking does nothing against, and he kites your short Q and W from barrel range. His global R also means he affects the map while you're stuck side-laning. You have to close this game on your earlier-to-mid windows — peel for your carries in teamfights with R All Out, but never bet on out-scaling a fed Gangplank 1v1.","whys":["You have only Q with no engage and he just barrel-pokes — neither of you wins level 1, so deny his last-hits and set up your level-3 window.","You pick up W or E and get your first trade tool — W a committed GP to eat the barrel and you're suddenly safer than his poke wants you to be.","Your full Q-W combo is online — you can W-knock and Q3-pull him, but his W (Remove Scurvy) cleanses the slow and his heal sustains, so it's a genuine skill trade.","You own the melee range but he banks barrel poke around your cooldowns — leads stay small and it comes down to who lands their windows.","All Out can win the 1v1 but strips your tankiness right as his barrel-crit burst spikes — whether you survive the chain decides it, so it's a skill check.","His barrel-crit damage and Trinity spike outpace your first item, and he kites your short Q/W from range — this window is his.","In a teamfight you reclaim value: R All Out pulls his carry off your team and your bulk peels, so the late game swings back to your disruption."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"gnar","win":["Gnar","Gnar","Gnar","Gnar","Skill","Gnar","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Gnar's boomerang (Q) and hop (E) outrange your Q cleave and dodge your W charge, so he chips you for free while you only get Q tip last-hits."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out turns you into a duelist who can survive mega-Gnar's burst and R his jump-stun, but if he's in mini form he just kites your shortened lockdown."},{"when":"Mega transform","text":"Watch his rage bar — Mega Gnar's Wallop (W) is the AOE stun in front of him, on 7s; GNAR! (R) is the separate wall-stun throw."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet plus your second tank item makes you an unkiteable peel threat — once you can W-engage past his hops, sidelane pressure flips your way."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait the mega GNAR! stun onto a minion, then W-charge in unstoppable and Q3 knock-up before he hops away","Use your passive move-speed-to-champions to close the kite gap and land a W stun against the wall","Survive to first item where Iceborn slow plus your bulk finally pin a kiting mini-Gnar"],"foe":["Stay in mini form and kite with boomerang (Q) plus hop (E) so your short Q and W never connect","Catch your W commit with Mega Gnar's Wallop stun and punish the 14s cooldown","Poke you out of every trade with boomerang and scale his transform burst past your armor stacking"]},"early":"Gnar owns these levels and I just farm. His boomerang (Q) outranges my Ntofo Strikes cleave and his hop (E) skips backward over my W charge, so every time I step up to last-hit he chips me and dances out. I have only Q at level 1 with no engage, so I tip-last-hit with Q range and refuse to chase a poke I can't catch. Don't burn W on a mini-Gnar who'll just hop it — I'd be unstoppable into empty air and then stunned.","mid":"Still his window. At 4-5 my Q-W combo is online but it's short-range into a champ built to kite it, so I trade only when his boomerang is on cooldown and he's stuck in mini form. The real danger is his rage bar: a fresh mega-Gnar lands the GNAR! AOE stun the instant I commit W, and that long W cooldown leaves me naked. At 6 it's genuinely even — All Out gives me the bulk to eat his transform burst and the dash to R his jump, but if he's mini he just kites my shortened lockdown, so I only swing for it when he's mega and out of position.","late":"This is finally mine. Once I have Iceborn Gauntlet and a second tank item the slow plus my passive move speed toward champions closes the kite gap his hops relied on — he can't boomerang-and-run forever. My armor stacking does nothing to his transform burst in a straight fight, but I don't need the straight fight: I W-engage past his hops, R him out of his backline, and peel. Force sidelane 1v1s and teamfight peels where his kite space is gone, not poke wars where his boomerang owns the range.","whys":["He has only mini form but his boomerang (Q) already outranges my Q cleave and I have no engage at level 1 — I concede and farm at Q tip.","His hop (E) skips over my W charge before I have my full combo, so he pokes with boomerang and I can't pin him.","My Q-W combo is online but short-range into a built-to-kite champ — his boomerang and hop beat my reach every trade.","He banks the lane-control peak by kiting in mini form and catching any W commit with Mega Gnar's Wallop stun.","Genuinely even: All Out lets me survive his transform burst and R his jump, but a mini-form Gnar still kites my shortened lockdown.","His first-item poke and a fresh mega GNAR! stun still punish my W cooldown before my Iceborn slow comes online.","Iceborn Gauntlet plus my passive move speed close his kite space — I W-engage past his hops and R him out to peel."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"gragas","win":["Skill","Gragas","Skill","Gragas","Skill","Skill","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Gragas hits 2 first off his pool-leashed clear and can E body-slam in for a Q-pool combo before your Q-W is fully online."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W combo comes online — W a committed Gragas mid-E and Q3's pull to even the trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out lets you dash through Gragas and recall-peel, but it strips your armor so his Q+E+R burst hits harder — only ult when you survive the combo."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"With Iceborn plus a second tank item your Q slows chain through his E dashes and you peel him off your carries — your one clean takeover window."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q3's shockwave pull when Gragas commits his E body-slam so he can't reposition out","Bank Footwork (E) shield and dash to avoid eating Q pool plus E displacement back-to-back","Reach 2+ items where your Q slow and R peel outvalue his single AP brawl burst"],"foe":["Body-slam E into a Q pool to displace you and proc max AP-scaling damage on his combo","Use W damage reduction to tank your Q3 trade then disengage with E before you can W-stun","Land R Explosive Cask to knock you off CS or into his jungler's gank path"]},"early":"Gragas owns the level-1-2 tempo here — his pool (Q) sustains the poke he throws and his E body-slam lets him pick the trade, so don't sit in E-range with your Q on cooldown. At level 1 you only have Q and no engage, so just farm the cleave tip and concede the level. The moment you hit 3 and your Q-W combo is live you get your first real window: if he E's in, W-charge to knock him back and Q3 to pull him, turning his short dash into a losing trade.","mid":"Levels 4-5 he still edges you because his Q-pool-into-E combo refreshes faster than your bulk can punish, and his W damage reduction eats your Q3 if he saves it for your engage. Bait that W down, then commit: W-charge through his E displacement so he can't knock you off, and Q3 to lock him. At 6 your All Out is a coin-flip — it gives you a duelist dash-through but converts away the armor that was tanking his AP, so only ult when you've already survived his Q+E+R burst, not as the opener.","late":"This is where the lane swings your way. With Iceborn Gauntlet and a second tank piece your Q slow chains through his E dashes and your R recall lets you yank him off your carries — his single-target AP brawl can't out-damage your peel in a 5v5. Don't let his R Explosive Cask catch you out of position near objectives, but in an extended fight your durability plus All Out's lockdown beats one AP bruiser. Close around your item spikes; this is your strongest window, not his.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1 — you have only Q and no engage, he hasn't drawn his E body-slam yet, so it's a neutral farm lane.","Gragas spikes to 2 off his pool-sustained clear and can E in for a Q-pool combo before your Q-W is online.","Your Q-W combo comes live — W his committed E and Q3's shockwave pull flips the trade, evening the level.","His Q-pool-into-E refreshes faster than your bulk punishes and W damage reduction soaks your Q3, so he edges 4-5.","All Out is a wash — it wins the dash-through duel but strips the armor that tanks his AP burst, so neither owns 6 cleanly.","Your Iceborn first item makes your Q slow stick and your durability climbs, but his AP spike keeps it even-handed.","With 2+ tank items your Q slow chains through his E and your R recall peels him off carries — your single-AP-brawl opponent can't out-trade your bulk."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"garen","win":["Garen","Garen","Garen","Garen","Skill","Skill","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Garen Q silences your Q3 cast mid-combo and his empowered strike chunks you while you only have one stack built — concede the level and farm at max Q range."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo is online, but he just W's the burst, walks out of your Q3 pull, and Q-silences your follow-up — your first 'trading window' barely exists here."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out turns you into a duelist who can out-DPS his spin, but his R is a missing-HP true-damage execute that ignores the armor you just gave up — bait W before you commit."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your peel and Iceborn/tank profile finally outscale his lane kit — by here you survive his combo and R him off your carry, the one window the lane swings your way."}],"wants":{"you":["Farm safely at max Q range and reach 2+ items where your tank peel beats his short-trade kit","Bait Garen's W (the damage-cut + tenacity) before you W-charge so your knock-up lands on a vulnerable target","Use your W's CC-immunity to eat his Q empowered-strike trade and walk away even, not behind"],"foe":["Q-silence the moment you wind up your Q3 or W to cancel the cast and land a free empowered hit","W up your W-charge and ult burst so the damage gets cut, then disengage with his passive regen","Snowball the silenced early levels and use R's true-damage execute to finish you before items"]},"early":"Garen owns these levels and it is mostly his Q. The silence cancels your Q3 cast and your W-charge if he reads it, and the empowered strike out-trades you while you only have one passive stack built. Do not step into auto range to throw a Q he can just silence — last-hit at the tip of Q and accept the chip. You have no level-1 engage anyway, so concede it and farm; the good news is his early poke can't burst a tank, he just denies you the trades you want.","mid":"Level 3 is supposed to be your first window, but it barely exists here — you W a committed Garen and he just walks out of the Q3 pull, W's to cut your damage and gain tenacity, then Q-silences your follow-up. At 6, All Out gives you a real 1v1: you convert to duelist stats and out-DPS his spin. But that strips your bulk exactly when his R becomes a missing-HP true-damage execute that doesn't care about armor. Only all-in when his W is down, and bait it first.","late":"This is your window. Once you hit 2+ items you stop being a punching bag and become a tank again — you survive his full combo, peel him off your carry, and your R yanks him out of position into your team. His lane kit doesn't scale into teamfights the way yours does; he becomes a side-lane splitpush threat, not a duelist who beats you. Match him in the side lane with your W-engage and Iceborn slow, and let your R do the work in 5v5s.","whys":["His Q silence cancels your Q3 and W cast at level 1, and his empowered strike out-trades your single passive stack — just farm at Q range.","He picks up his spin and out-trades you in extended range while you still lack a W engage — keep last-hitting and don't commit.","Your full Q-W combo is online but he W's the burst, walks out of the Q3 pull, and Q-silences your follow-up, so your 'trading window' is dead on arrival.","These are normally your lane-control levels as a tank, but Garen's W tenacity and damage cut plus his Q silence keep him ahead in every short trade.","All Out lets you out-DPS his spin, but it strips your tankiness right as his R becomes a missing-HP true-damage execute that ignores your armor — call it Skill and bait his W.","Your first tank item closes the gap — you survive his combo now, but his level kit still trades even, so the lane is genuinely a coin-flip here.","At 2+ items your tank profile and R peel finally outscale his short-trade kit — you eat his combo and pull him off your carry while he can only splitpush."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"graves","win":["Graves","Graves","Graves","K'Sante","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"With only Q you have no engage, but Graves has no E-dash escape yet either — match his pushes and farm at Ntofo Strikes range."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q-W-E combo comes fully online at 3: W-charge through his autos, knock him into terrain, and Q3 pull him for your first real all-in window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is a coinflip here — it gives you a duelist 1v1 but strips your tankiness, so his shotgun burst can shred the squishier you if the smoke cuts your sight first."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet's slow field plus your W stun makes him uniquely unkiteable for an immobile-after-E ADC — this is the window to collapse on him in the side lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Land W against terrain to cancel his kite and stun him long enough for Q3","Bait his E-dash early, then Iceborn-slow him so his shotgun reset never lands clean","Force side-lane all-ins at first item where his blind can't save him from your stun chain"],"foe":["Kite you with Smoke Screen — it cuts your sight and slows you — and walk back on your cooldowns","E-dash over your Q3 and out of your W path, then burst you with shotgun double-tap","Build tanky and out-trade your weak early before your stun threat comes online"]},"early":"Level 1 you both have nothing scary — you only have Q and no engage, but Graves has no E-dash to escape yet, so match his wave and last-hit at the tip of Ntofo Strikes. The trap is levels 2-3 once his shotgun and smoke (W) come online: it cuts your sight and slows you on impact while your short Q and W are on cooldown. Don't walk into auto range to throw a Q he can just dance around — farm, eat a little poke, and respect that his early all-in burst beats your skeleton kit.","mid":"From level 3 your Q-W-E combo is whole and the lane flips on a good W. Charge Path Maker through his autos to become unstoppable, slam him into a wall for the long stun, then E in and Q3 to pull him — that locks an immobile ADC who's spent his E-dash. The danger is 6: All Out gives you a real 1v1, but it trades your armor for a duelist profile, so if you ult into a full-charge shotgun and a smoke cloud you melt the squishier version of yourself. Only pop R when his E and W are down.","late":"Your first item is the peak — Iceborn Gauntlet's slow field plus your W stun makes Graves uniquely unkiteable, which is rare for a kiting ADC, so force every side-lane fight here while you out-stat him. Past two items it stays close: he builds tanky-for-an-ADC and his shotgun reset still bursts you if you let him space, but you keep the engage and the lockdown he can't answer once his E-dash is gone. Close on your first-item window and your stun threat rather than betting on a poke war you can't win.","whys":["You have only Q and zero engage, but Graves has no E-dash to escape yet either — neither of you can commit, so farm at Ntofo Strikes range.","His shotgun and Smoke Screen come online — it cuts your sight and slows on impact — while your short Q and W sit on cooldown and he out-trades you.","At 3 he still out-pokes you in the open, dancing his autos around your short Q and E-dashing out of your W path before your combo is whole enough to punish.","Your full Q-W-E combo lets you W-charge into terrain for a long stun, then E-Q3 pull a Graves who's burned his E — your lane-control peak as a tank.","All Out hands you a duelist 1v1 but strips your armor, so against his shotgun double-tap and smoke blind it's a genuine coinflip on your execution.","Iceborn Gauntlet's slow plus your W stun makes him uniquely unkiteable for an E-reliant ADC — collapse on him in the side lane here.","You keep the engage and the peel his kit can't escape once his E is down, and your W lockdown still answers a tankier Graves while he can't burst through your stun chain."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"gwen","win":["Skill","Skill","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","Gwen","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"My full Q-W combo comes online — if she steps up to last-hit I can W-stun her against the wall and Q3 knock-up, the one clean melee window before her mist makes her slippery."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Gwen's takeover: her R Needlework pokes me from outside my Q range and W Hallowed Mist hides her from my W charge and Q3, so my All Out duel loses tempo against her slows and true damage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Her Riftmaker / Nashor's spike: Q true damage plus E attack-speed steroid out-DPS my armor stacking, and W mist resets every fight she takes near it."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"My peel window: in a 5v5 I W through her mist, R-All-Out her off my carry and re-cast to drag her out — her duel scaling doesn't save her when I deny the mist real estate."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach my level 3 Q-W and stun her against terrain before she has W Hallowed Mist to hide from the combo","Bank a small CS or HP lead in the level 3-5 window so her Q true damage and mist scaling never get even","In teamfights W through her mist and R-All-Out peel her off my carry, then re-cast to pull her out of the fight"],"foe":["Drop W Hallowed Mist on herself so my W charge and Q3 knock-up whiff and she takes no trade","Poke me out with Q true damage and R Needlework slows from outside my short Q-W range","Scale to Riftmaker/Nashor's where her on-hit true damage ignores my armor stacking entirely"]},"early":"Gwen has a weak level 1 and so do I — I only have Q with no engage threat, so I just farm with the cleave tip and don't walk into a trade I can't finish. The lane opens up at level 3 when my full Q-W is online: if she oversteps to last-hit I can charge W, smash her into the wall for the stun, and Q3 to knock her up and pull her in. That's my one window before her W Hallowed Mist exists, so I punish any greedy CS step. Never burn W when she can just sidestep onto the mist later — early she has no mist, so this is the honest trade window.","mid":"Levels 4-5 I keep banking small leads with my bulk, trading around her cooldowns, but at 6 the lane tilts to her. Her R Needlework slows and pokes me from outside my short Q-W range, and the moment I commit a W charge she drops Hallowed Mist on herself — my dash whiffs, my Q3 finds nothing, and she chips my low-econ HP bar with Q true damage. All Out gives me a 1v1 against most bruisers, but against Gwen it strips my tankiness right when her mist and slows deny the duel, so I don't blindly ult a healthy Gwen sitting in her mist. Bait the mist or fight her when she's stepped off it.","late":"This is where she's supposed to take over — her Q true damage and Nashor's/Riftmaker on-hit ignore my armor stacking, and the W mist resets every skirmish she takes near it, so a straight sidelane duel into a fed Gwen is a losing bet. My value flips in the 5v5: I don't try to out-scale her, I peel. I W through her mist to reach her, R-All-Out to knock her off my carry, and re-cast All Out to drag her out of the fight entirely where her duel scaling means nothing. Close the lane on my level-3-to-5 windows, then stop dueling her and make every fight a teamfight my R controls.","whys":["Gwen is a weak level 1 and so am I — with only Q and no engage I just farm the cleave tip and deny her free Q last-hits, neither of us can commit.","Still even at level 2 — I pick up W or E for safety but she has her dash and Q true damage to match my poke, so the trade is a wash.","Her level 3 and on lets her sidestep my short W charge, and once Hallowed Mist arrives my Q3 knock-up finds nothing while her Q true damage chips me.","She controls the 4-5 window with mist uptime and Q true damage that ignores my armor — I'm conceding the wave and farming, not trading.","At 6 her R Needlework slows and pokes me from outside my Q-W range, and All Out strips my tankiness exactly when her mist denies the duel.","Her Riftmaker/Nashor's spike turns Q into reliable on-hit true damage that out-DPS my armor stacking, and mist resets every fight she takes.","I reclaim it in teamfights — I W through her mist and R-All-Out peel her off my carry, then re-cast to drag her out where her duel scaling means nothing."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"heimerdinger","win":["Skill","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Skill","Heimerdinger","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Heimer drops his first turret on the wave and W-pokes you off the minions before your Q-W combo is even online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is your one clean window — R launches him back through a wall and away from his nest, and the duelist stats let you survive an E-grenade burst you could not before."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His turret count and Q stun-grenade make his zone hardest here — your Iceborn Gauntlet helps you walk through, but you still eat rocket poke crossing the no-man's-land of turrets."},{"when":"Late","text":"2+ items: with R range and move-speed stacks from your passive you finally close the gap and peel/blow him up before his turret nest matters in a teamfight."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive lane to 6, then R him back through a wall to strand him away from his turrets for the all-in","Build move speed off Passive marks so you can cross his W-rocket lane and reach him in one E-Q gap-close","Reach 2+ items where your R range lets you blow him up in fights before his turret nest sets up"],"foe":["Plant a turret on the wave so you cannot last-hit or step up without eating turret + W rockets","Land E stun-grenade to lock your W-charge or cancel your Q3 pull, then kite back behind turrets","Stack turrets on a choke and W-poke you out so you concede the wave and never reach all-in range"]},"early":"Heimer owns the first levels because his turret zones the wave before my Q-W combo exists — I only have Q at level 1 and no engage, so I just farm at max Q range and eat poke. His W rockets and turret chip me every time I step to a minion, and walking into his turret field to throw a Q just feeds free damage. Do not blow E trying to gap-close early; his E stun-grenade will catch me mid-dash or cancel my Q3 pull. Last-hit, hold position, and save my health bar for level 6.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are still his because a tank K'Sante cannot out-range turrets — he resets his turret on the wave and W-pokes me whenever I commit. My one real window is All Out at 6: ult converts me to the duelist profile so I survive his E-grenade + turret burst that would chunk a tank, and R launches him back through a wall, away from the nest. Bait the E-grenade first — it is a flat 11s — then E-Q in and ult through him. Respect that his stun-grenade is the whole matchup; eat it and the all-in dies.","late":"Late is finally mine. With 2+ items my Passive stacks move speed toward him so I can cross the rocket lane, and R's bonus range plus the recall recast lets me dive past the turret nest and either delete him or peel him out of a fight. He has no escape once I'm on him — his turrets do nothing if I've already closed. The plan all game is to weather his zone, scrap even at 6, and cash in the teamfight phase where my engage range beats his stationary setup.","whys":["Heimer is weak at level 1 with just a turret, but I have only Q and no engage either — neither of us can punish, so it is a wash while we both farm.","He plants his first turret on the wave and W-pokes me off the minions before my W-E or Q3 combo comes online — I cannot answer the chip yet.","With his turret reset plus E stun-grenade he zones me out of last-hits, and my full Q-W combo still cannot reach him through the turret field.","Levels 4-5 he banks poke leads behind his turret nest while my tank stats give me no way to cross the rocket lane and start a trade.","All Out is my one even window — the duelist conversion lets me survive his E-grenade burst and R launches him back through a wall, so a baited E means I win the 1v1.","His first-item turret count and stun-grenade make his zone hardest here; even with Iceborn Gauntlet I eat rocket poke crossing the no-man's-land between his turrets.","At 2+ items my Passive move-speed stacks and R's bonus range let me finally close the gap and blow him up before his stationary turret nest matters in the fight."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"illaoi","win":["Skill","Illaoi","Illaoi","Illaoi","Illaoi","Illaoi","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Neither of you wants this — but punish her with Q pokes before her tentacles spawn, because once they're up she heals everything back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her R drops a wall of tentacles — Path Maker's charge cuts the damage you take (it does not make you CC-immune), so W out of the field and Q3 her bare."},{"when":"Her ult field","text":"Inside R + E-spirit she does monstrous AOE — never trade standing on her tentacles or your own shadow becomes a third attacker."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"With Iceborn and your peel online you out-position an immobile Illaoi — drag her off her field with R and she's a sitting duck."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her E so it misses, then W-charge — the damage cut, not immunity — and Q3 her while she's away from the field","Fight on the OUTSIDE edge of her tentacles, never in the middle, and use R to drag her off her spawned tentacles","Survive her level-6 R window with W's damage-resist, then close the lane on your 4-5 tank peak before her sustain snowballs"],"foe":["Land E to rip your spirit so you fight your own tentacle-shadow plus her AOE","Spawn a forest of tentacles with Q passive and W, then force you to trade inside the field where they all slam you","Drop R for a wall of tentacles in a teamfight and out-sustain everything with vessel healing"]},"early":"Neither of us is a real level-1 threat — I only have Q and she's just placing tentacles, so I farm and chip her with the tip of my Q cleave before her tentacle field grows. The trap is her E: the spirit echoes a share of the damage it takes back onto me, so dodge it or never stand near her tentacles when I trade. By level 3 my Q-W combo is online and I can W-shove her off a tentacle and Q3 to pull her in, but I do not commit inside the field — every tentacle there slams me.","mid":"This is the dangerous stretch — at 4-5 I'm at my tank lane-control peak and can bank small leads trading around her cooldowns, but the second she hits 6 her R carpets the ground in tentacles and her sustain becomes monstrous if I stand in it. My answer is W: I charge it unstoppable so her tentacle slams can't CC-lock me and the damage-resist eats the burst, then I W-knock her out of her own field and Q3 her bare. Bait her E first — if it's down, she has no spirit-rip and the field is just chip damage I can tank and walk out of.","late":"Late is where I finally flip it. Illaoi is huge inside her tentacle field but immobile and useless dragged out of it, and that's exactly what my R does — I dash through her, knock her back off her tentacles, and re-cast to peel her out of the fight entirely. With Iceborn and a second tank item I out-position her every time; she can't chase, can't reposition, and her whole identity dies the moment she's off her field. Don't ever facecheck her tentacle nest, but in an open fight my mobility and lockdown beat her stationary AOE.","whys":["Neither of you threatens level 1 — you have only Q, she's placing tentacles. Chip with Q's tip before her field grows and last-hit safely.","She gets her tentacle field rolling faster than you stabilize — at 2 her E spirit-rip and a tentacle or two punish any greedy step, so respect the field.","Your Q-W combo is online but the field favors her — if you trade inside her tentacles they all slam you, and her E makes you fight your own shadow.","Her tentacles and sustain own these levels — she heals every trade back inside the field, so you concede tempo and farm the edge rather than commit.","Her R carpets the ground in tentacles and her vessel sustain spikes — even with W to survive the slam-CC, the AOE and healing tilt the window her way.","Her first-item Illaoi out-sustains your trades inside the field and her tentacles out-damage your tank profile — you can't win a stand-up fight on her ground yet.","Now you flip it — R drags an immobile Illaoi off her field where she's helpless, and your Iceborn peel and positioning beat her stationary AOE."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"irelia","win":["Skill","Skill","Irelia","Skill","Irelia","Skill","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q3 pull into W stun is your only hard CC chain — the cleanest window to punish an Irelia who Q-dashes onto you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her ult plus a stacked E stun is her all-in: Ionian Fervor stacks attack speed, and Defiant Dance cuts the physical damage she takes."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet makes you sticky and disruptive — chain the slow into Q3 so she can't Q-reset off a minion to safety."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your peel takes over — R All Out yanks her off your carry and your bulk outlasts her sustained DPS in extended fights."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q3's shockwave pull after she commits a Q-dash so she can't reset out","Time W to eat her E stun or her Q burst, not waste it on the charge while she dodges","Drag the game to teamfights where R All Out peels her off your carry"],"foe":["Use Q to dash through minions and reset, dodging your short Q and W entirely","Land E stun while your W is on cooldown, then full-combo at max Fervor stacks","Snowball an early kill and scale her duelist sustain past your tank stats"]},"early":"Level 1 you only have Q and no engage, so just farm — she has no reset target to abuse you with yet either. The danger starts at 2-3: her Q dashes through minions to reach you and her E stun sets up her trade, and every Mark it lands refreshes that dash. Your one real punish is Q3's shockwave pull — if she Q-dashes onto you and her reset is on a minion that's dying, W to brace the E stun and Q3 her before she can Q-reset out. Don't throw a naked Q she'll just dash around.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are genuinely even — trade around her 16s E and bank small leads with your bulk, because her sustained DPS can't break you while your W is up. At 6 it flips: All Out strips your tankiness, and her ult plus a stacked E stun out-damages your duelist form while Ionian Fervor stacks her attack speed. Don't spend W into a charging Defiant Dance — it cuts the physical damage she takes, so the trade lands short. Hold it for her E stun, and only ult once that E is baited down.","late":"This is where you reclaim it. Stop dueling her in the side lane — she wins the sustained 1v1 if she's fed — and group. With two items your bulk outlasts her and R All Out is the whole point: dash through her, knock her off your carry, and re-cast to drag her back into your team when she Q-dashes onto a backline. Iceborn's slow plus Q3 stops her resetting away. You're the better teamfighter; make every fight 5v5, not a sidelane race she can snowball.","whys":["You have only Q and no engage, but so does she have no reset to punish you with — both just farm the first level.","Her Q can dash through minions to reach you but her E stun isn't reliably online yet — it's an even poke-and-position level.","She owns it: her Q-reset off minions lets her trade and slip your short Q and W, and her E stun beats your incomplete combo.","Your full Q-W combo and tank bulk let you trade around her cooldowns and bank small leads — genuinely even and skill-dependent.","She owns it: her ult plus E stun out-duels your All Out, which strips your tankiness while Ionian Fervor stacks her attack speed.","Iceborn Gauntlet makes you sticky and disruptive — the slow into Q3 stops her Q-reset, evening the all-in back out.","You own it: R All Out peels her off your carry and your tank bulk outlasts her sustained DPS in 5v5 teamfights."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"jax","win":["K'Sante","Skill","Jax","Skill","Jax","Skill","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W combo is fully online — W a committed Jax and Q3 to pull before his E stun comes back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Jax's R turns his bruiser stats into a duelist spike — his cleanest 1v1 window before your items, so respect the all-in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet makes you durable and sticky — your Q slow plus the proc keeps Jax from kiting between his E windows."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"As a control tank you peel Jax off your carries with R All Out — recall-dash drags him out of the fight your team can't 1v1."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q3's pull and the W stun the moment Jax commits, before Counter Strike is back","Hold W until his E window ends — it cuts damage, it does not stop the stun at the end","Stall the lane even and let your R All Out peel-and-scaling decide teamfights"],"foe":["Pop E Counter Strike during your Q autos and W charge to dodge them and stun you back","Stack his Q-W-E burst at 6 with R's defensive stats to win a clean 1v1","Drag the game to 2-3 items where his on-hit duelist profile out-DPSes a single tank"]},"early":"You own Level 1 outright — Jax has only Leap Strike and nothing to punish you with. The whole early game is his E Counter Strike, and the key is that it dodges basic ATTACKS, not abilities: it is 17s at rank 1, so throw Q and W into it freely and hold your autos until it expires. Release W after the dodge window ends so your knockback-stun lands clean. At Level 3 with full Q-W you can W a committed Jax and Q3 to pull him, since he can't dodge a stun he's already mid-leap on.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your tank lane-control peak — you trade around his Q-W gap-close cooldowns and bank small leads with your bulk, but it's genuinely even because his E keeps blanking your best autos. Six is his window, not yours: his R hands him huge defensive stats and turns his on-hit duelist profile lethal, so don't greedily flip a 1v1 into a freshly-ulted Jax. Your own R strips your tankiness, so only pop All Out into him if you've already eaten his E and his burst is on cooldown. Otherwise hold the lead and let Iceborn make you sticky.","late":"This is where you reclaim it. Jax wants the side-lane 1v1, but a control-tank K'Sante with two items doesn't lose the lane and, more importantly, doesn't have to — your job is R All Out in teamfights, dashing through Jax and recall-dragging him off your carries before his on-hit DPS deletes them. He can still out-duel you in an isolated splitpush, so don't island-fight a fed Jax under his tower; group, peel, and let his single-target threat get neutralized in the 5v5 where your W stun and R peel win.","whys":["At Level 1 Jax only has Q and no E yet — you concede nothing he can punish, farm with Q range and set up your level-3 spike.","He picks up E Counter Strike and you get W or E — genuinely even, his dodge-stun answers your poke so trade around his E cooldown, not into it.","Jax edges Levels 3 as his Q-W gap-close plus E stun out-trades a K'Sante who hasn't itemized — bait the E before you commit your combo.","Lane-control is even: your bulk banks leads but his E keeps blanking your Q autos and W hit, so neither side runs the other down.","His R All Out gives him huge defensive stats and a clean duelist 1v1 — this is his spike, so don't flip into a freshly-ulted Jax.","Iceborn Gauntlet makes you durable and sticky, but his first on-hit item keeps the duel even — hold the lead rather than force it.","By 2+ items your R peels Jax off your carries and your tank profile survives his burst — you reclaim it in teamfights, not the splitpush."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"jayce","win":["Jayce","Jayce","Jayce","Skill","K'Sante","Skill","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Jayce owns this: his ranged Q acceleration-gate poke chips you while you only have Q and can't reach him to start your Q3 combo."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is your swing window — R into Jayce converts you to a duelist and your W charge eats his E-knockback burst before you peel him."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet slow plus your Q chase closes the gap his ranged Q can no longer kite from — force side-lane all-ins here."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"You out-scale a poke Jayce: he can't burst a two-item control tank, and your R duelist window plus W's damage cut blunts his combo."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his E knockback or a gated Shock Blast, then W-charge through the damage and Q3 to pull him back in","Reach 2 items so Iceborn slow plus passive move speed lets you stick to him past his poke range","Use R All Out to turn the 1v1 into a duelist fight his squishy hammer-stance can't survive"],"foe":["Land Acceleration Gate empowered Q ranged poke to chip you out before you ever get in W range","Hold E knockback to deny your W-charge engage and reset the lane to his poke","Trade in short bursts and back off so your Q3 and W never connect, scaling his lead"]},"early":"Jayce owns levels 1 through 3 outright — his Acceleration Gate empowered Q out-ranges everything I have, and with only Q online I can't walk it down to start my combo. Don't chase a single creep into his cannon-stance poke; soak the Q chip, last-hit at max Q range, and refuse to give him a free E-knockback into hammer burst. My W-charge only cuts the damage I take — it will not stop that knockback — so I just farm and keep my HP healthy for the windows later.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are even because I finally have my Q-W-E kit and can punish a greedy poke step: bait his E knockback out first — it is 20s at rank 1 — then W-charge in and Q3 to pull him. At 6 the lane swings to me: All Out converts my tank stats into a duelist profile and the W charge cuts his cannon-Q-into-E burst, so I dash through, knock him back, and re-cast R to drag him out of his own poke spacing. The key is patience — the charge reduces damage, it does not make me unstoppable, so a live Thundering Blow still cancels the commit.","late":"This is where the EVEN matchup tips my way. A poke Jayce can't burst down a two-item control tank, and with Iceborn Gauntlet plus my passive move-speed stacking I close his kiting gap and stick on top of him. My R duelist window survives his full combo, and once his 20s Thundering Blow is spent there is nothing left to reset his spacing. I just have to respect that his early lead can snowball his team — if he got fat off the lane, force the side-lane 1v1 where my sustained DPS and lockdown beat his single burst rotation rather than letting him poke a grouped fight.","whys":["Jayce's Acceleration Gate empowered Q out-ranges your single Q and chips you before you can ever step up to combo.","He picks up his full poke rotation while you only have Q-W; his ranged cannon stance dictates the lane and you just farm.","With cannon Q plus E knockback he zones you off the wave and punishes any walk-in, owning the trade before your Q3 is online.","Now your Q-W-E combo exists — you can W-charge through his poke and Q3 him, but only when his E is down, so the window is even.","All Out converts you to a duelist and W's charge cuts his burst damage; you dash through, knock him back, and peel him out of his spacing.","Iceborn slow and your chase let you close the gap, but a fed Jayce can still kite a bad commit — it comes down to whether his E is up.","A poke Jayce can't burst a two-item control tank; your R duelist window and W's damage cut blunt his combo and you reclaim the 1v1."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"karma","win":["Karma","Karma","Karma","Karma","Skill","Karma","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Karma's empowered RQ root-and-tether plus her Mantra-shield (E) lets her poke you off the wave before your Q-W combo is even online."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W kit comes up, but with no gap-closer your only all-in is W-charge into a Q3 knock-up — and she just E-shields and walks out of your short range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out (R) is your one real window: dash through her, knock her into terrain, and the duelist stat-shift can survive a full Mantra-Q to actually punish a missed root."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Past two tank items you're a teamfight peeler again — R can rip Karma out of position before she shields and tethers your carry, your one stable lead over her."}],"wants":{"you":["Use W's charge-up damage reduction to eat her Mantra Inner Flame, then E over the wave to close the gap she keeps","Bait Focused Resolve, then W-stun her on its 12s cooldown and land the two-stack pull","Survive to 2+ items where R can recall her out of a fight before she peels your carry"],"foe":["Land Mantra-empowered RQ to root and tether you, then kite with E's move-speed shield out of Q range","Poke you with Inner Flame from 950 range each time you walk up before your combo","Stay at max range and peel — shield allies and burn your engage cooldowns from safety"]},"early":"Karma owns these first levels and it's not close — she has a point-and-click Q poke and an E shield with move speed, while I'm stuck at level 1 with only Q and no engage. I can't trade because I have to walk into her to do anything, and her Mantra-RQ root locks me down before I even get my Q3 knock-up online at level 3. Last-hit at the tip of Q, soak her poke, and don't flash-forward into a root with no W to charge through it.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still hers — she trades around my W and just E-shields, move-speeds away, and pokes me back down. The honest plan is to weather it. At 6, All Out is my one real swing: the duelist stat-shift lets me survive a full Mantra-Q burst, so if I dash through her, knock her into terrain and Q3, I can punish a missed root. But if she shields and roots clean, even my R window stays a coin-flip — that's why it's Skill, not mine.","late":"This is where I finally claw it back. Karma falls off as a poke-enchanter while my tank stacking and R come online — past two items I'm a teamfight peeler, and All Out can dash through her line and recall her out of position before she shields and tethers my carry. I win by being the bigger objective and skirmish presence, not by ever winning the straight lane poke. Force grouped fights where my W-engage and R-pull matter more than her range.","whys":["She has a ranged Mantra-Q poke and an E shield at level 1 while I have only Q and must walk into her range to do anything.","Her RQ root-and-tether locks me down and her E move-speed shield kites my second level out before my combo exists.","My Q-W combo is finally online but with no gap-closer she just E-shields and steps out of my short Q3 range.","She trades around my W charge, shields the Q3, and pokes me back down through levels 4-5 from safety.","All Out's duelist shift lets me survive a full Mantra-Q and punish a missed root, but a clean RQ-shield keeps it a coin-flip — genuinely even.","Her poke and Mantra-Q out-range my first tank item, and she peels herself with E every time I commit a W.","Past two tank items my R can recall her out of position before she shields and tethers my carry, and her enchanter poke falls off."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"kassadin","win":["K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","K'Sante","Kassadin","Kassadin","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"My Q-W combo comes fully online — Path Maker (14s) charges into a committed Kassadin and the two-stack Ntofo pull follows, while he still has no Riftwalk escape."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Kassadin's turning point: Riftwalk is a 5s blink at rank 1 falling to 2s at rank 3 — it slips my W stun and the Ntofo pull, so my lockdown loses its target."},{"when":"2 items","text":"His threat peak — once Kassadin stacks Rylai's/Nashor's his magic burst and Riftwalk spam ignore my armor stacking entirely and he kills me before I can land All Out."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"My reclaim window in a team setting: All Out turns me into a duelist and I can R-dash through Kassadin and recast to drag him off my carries even after he's scaled."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 3 and W-charge a stepped-up Kassadin into the two-stack Ntofo pull before Riftwalk exists to blink the combo","Bank an early CS and HP lead in Levels 2-5 so his weak melee phase costs him plates and tempo he can't recover","Itemize Iceborn/first tank piece and end fights on side-lane skirmishes before his Riftwalk + Rylai's spike outscales my armor"],"foe":["Survive the early melee phase behind Void Stone's magic reduction and Null Sphere's shield, conceding plates rather than trading","Reach Level 6 Riftwalk to blink out of my W stun and Ntofo pull, then snowball a 5s blink down to a 2s one in skirmishes","Stack Rylai's/Nashor's into 2 items where his magic burst and slow ignore my armor and end the 1v1 before All Out lands"]},"early":"Kassadin is meleed-down and miserable levels 1-3, and I'm built to punish exactly that. At Level 1 I only have Q, so I farm and don't walk into Null Sphere for free. The lane turns at Level 2-3 when Path Maker and the Q-W combo come online: if he steps up to last-hit, I W-charge in, knock him back, and land the two-stack Ntofo Strikes pull for a real chunk while he has no Riftwalk to escape. Void Stone cuts my magic damage and his Q leaves a shield, so commit with the full combo, not single pokes.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay my lane-control peak — I trade around his Q and bank small leads with my bulk while he's still a blink-less assassin who has to walk into my Q range to farm. Then Level 6 flips it: Riftwalk is a short-cooldown blink that slips out of my W stun and dodges the Q3 pull, so the moment I commit he can just teleport out and my lockdown finds no target. Don't burn W and R chasing a Riftwalk — bait the blink, keep him off CS, and try to deny the items that let his blink spam come online.","late":"This is Kassadin's matchup to take. Once he stacks Rylai's and Nashor's his magic burst and slow ignore my armor stacking completely — my whole tank identity does nothing against an AP scaler, and he kills me in a sidelane 1v1 before I can ever land All Out. So I don't duel him late. My job is the teamfight: All Out converts me to a duelist with extra range, and I R-dash through him and recast to recall him out of my backline, peeling the carry he wants to delete. Win on my earlier windows, then group — never bet the very late 1v1 against a hard scaler.","whys":["Kassadin is meleed-down hard at Level 1 with only Null Sphere, and I out-position him on the wave — I farm safely and deny his last-hits without eating his Q shield.","My W Path Maker comes up and any step-up to CS lets me knock him back and start a trade his weak early melee body can't answer or escape.","Even — my two-stack Ntofo Strikes pull all-in chunks him, but Null Sphere's magic shield and his ability to sit back and farm make it a coin-flip whether he trades at all.","Riftwalk arrives: a 5s blink slips out of my W stun and dodges the Ntofo Strikes pull, so my lockdown loses its target and the lane starts tilting to him.","With a first AP component his Riftwalk skirmishing and Q burst out-trade me, and my armor does nothing against his magic damage once he's blinking freely.","His two-item Rylai's/Nashor's spike ignores my armor stacking entirely — he bursts and slows my body down and ends the 1v1 before All Out can ever land.","I reclaim it only in a team fight: All Out makes me a duelist and I R-dash through him and recast to drag him off my carries, where a hard scaler can't isolate me 1v1."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"kayle","win":["Skill","K'Sante","Kayle","Skill","Kayle","Kayle","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online — W her as she steps up to melee last-hit, then the two-stack Ntofo pull, your one clean trade before she has range at all."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Kayle's first takeover spike: Divine Judgment makes her untargetable through your R All Out dash, so she just ults the burst and walks away unkillable."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Kayle hits Nashor's/Berserker's ranged form and waveclears with E autos from outside your Q-W range — she shoves and farms while you can't touch her."},{"when":"Late","text":"Her threat peak: full-build ranged Kayle kites your dash range and her DPS ignores your armor stacking, so any 1v1 past two items is unwinnable for you."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach level 3 and W a stepped-up Kayle into the two-stack Ntofo pull before her ranged form","Trade and freeze early so the jungler can punish her melee Levels 1-5 before she comes online","Use R All Out to peel her off your carries in teamfights, not to try to solo-kill her after her ult"],"foe":["Hit level 6 and use Divine Judgment to negate your R All Out engage and survive every all-in","Reach her first item and E ranged form to autohit you from outside Q-W range and shove the wave","Scale to 2+ items where her ranged DPS ignores your armor stacking and out-ranges your dash"]},"early":"Kayle is melee and miserable Levels 1-2, but so am I — I only have Q at level 1 and no engage, so I just farm and avoid feeding her any free CS-denial leverage. The real window is level 3: once my Q-W combo is up, I W into her the instant she steps forward to melee-last-hit, charging through her damage into the knock-back stun, then land the two-stack Ntofo pull. That's my one honest trade, so make it count and call my jungler — she has no escape and no range yet.","mid":"Levels 4-5 I can still bully a melee Kayle if she oversteps, banking small leads with my bulk while she has nothing to punish my cooldowns. But level 6 is where it slips: Divine Judgment makes her untargetable for the duration, so my R All Out dash just whiffs through an invulnerable target and I burn my whole kit for nothing. Do NOT R her expecting a kill — she ults the burst and walks. Spend this window crashing waves and roaming or helping my jungler invade, because the second she gets her E ranged form she stops walking into my Q-W at all.","late":"This is lost the longer it goes. Once Kayle has Nashor's and her ranged E autos she shoves me in and farms from outside everything I have — my Q is short, my W is a telegraphed charge she sidesteps, and my R converts me into a squishier duelist her DPS shreds. My armor stacking does literally nothing against her on-hit magic damage, and she out-ranges my dash, so I never touch her in a sidelane. My only job late is to group, use R All Out to recall a key carry out of the fight or peel Kayle off my backline, and pray we ended on the lead I built before level 6.","whys":["Level 1 is a wash — Kayle is one of the weakest melee level-1s in the game, but I only have Q and zero engage threat, so we both just farm.","My Q-W combo isn't fully online but I pick up W or E and become safe, and a still-melee Kayle can't punish me — I edge this farming window.","Her ranged E and waveclear start arriving and she only has to survive; even my best level-3 W-Q3 all-in is on a timer before she out-ranges me entirely.","Levels 4-5 she farms safely toward her spike while my bulk means little — she's scaling and I can't force a kill that sticks.","Divine Judgment makes her untargetable straight through my R All Out dash, so my single biggest all-in just whiffs and she survives every commit.","Her first-item ranged form lets her E-auto me from outside Q-W range and shove the wave, so she controls the lane while I can't reach her.","Teamfights are my one reclaim: I R All Out to peel or yank her off my carries, since I can never solo-duel a full-build ranged Kayle whose DPS ignores my armor."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"kennen","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"My full Q-W combo comes online — if Kennen steps in to poke or last-hit, I W-charge him and land the two-stack Ntofo pull, the only window I pin a champ who kites me forever."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Kennen's Slicing Maelstrom plus his triple Mark of the Storm stun is the lane's scariest moment — his R stun-lock chains through my W charge if I mistime it and lets him kite my whole All Out duel."},{"when":"1st item","text":"My first tank piece (Iceborn Gauntlet) lets me walk through his Q/W poke and W-stun him, forcing the side-lane all-in his energy poke can't refuse forever."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"My window: full tank into R All Out, his squishy AP body has nothing to answer it — I soak his combo behind W's charge-up damage reduction and run him down."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach level 3 and bank the W-charge into the two-stack Ntofo pull the moment he oversteps to poke","Build MR/Mercs and an early tank piece so his Mark of the Storm poke and R stun stop chunking me out of lane","Soak his level-6 Slicing Maelstrom behind W's charge-up damage reduction, then R All Out him on its 120s cooldown"],"foe":["Kite back on Lightning Rush's move speed and 950-range shuriken, never standing in my Q-W range","Stack three Mark of the Storm with Q-W and Slicing Maelstrom to stun-lock me the instant I W-charge in","Poke my low-econ early down with Thundering Shuriken and zone me off the wave before my item spike"]},"early":"Kennen has no engage threat at level 1 and neither do I with only Q, so the first level is a farm standoff — I tank a little Thundering Shuriken poke and last-hit with the tip of Ntofo Strikes. The problem starts at 2-3 once his Mark of the Storm chain is online: he Q-pokes me, weaves an Electrical Surge auto, and the third stack stuns me before I can ever reach him. My only real answer is level 3 — if he steps into Q range to CS or poke, I Path Maker charge into him and land the two-stack Ntofo Strikes pull, the one trade I actually win. Otherwise I eat poke and stay healthy.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are his to control. Lightning Rush move speed and a 950-range shuriken mean he kites my short Q-W range all day and chips me down while I have no way to close without burning W. At 6 Slicing Maelstrom plus a three-mark Mark of the Storm stun is the scary window — his R runs a flat 120s but stun-locks me the moment my charge ends, and he kites the All Out duel for free. So I don't dive a healthy Kennen with R up: I bait his Q, soak the ult on my bulk, and commit W only once Maelstrom is spent.","late":"This is the only stretch that swings to me, and it's why the lane stays tricky rather than lost. Kennen is a squishy AP carry with no percent-HP or true damage, so my MR and HP actually matter against him — once I have a tank item or two, his Q/W poke stops zoning me and I walk through it. With first item I force the side-lane all-in his energy pool can't refuse forever, and from 2+ items my R All Out flips into a duelist profile that runs his fragile body down after I soak his combo behind W's charge-up damage reduction. In teamfights my R peels him off my carries before his AoE Maelstrom lands. I have to reach this window even on his terms — close on my tank spike, don't bet on out-poking him.","whys":["Neither of us has engage at level 1 — I farm with the tip of Ntofo Strikes and tank a little Thundering Shuriken poke while he can't punish me yet.","His Mark of the Storm chain comes online — Q plus an Electrical Surge auto stuns me from outside my range before I can ever reach him.","My Q-W combo is up but Lightning Rush's move speed kites it and his 950-range shuriken pokes me, so only a level-3 W-charge punishes an overstep.","Lightning Rush move speed and 950-range poke chip my low-econ body while I have no tool at all to close the short Q-W gap on him.","Slicing Maelstrom plus a three-mark stun-lock chains through my W charge if I mistime it and lets him kite my whole All Out duel for free.","His shuriken poke and a 120s Maelstrom keep zoning me off the wave, and my tankiness isn't online enough yet to walk through it and pin him.","Full tank into R All Out beats his squishy AP body — MR and HP answer his magic damage, and W's charge-up damage reduction eats his combo."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"kled","win":["Skill","Kled","Kled","Kled","Kled","Kled","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Kled's spike: mounted Skaarl bullies you off the wave with Beartrap-on-a-Rope (Q) grabs and Violent Tendencies autos before your Q-W combo is fully online to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your window: All Out (R) converts your tank stats to a duelist profile and lets you survive his remount burst, then W-stun him against a wall for a real 1v1 win."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Kled's threat peak: with a first bruiser item his mounted Bear Trap pull plus a Skaarl remount out-trades your Iceborn Gauntlet durability in extended skirmishes."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your reclaim window: from two items you peel him in teamfights — W's charge-up damage reduction eats his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) and R yanks him off your carry."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive his level 2-3 mounted aggression by farming at Ntofo's 450 range, then bank a lead once your Q-W combo is online","Hit level 6 and use All Out (R) to win the duelist 1v1 his remount burst can no longer out-trade","Charge W through his damage and stun him against terrain on its 14s cooldown, before he restores courage"],"foe":["Bully you mounted at level 2-3 with Beartrap (Q) grabs and Violent Tendencies attack speed before your combo answers","Land the mounted Bear Trap pull to force the skirmish, then restore Skaarl's courage and remount for the damage spike","Snowball his early kill pressure and use Chaaaaaarge! (R) to engage and scale his bruiser items past your tank stats"]},"early":"Kled owns the early because I'm weak at level 1 with only Q and no engage, so I just farm and concede the wave while he sits mounted on Skaarl. From level 2-3 his Beartrap-on-a-Rope (Q) grab plus Violent Tendencies attack speed lets him bully me before my Q-W combo is fully online to punish. I do not walk into his Q pull range to contest a CS — I last-hit at the tip of Ntofo Strikes (Q) and accept the chip. The thing to bait is his dismounted Q: if he whiffs the grab, Skaarl is gone and I can step up, but until then I farm and survive.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay his — a mounted Kled out-trades me in extended melee and his remount sustain heals the chip I do land, so I bank what farm I can and wait for 6. All Out (R) is my one clean flip: it strips my bulk but converts me to a duelist who survives his remount burst, and I pair it with a charged Path Maker (W) to stun him against a wall and win that single 1v1. I do not blow R into a full-health mounted Kled with his own R up — I bait his Chaaaaaarge! (R) engage and his dismount first, then commit when he can't remount out of my stun.","late":"My armor stacking does nothing against a fed snowballing Kled in the sidelane, and his first bruiser item plus a Skaarl remount out-grinds my Iceborn durability one-on-one — he's the scaler in any solo skirmish, so I don't duel him alone. My reclaim is the teamfight from two items: Path Maker's (W) charge-up damage reduction eats his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! engage and the wall-stun locks him, then All Out's (R) yank pulls him off my carry the instant he dives. I close on my level 6 / teamfight peel windows and let his early kill pressure mean nothing in a 5v5 where I out-position him.","whys":["You're a weak level-1 with only Q and no engage, but so is a Kled who hasn't snapped into his mounted aggro yet — farm safely and set up the lane.","Mounted Kled spikes at 2 with Beartrap (Q) grabs and Violent Tendencies attack speed, out-bullying you before your Q-W combo is fully online to answer.","His full mounted kit out-trades you in melee and restoring Skaarl's courage undoes your chip — concede the wave, farm at Ntofo's 450.","A mounted Kled keeps the trade edge through 4-5 and his remount damage spike beats your tank stats if you step up, so you bank farm and wait.","Kled's level-6 Chaaaaaarge! (R) and overall early pressure still edge the lane, but your All Out (R) wall-stun all-in is the one window you can flip — bait his dismount first.","His first bruiser item plus the mounted Bear Trap pull and a remount out-grind your Iceborn Gauntlet durability in any extended sidelane skirmish.","From two items you peel him in teamfights — W's charge-up damage reduction eats his R engage and All Out yanks him off your carry, which his lead can't answer."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"lillia","win":["Skill","Lillia","K'Sante","Skill","Lillia","Lillia","Lillia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W combo comes online — your one real window to catch Lillia against a wall with Path Maker before she has W/E to bounce out."},{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Lillia's threat ramps: her W (Watch Out!) and E (Swirlseed) start chunking you with magic poke your armor does nothing against."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her R (Lilting Lullaby) sleeps you — she lands max-charge W on the sleeping target for a burst your tank HP cannot absorb."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Full-AP Lillia kites you forever — her DOT passive and move speed outrun your Q/W and your stacked armor is worthless into her magic damage."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Watch Out! Eep! and Swirlseed, then W her into a wall for the stun and the two-stack pull","Use the level 3 window to all-in before she has the move speed to perma-kite you","Force a gank or roam — you cannot solo-kill a Lillia who respects your Q/W range"],"foe":["Kite you with Swirlseed's 700-range slow, chunking you with damage your armour cannot answer","Stack Blooming Blows move speed on every spell hit to stay outside your 450 Q range all game","Reach 6 and combo R sleep into a max-charge W for burst that beats your tank HP"]},"early":"Lillia has no hard CC and no escape until she ramps move speed, so level 1 is genuinely even — you both just farm. But the second she has W (Watch Out! Eep!) and E (Swirlseed) at level 2, she starts poking you with damage your armor stacking does absolutely nothing against, and she dances just outside your 450-range Q. Don't chase a pull you can't land — Blooming Blows keeps stacking her move speed and your Q slow is too little to pin her. Your only clean window is level 3: bait her W, then W her into a wall for the extended stun and follow with the two-stack Ntofo pull.","mid":"This is where it slips away. Your level 3-5 tank-control peak means nothing if she just kites — she has the move speed off her passive and abilities to stay outside your Q/W range and chunk you with the DOT and Swirlseed all day. At 6 her R (Lilting Lullaby) is the problem: she sleeps you, then lands a max-charge W on the sleeping target for a burst that your tank HP eats far worse than her magic damage suggests. Your R (All Out) strips your bulk for a duelist profile, but you can't catch her to use it — she's already three move-speed stacks gone before your dash lands.","late":"You lose the long game outright. Full-AP Lillia is a perpetual-motion kiter — her max-health DOT passive and stacked move speed outrun every dash you have, and your armor-stacking identity is dead weight against magic damage that turns true on Q's edge. You can't peel what you can't touch, and All Out's duelist shift doesn't matter when she's never in front of you. Your only path is to have snowballed off a level 3 all-in or a gank; if the game goes late even, she wins by attrition. Group, force objectives early, and let your team apply the lockdown you can't.","whys":["Lillia has no level-1 CC or escape and weak base trades — but you have only Q and no engage either, so neither of you can commit and you both farm.","Her W (Watch Out!) and E (Swirlseed) come online and poke you with magic damage your armor stacking completely ignores, and she kites outside your Q range.","Your full Q-W combo is online — your one window to W her into a wall for the stun and the two-stack Ntofo pull before Q stacks her move speed up.","She kites your 450-range Q with Blooming Blows' ramping move speed, but you still threaten a wall-stun if she misplays, so it stays a coin-flip.","Her R (Lilting Lullaby) sleeps you and sets up a max-charge W burst that your tank HP absorbs poorly, while your All Out strips bulk for a duel you can't catch her in.","Her first AP item amplifies poke your armour cannot answer — Blooming Blows' edge even deals true damage — and she stays outside your dash range.","Full-AP Lillia kites you forever with her DOT passive and move speed, and stacked armor is worthless into her magic damage — she reclaims the game by attrition."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"lucian","win":["Lucian","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Lucian"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Lucian's window: with only my Q (Ntofo Strikes) and no engage threat, his passive double-shot and Q/W poke chip me freely and I just farm the cannon."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"My Q-W combo comes fully online — if he steps up to last-hit I W (Path Maker) into him and land the two-stack Ntofo pull for my first real trade of the lane."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is double-edged: it gives me a duelist 1v1 but strips my tankiness, so I only ult him when I can W-stun and close, never as a raw stat check into his double-shot kite."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His takeover: a two-item Lucian's sustained DPS and E-dash kiting shred me once my W charge is the only thing keeping me alive and All Out is on cooldown."}],"wants":{"you":["Walk him down behind W (Path Maker)'s damage-reduced charge so his poke can't stop me, then land the two-stack pull","Bait Relentless Pursuit before I commit W, so he can't slip the stun and re-kite me","Hold Q3 and All Out for when he has no dash up, turning my duelist window into a kill before he resets distance"],"foe":["Poke me with Lightslinger double-shots and Piercing Light from outside my 450 Q range","Save Relentless Pursuit to slip my W charge so the stun whiffs and he keeps kiting","Reach 2+ items where his sustained DPS and dash-kiting out-trade me once All Out is down"]},"early":"Lucian owns level 1-2 here — I only have my Q (Ntofo Strikes) cleave and no engage threat, so his Lightslinger double-shot and Piercing Light poke chip me down while I just farm and concede the first level. Don't try to fight under his harass; soak the wave at Q range and stack my passive marks off any auto I can land. The moment that flips is level 3: with my full Q-W combo I can W (Path Maker) charge into him and land the two-stack Ntofo pull for a real trade he can't poke his way out of.","mid":"Levels 3 through 5 are my lane-control peak. He has to walk into my range to CS, and a charged W (Path Maker) takes reduced damage through his poke, so I bank small leads by W-stunning him into the two-stack pull whenever he steps up. The key is patience: bait Relentless Pursuit first, because if he saves it he slips my W and re-kites my short range. At 6 it goes even — All Out gives me a duelist profile to win the 1v1, but it strips my bulk, so I only commit when I can land W and close, never as a raw stat-check.","late":"Late game tilts back to Lucian. Once he has two-plus items, his sustained double-shot DPS and constant E-dash kiting shred me the instant my W charge ends and All Out is on cooldown — my armor stacking does nothing against a ranged carry who never stands still. So I have to cash my mid-game leads before this; close the side lane on my 3-5 and first-item windows. After that, stop trying to solo-duel him and play to my real strength: R (All Out) recasting to peel him out of his backline in a 5v5, where he can't just kite me in a straight line.","whys":["Lucian owns level 1 — I have only Q (Ntofo Strikes), no engage, and his passive double-shot plus Q/W poke chip me while I'm stuck farming.","Even at 2 — I pick up W or E and get safer, but he still out-ranges me, so it's a wash on whether he can keep poking without overstepping.","My full Q-W combo is online: W (Path Maker) charges through his poke and the two-stack Ntofo pull lands the first trade he can't answer.","I trade around his cooldowns and bank small leads with my bulk — he has to walk into my Q range to CS and eats a W-stun every overstep.","All Out is a coin-flip at 6 — it wins me the duelist 1v1 if I land W and close, but strips my tankiness if he kites the charge with E.","My first tank-engage item makes my W disruption stick and forces side-lane fights, but his sustained poke keeps it a genuine skill window, not a free kill.","Two-item Lucian's double-shot DPS and E-dash kiting out-trade me once All Out is down and armor stacking does nothing — close before this or peel him in teamfights."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"malphite","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Malphite","K'Sante","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online — W a committed Malphite, land the two-stack Ntofo pull, and Path Maker's true damage chunks his armour stack."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out turns you into a duelist and its knockback peels him off your carry — but Ground Slam grounds the R dash on a 7s cooldown, so time the commit off his E, not his R."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet plus your passive magic damage out-trades a pure-armor Malphite in any side-lane skirmish — force fights at terrain for the W stun."},{"when":"Lvl 6+ (his R)","text":"Unstoppable Force (130/115/100s) is his one real threat — if it lands while your W is down, you eat a full engage and the gank behind it."}],"wants":{"you":["Land the two-stack Ntofo pull after a W stun so Path Maker's true damage shreds his armour","Charge W through his R engage on reduced damage, then re-cast All Out to drag him off","Trade with your passive magic damage, since his armor-stacking does nothing to it"],"foe":["Poke you with Q slows to drain your low early mana before you reach combo range","Ground you with Seismic Shard or Ground Slam so your W, E and R dashes all die","Stack armor and W you for value, betting his teamfight R outscales your side-lane duel"]},"early":"Two tanks farming — this is dead-even until level 3. Seismic Shard chips you and steals your move speed toward his Thunderclap auto, so don't walk straight at him with your tiny early mana pool; last-hit at the tip of your Q instead. The key fact: he stacks armour, and Path Maker deals true damage, so the longer trades go the more you win them. Just don't get caught by his Q with your W charge down.","mid":"Levels 3 through 5 are your window. Bait his W or Q, then W-charge into him for the terrain stun, land the two-stack Ntofo pull, and let Path Maker's true damage carve his armour-stacked bar — resistances do not answer it. At 6, All Out is a real 1v1 button because it converts you to a duelist, but it sheds your tankiness, so only pop it to commit a kill or to peel, never to clear a wave. The real trap is Ground Slam: on 7s it grounds your W, E and R alike, so never start into a fresh one.","late":"It flattens back to even — two control tanks who can't solo-kill each other and both bring a hard engage to teamfights. Your edge is that Path Maker's true damage ignores his armour stack entirely; his edge is a longer-range, lower-skill R engage on your carries, plus two grounding spells that switch your dashes off. Win the side-lane skirmishes with your duelist All Out and use your R to peel his R off your backline. Don't bet on a 1v1 — this lane closes on map pressure, not a kill.","whys":["Two of the weakest level-1 tanks in lane — you only have Q, he only has Q, so it's a pure farm standoff.","He picks up W to auto-poke and you pick up W or E to stay safe — neither can commit, so it stays even.","Your full Q-W combo lands: W stun into the two-stack pull, and Path Maker's true damage ignores his armour.","Your lane-control peak — trade around Thunderclap (10s) and Seismic Shard (8s), and W's true damage beats his armour.","Ground Slam (7s) grounds All Out, Path Maker and Footwork alike, so your whole engage can be switched off — his 6 edges it.","Iceborn plus Path Maker's true damage out-skirmishes a pure-armour Malphite in the side lane — force fights now.","Both reclaim parity as teamfight tanks; his R engages your carry, your R peels it back, and neither solo-kills the other."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"maokai","win":["Skill","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online — W a committed Maokai and land the two-stack Ntofo pull once his W dash is spent."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out turns you into a duelist who out-DPSes his sustain — recast R yanks him out before saplings reset, your cleanest 1v1 of the lane."},{"when":"Maokai W","text":"Twisted Advance goes UNTARGETABLE mid-dash and then roots — burst spent into it is wasted, so wait it out and commit on its 14/13/12/11/10s cooldown."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Two armor-stacking tanks grind to a stalemate — neither kills the other, so the lead comes from roams and teamfight R peels, not the 1v1."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Twisted Advance, then W-charge on reduced damage and land the two-stack pull","Reach Level 3 and trade on top of his Q-knockback cooldown, not into his saplings","Use Level 6 All Out to win the duelist 1v1 his tank sustain can't answer"],"foe":["Ground you with Bramble Smash so your W, E and R dashes die, then root and sapling you","Sustain through your Q poke with his passive and trade even all lane","Drag the lane to a 2-item armor stalemate where neither tank can close"]},"early":"Two tanks farming — neither of you wins Level 1, so just hit your Q tip and stack passive marks on him. The thing to respect is his W: it goes untargetable mid-dash and roots on arrival, so anything you spend into it is wasted, and then Bramble Smash plus a sapling free-hit you. Don't throw W at random — hold it until he lands, and remember Bramble Smash grounds your dashes.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are your window. With the full Q-W combo you out-trade him: charge W through his damage, land the two-stack Ntofo pull, and his W is a 14s cooldown he cannot re-dash on. At 6, All Out is your real edge — it converts tank stats into duelist damage that out-DPSes Sap Magic, and the recast yanks him out before his saplings reset. Trade on Bramble Smash's 7s cooldown, never into a sapling field.","late":"This levels off into a true tank mirror. Once you're both armor-stacking, neither of you bursts the other down — your R duelist spike survives him but can't execute through his sustain, and his W-root can't kill you either. The win comes off the map: your R is the better teamfight tool, so peel a carry with All Out and let your lead come from objectives and roams, not the dead-even 1v1.","whys":["Both of you are weak at Level 1 with no engage — you have only Q, he only saplings, so it's a farming stalemate.","He picks up W or Q knockback and you pick up W or E — both get safer, neither gets a kill threat, so it stays even.","Your full Q-W combo lands first: charge W on reduced damage and land the two-stack Ntofo pull on a Maokai whose W is spent.","Your tank lane-control peak — trade on Bramble Smash's 7/6.5/6/5.5/5s and bank leads his even trades can't match.","All Out converts you to a duelist who out-DPSes his passive sustain, and the recast pulls him out before saplings reset.","First items even it back out — Iceborn keeps you durable but his sustain and W-root mean neither tank can close the 1v1.","Two armor-stackers stalemate: your R can't execute through his sustain and his root can't kill you, so the lead comes off the map."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"mel","win":["Skill","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo is online — W-charge through her Q poke into the two-stack Ntofo pull is your first punish window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out converts you to a duelist and dashes through her — but Rebuttal (W) reflects projectiles, so force it out before your Q."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet makes you sticky and durable; her short Q range can't kite a slowed, marked target out of your reach."},{"when":"Late","text":"Her biggest window — Golden Eclipse detonates every Overwhelm stack globally, so leaving lane chipped is what actually kills you."}],"wants":{"you":["Walk up behind minions, W-charge through her Q poke on reduced damage, then land the two-stack pull","Use E over a wall or off the wave to flank her short-range Q and pin her with W against terrain","Reach Iceborn Gauntlet so its slow-on-hit stacks with Ntofo's and her ranged kite stops working"],"foe":["Land Q pokes from max range and back off before your W-charge releases, chipping you each wave","Hold Rebuttal (W) to reflect your Ntofo Strikes and blank your committed engage","Stall to 2+ items where Solar Snare zoning and Overwhelm execute beat your armour from 1000 range"]},"early":"She has only her Q poke and no escape at Level 1, but so do you — last-hit at the tip of your Q and don't burn W charging at a target who can just step back. Eat a little poke; her Q chip cannot out-damage your tank base stats this early. The moment you hit Level 3 and have W plus Q online, the lane flips: bait her Q, then W-charge through it on reduced damage and land the Ntofo pull.","mid":"This is your takeover. Once you can W-charge through her poke and land the two-stack Ntofo pull, she has no dash to escape your range — pin her against the wave or terrain and her squishy frame folds. At 6, All Out lets you dash through her and duel, but respect Rebuttal: it reflects projectiles, so your own Ntofo Strikes bounces back at you. Force it out — 26s even at rank 5 — then commit. With Iceborn your slow glues you to her and 950 poke cannot kite.","late":"You own every clean 1v1 through your item spikes, and Mel stays beatable late provided you respect two things: she pokes from 950 range, outside your Q, and Rebuttal reflects projectiles straight back at you. Your armour does nothing against her magic, so build MR and force Rebuttal out before every engage. Close the side lane and snowball your earlier leads before Golden Eclipse can detonate a chipped team from anywhere.","whys":["She only has Q poke at Level 1 — but so do you, so just farm at Q range and don't overextend into her chip.","Still mostly her poke window with no full combo for you yet; soak Q damage and set up your Level 3 spike.","Your Path Maker plus the two-stack Ntofo pull comes online — bait her Q, charge through it on reduced damage, and pin her.","Your tank lane-control peak: you trade around her Q cooldown and bank leads her short-range poke can't punish.","All Out turns you into a duelist and dashes through her, and she has no dash to answer — bait Rebuttal (W) first, not her R.","Iceborn Gauntlet's slow plus the Ntofo slow make her kite useless and keep her pinned inside your 450 range.","Full-AP Mel reclaims it: she pokes from outside your Q/W and her R can reflect your engage burst, and your armor does nothing to magic damage."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"mordekaiser","win":["Mordekaiser","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Mordekaiser","K'Sante","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Mordekaiser hits his Q1-W spike first and out-trades you while you only have Q charges, so give ground until your full Q-W combo is up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R Realm of Death rips you into a 1v1 and steals your stats — a 140s cooldown at rank 1; never get isolated low, and W-charge to cut the damage inside."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His first AP item makes the realm a near-guaranteed kill, but Iceborn Gauntlet plus your bulk lets you W his Q slam and Q3 knock-up him before he heals it back."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"You out-scale: stacked armor and HP plus R's peel mean his Q isolated bonus and W shield can't burst you, and you drag him off your carries."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach your Level 3 Q-W combo and trade only when his W shield/heal is on cooldown","Bait or W-charge through his R realm so you survive the 1v1 instead of feeding it","Stack armor and HP into 2+ items where his single-target Q burst stops killing you"],"foe":["Land E pull into Q isolated slam to chunk you before your combo comes online","Win the level 2-3 window with W shield up while you're still Q-only","Catch you isolated and ult you into Realm of Death to steal your tank stats"]},"early":"Morde owns the very early levels here — at 2 and 3 his Q slam plus W shield/heal out-trades you while you still only have Q charges and no engage. Don't walk up to throw a Q he can E-pull and Q-isolate; last-hit at range and respect his level-2 spike. The good news is he has no dash, so once you have your Q-W combo you can pick the trades, not him.","mid":"Level 6 is the danger window: his R drags you into a 1v1 and steals your stats, and a low K'Sante just dies in the realm. Never get caught isolated — and if he ults you, hold W: the charge-up reduces damage taken, so spend it on his Obliterate slam. Around your first item you flip it: Iceborn plus your bulk lets you eat that Q, Q3 knock-up him, and burst him before the 8s Indestructible heal returns.","late":"This is where you take over. With 2+ items your stacked armor and HP shrug off his single-target Q burst and W shield, and his realm steal does far less against a fully tanky K'Sante. Use R All Out to peel him off your carries in fights and recast to drag him out of the dive. He has no escape — once you're durable, his only win is catching someone alone, so deny the isolated picks and you own the late game.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1 — he has no engage without W up and you have only Q, so just farm and set up the lane.","Mordekaiser's level-2 Q-W spike out-trades your Q-only kit; his shield and heal win the short trade.","At 3 he can E-pull you into his Q isolated slam before your full combo answers — concede the window and farm safe.","Your Q-W combo and tank bulk come online, so you trade evenly around his W cooldown — it's a skill window now.","His R Realm of Death isolates you and steals your tank stats — a clean 6 belongs to him unless you W through it.","His first AP item turns the realm into a near-guaranteed kill, so he edges the first-item window if you get caught.","You out-scale: stacked armor and HP blank his Q burst, and R peels him off your team — the late game is yours."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"nasus","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","K'Sante","Nasus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full combo is online — Path Maker (W) knocks back and stuns a stacking Nasus, then two Q stacks pull him off the wave pre-Wither."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out turns you into a duelist who survives his slow drain — dash through him and run him down before his R lifesteal carries the fight."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet makes you a sticky wall — perma-shove and freeze him off the wave so his Q never stacks."},{"when":"Late","text":"Nasus's biggest window: a 300+ stack Q with Wither shutting off your attack speed shreds you even through armor — close before this."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and W a stack-hungry Nasus, then Q3 knock-up him off the wave before Wither is online","Deny Q stacks by freezing or shoving so his last-hit damage never ramps","Use All Out at 6 to win the duelist 1v1 and snowball before his late-game stacks matter"],"foe":["Free-farm Q stacks and hit his power timer at 200-300 stacks","Land Wither to cripple your attack speed and move speed so you can't kite or peel","Stall lane to 2+ items where his stacked Q and R lifesteal out-duel your armor"]},"early":"Nasus is helpless at Level 1-2 — he has no stacks, no Wither until later, and just wants to last-hit with Q. Don't let him free-farm: at Level 3 you have the full combo, so Path Maker (W) knocks back and stuns a Nasus who steps up to stack, and two Q hits pull him back in. Every stack you deny is permanent damage off his late game, so trade hard while Wither is still a 15s cooldown.","mid":"This is your takeover window. With Iceborn Gauntlet you become a sticky wall — perma-shove so he can't safely stack Q, and freeze him under tower. At 6 your R All Out converts you into a duelist who survives his slow Q-Wither-E drain: dash through him, and even with Wither slowing your attack speed your burst plus mobility wins the 1v1 before his R lifesteal turns it. Bank these leads — your bulk and CC own a Nasus who has nothing but stacks he hasn't earned yet.","late":"Be honest: late is his game, not yours. A 300+ stack Q with Wither shutting off your attack speed shreds you even through full armor, and his R lifesteal lets him out-sustain your duelist form. Your armor stacking does nothing against a percent-melting stacked Q. You must close the game on your earlier windows — group, take towers, and use R to peel his Wither off your carries in fights rather than betting on a 1v1 you no longer win.","whys":["You both have weak Level 1s — he only has Q to last-hit, you only have Q with no engage, so just deny his early stacks and farm.","You pick up W or E and become safer while he still has no Wither and no stacks — start contesting his last-hits.","Your full Q-W combo is online: W a committed Nasus and Q3 knock-up to deny stacks before he ever gets Wither.","Your tank lane-control peak — you trade around his cooldowns and shove him off the wave so his Q never ramps.","All Out makes you a duelist who survives his slow drain — dash through and run him down before his R lifesteal turns the fight.","Iceborn Gauntlet makes you a sticky disruptive wall — freeze and perma-shove so he can't safely stack Q.","He out-scales hard: Wither guts your attack and move speed while Fury of the Sands burns percent health — armour alone does not answer that."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"nautilus","win":["Skill","Skill","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","K'Sante","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your combo comes fully online — Path Maker's stun into a second Ntofo Strikes stack pulls him in, a trade a 14s single-target hook cannot answer."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your lane-control peak: you trade around his Dredge Line cooldown, tank the passive root proc with W's damage resist, and bank small leads on his missed hooks."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out gives you a duelist 1v1, but it strips your bulk right as his R Depth Charge knockup plus passive root chain locks you for his full E-AOE — a double-edged window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Nautilus's threat window: an Iceborn/tank Naut who lands Dredge Line into his passive root and Depth Charge chains CC for longer than one Path Maker charge covers."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and W-charge a committed Nautilus, then Ntofo Strikes third-cast knockup-pull him for a trade his single hook can't match","Bank lane control at Levels 4-5 by trading on his Dredge Line cooldown while W eats his passive root proc","Save Path Maker's damage-reduction charge for his Depth Charge, not to engage into a hook that is up"],"foe":["Land Dredge Line hook to drag you in, proc his passive root on the follow-up auto, and E-AOE you while you're stuck","Bait out your W charge, then engage his hook-into-root-into-Depth Charge chain when you can't go unstoppable","Stall the lane even and let his tank scaling and superior teamfight CC matter more than your sidelane duel"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — you only have Q and no engage, and Nautilus has Dredge Line but can't all-in either, so farm with Ntofo Strikes and stay out of its 1150 range with the wave between you. Staggering Blow roots on his first attack against you, so never open a toe-to-toe auto trade before W. At Level 3 it tips your way — Path Maker's charge cuts the damage he returns, then your second Q stack pulls him in, and a 14s hook can't trade back with that.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your lane-control peak. Trade around Dredge Line — bait the hook, and inside those 14 seconds you W in, eat the passive root through the charge's damage reduction, and land both Q stacks for a trade he can't answer. Bank those leads. At 6 it goes even: All Out wins the raw 1v1 but strips your resists exactly when Depth Charge knocks you up into Riptide's slow, so never ult into a full-CC Nautilus. Bait his R or his hook first, then commit.","late":"This stays a coin-flip into the late game and that's honest — a tank mirror where neither side deletes the other in a side lane. His first-item spike is his window: hook into passive root into Depth Charge locks you down for longer than one Path Maker charge covers, and Titan's Wrath shields the burst you answer with, so force that 12s shield out before you commit. Your edge is teamfights, where All Out peels a key carry out of his lockdown. Don't bet on out-scaling him — close on your 3-to-5 trading windows and the first reset, then group.","whys":["You only have Q and no engage threat, but so does a hook-reliant Nautilus who can't commit at 1 either — farm safely and never auto-trade into his passive root.","You pick up W or E and get safer, but he keeps Dredge Line as a poke-and-engage threat, so neither of you owns the level outright yet.","Your full combo is online — Path Maker knocks him back and stuns, then two Q stacks pull him in; his 14s hook can't match that.","You trade around his Dredge Line cooldown and W's damage resist eats his passive root proc, so you bank small leads on every hook he misses.","All Out wins the raw 1v1 but strips your bulk just as his Depth Charge plus passive root can chain-lock you for his E-AOE — it's a genuine coin-flip.","His Iceborn/tank first item lands a full Dredge-into-root-into-Depth Charge chain that outlasts your one W charge — a tank mirror neither side stomps.","It stays even: you peel a carry with R All Out in fights, but his point-and-click hook and ult CC match your reliability, so close on your earlier windows instead."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"neeko","win":["Neeko","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Neeko","K'Sante","Neeko"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full combo is online — Path Maker stuns a committed Neeko, then a second Q stack pulls her back, punishing every step into E range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out turns you into a duelist who survives Pop Blossom's stun and Q burst, then dashes through and shreds her — she has no escape, only a clone."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn / first tank piece makes you durable enough to walk through her poke and run her down the moment her E-root is on cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Neeko's biggest window — full-AP she sits back with W clone, lands a hidden R or E-root and one-shots you before R can convert; never facecheck for her."}],"wants":{"you":["Walk down Neeko the instant her E-root and Q whiff — your bulk eats her poke and she has no escape","Land Path Maker into terrain for the stun, then pull with your second Q stack so she cannot kite","Use R All Out to survive her R stun burst and convert to duelist damage, killing her before she pools to safety"],"foe":["Land E-root from range or off her W clone to lock you down for the Q-into-R poke combo","Hide her real model with W clone and bait your W charge / R onto a fake","Scale to full AP and one-shot you from fog with a hidden R stun before All Out can reach her"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you only have Q and no engage, and Neeko just wants to poke with Q and farm, so trade Q-cleave for Q and last-hit. The turn comes at 2-3: once your W and the full Q combo are online, she cannot step up to E-root or land Q poke without you charging W into her and following with Q3 to knock her up and drag her in. She is squishy with no dash, so every time her root or Q misses, you get a free walk-down — punish the cooldown, do not chase blindly past her clone.","mid":"This is your lane. Bank small leads through 4-5 with your bulk — you out-trade her poke and heal nothing back but tank it all while she has to land a skillshot E-root to do anything. At 6, All Out is your answer to her burst: pop it to survive the R-stun-into-Q combo, dash through her, and her squishy AP body folds before she can pool to safety. The one thing to respect is her W clone — do not blow your W charge or your R recall onto a fake, and do not facecheck brush where a hidden Neeko can land R first.","late":"Late game flips to her. Full-AP Neeko sits behind her team, disguises with W, and a single landed R stun or E-root from fog deletes you before All Out can even reach her — your armor stacking does nothing against her AP burst. You must have closed this lane on your 3-to-first-item windows; if it goes long, your job is to never get picked, hold your R to peel her off your carries the instant she flickers her clone, and let your team punish her squishiness rather than betting on a 1v1.","whys":["You have only Q with no engage and she just wants to poke and farm — neither of you threatens a kill, so last-hit at Q range.","Your W comes online and she has no dash to escape it — step up and threaten the charge so she cannot freely E-root or Q-poke.","Full combo is live: Path Maker knocks her into terrain and stuns, two Q stacks drag her back, and a no-dash mage cannot answer.","You out-trade her poke with pure bulk and punish every missed E-root with a free walk-down — bank the lead.","All Out lets you survive her R stun plus Q burst, then dash through and shred her before she pools the combo.","Your first tank item makes you unkillable to her poke and you run her down whenever the E-root is on cooldown.","Full-AP Neeko kites with W clone and one-shots you with a hidden R from fog — armor does nothing, so play safe and let your team kill her."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"olaf","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Olaf owns it — his axe (Q) slow and Reckless Swing true damage poke you down before you have a W or combo to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full kit is online — Path Maker stuns a committed Olaf, a second Q stack pulls him in, and your bulk eats his trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6 (Olaf R)","text":"Olaf's Ragnarok makes him immune to disables for as long as he keeps attacking — never bank a fight on locking down an Olaf who still has it."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His Q-slow plus axe-pickup resets let him stick to you and his true damage shreds your armor stacking — fights become coinflips, not a clean win."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3, stun a committed Olaf with Path Maker, then pull him before his axe resets","Dodge his thrown axe (Q) so he can't pick it up for the move-speed and reset his trade","Use bulk to win short trades around his Reckless Swing self-damage, not extended ones into his lifesteal"],"foe":["Land his axe (Q) and walk over to pick it up for the slow plus reset, keeping you stuck","Trade with Reckless Swing true damage that ignores your armor stacking entirely","Pop Ragnarok (R) to break your W stun and tank through your combo with CC immunity"]},"early":"Level 1 belongs to Olaf — his axe (Q) slow plus Reckless Swing true damage out-trade you while you only have Ntofo Strikes (Q) and no W to answer. Don't walk up to last-hit into a thrown axe; sidestep it so he can't retrieve it for the move speed and trade reset, and just farm at the tip of your Q. The moment you hit 3 and have Path Maker (W) plus Footwork (E), you stop conceding — but until then his poke is real true damage your armor does nothing about.","mid":"Levels 3 to 5 are your window. Charge Path Maker when he commits — the longer the charge, the longer the stun into a wall — then take your second Q stack to pull him back and stick the cleave. Your bulk wins short exchanges around Reckless Swing's self-damage, so trade in bursts and back off before his axe slow and his missing-health lifesteal grind you down. At 6 it flips to a coinflip: Ragnarok makes him immune to disables for as long as he keeps attacking, so never bet a fight on landing your W stun into an Olaf still holding R.","late":"This stays a knife-fight at 2+ items rather than a clean win. Olaf's true damage ignores everything your armor stacking buys you, and his Q-slow plus axe-pickup resets let him glue to you, so you can't kite the duel out. Your value is teamfight peel — R All Out to recall a carry out of his dive — but the instant he's in Ragnarok your CC is off the table, so peel BEFORE he ults and force him to spend R reaching you. Close on your earlier mid-game leads; this lane never becomes free.","whys":["Olaf out-trades you at 1 with his axe (Q) slow and Reckless Swing true damage while you have only Q and no W to answer.","You pick up W or E and stop bleeding, but his thrown-axe poke and lifesteal keep it a genuine coinflip until your combo is full.","Your full kit is online — Path Maker stuns, the second Q stack pulls, and your bulk eats a trade his self-damage can't sustain.","Levels 4-5 are your tank lane-control peak — trade in bursts around his Reckless Swing cost and bank small leads with your bulk.","Ragnarok makes him immune to disables while he keeps attacking, so your W stun and Q pull stop applying — 6 is a coinflip.","Your first tank-engage item keeps you durable, but his Q-slow and axe resets let him stick — neither side cleanly owns the trade.","His true damage ignores your armor stacking and his slows glue him to you, so late fights stay a coinflip you can't kite out."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"ornn","win":["Skill","Ornn","Ornn","Skill","Skill","Ornn","Ornn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full combo comes online — Path Maker stuns a committed Ornn into a wall, then a second Q stack pulls him back into your cleave."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Trade around Searing Charge (E), 14s at rank 1 — with his only dash down he has no escape and you out-bully an immobile tank."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is a wash here — it wins the duel but strips your bulk, and his Call of the Forge God (R) can re-knockup you twice through it, so don't bet the lane on it."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Both of you go full tank and the lane flatlines into a CC-trading teamfight stalemate — your R peel vs his double knockup decides fights, not the 1v1."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and W-charge into a committed Ornn, then Q3 to knock up and pull him for a guaranteed trade","Trade while Searing Charge (E) is on its 14s cooldown so he can't dash off or knock you into terrain","Use Path Maker's charge to soak his Q-into-E knock-up, the only real burst window he owns"],"foe":["Land Searing Charge (E) into his Volcanic Rupture pillar (Q) to knock you up against his own terrain","Make you Brittle with Bellows Breath (W) so his knock-up lands and his team's follow-up damage spikes","Stall the lane even, out-itemize you with his free upgrades, and win the 5v5 with double knockup R"]},"early":"Neither side does anything at Level 1 — you only have Q, he only has autos, so farm at the edge of Ntofo Strikes. The lane wakes up at 3 when your full kit is online: Path Maker (W) charges through his poke taking reduced damage, and the release stuns him if you pin him to a wall, then your second Q stack pulls him back in. Watch for Volcanic Rupture (Q) into Searing Charge (E) — that pillar-and-charge knock-up is his whole early trade; charge W through it and his one combo does nothing.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your window — you out-bully an immobile tank when you trade on his cooldowns. Bait Searing Charge (E); for the next 14 seconds he can't escape or knock you up, so step in, stun him with Path Maker, pull with your second Q, and bank the trade. At 6 don't over-respect All Out: it gives you a duelist 1v1 but peels off your tankiness, and Call of the Forge God is a 140s ultimate he can recast for a second knock-up, so save R as counter-engage rather than a solo-kill button. This is an even tank mirror you edge on the cooldown trades.","late":"Late game this flatlines — you both build full tank, neither of you kills the other, and armour stacking does nothing against an Ornn who exists to peel and CC. The fight is decided in the 5v5, not the lane: your R knocking his carry back through a wall against his R making your whole team Brittle. Make sure you are the one peeling for your carries, because if Forge God lands on your backline first, his free-upgrade itemised team wins the exchange. Close any small lead earlier — there's no scaling 1v1 here.","whys":["Neither of you has a Level 1 threat — you have only Q, he has only a brittle auto, so it's a pure farm standoff.","He picks up E or W and you pick up W or E, but neither combo is online yet, so the lane stays even and safe.","With your full kit you pin him with Path Maker's stun and pull with a second Q stack — his cooldowns can't answer an all-in.","You out-bully him while Searing Charge (E) is on its 14s cooldown — without that dash he has no escape.","All Out wins the duel but strips your bulk, and his Call of the Forge God can re-knockup you through it, so the 6 spike is a wash.","Both of you spike into tank durability and the lane neutralizes — neither first item gives a clean kill.","Full tank vs full tank, your armor does nothing to his CC and his does nothing to your peel, so it's a teamfight stalemate, not a 1v1."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"pantheon","win":["Skill","Pantheon","Pantheon","Skill","Skill","Pantheon","Pantheon"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Pantheon's point-click W stun into Q empowered spear is his cleanest all-in window before your combo exists — respect it and hug XP."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your combo comes online: charge Path Maker through his stun, knock him into terrain, then pull with a second Q."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet plus your bulk lets you walk through his fading poke — this is where you flip the lane and force side-fights."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R is a global roam threat, not a 1v1 win button — ping it and don't overstay, your All Out doesn't out-burst his combo here."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive levels 1-2 hugging XP, then hit your Lvl 3 Q-W combo to trade evenly","Charge Path Maker through Shield Vault, then stun him into terrain and pull","Get to your first tank item where his poke stops mattering and you out-bulk him"],"foe":["Win levels 1-2 with W point-click stun into empowered Q spear before your combo exists","Poke with Comet Spear, then Aegis Assault to block your damage from the front","Snowball his early lead or use global R to roam before you out-scale him"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 belong to Pantheon — Shield Vault is a point-click stun he can't miss on a 13s cooldown, and he chains it into an empowered Comet Spear. You have only Q at level 1 and no engage, so don't contest the wave aggressively; soak XP at melee range and accept the chip. From level 3 your full kit answers: Path Maker's charge cuts the damage, the release stuns him into a wall, and your second Q stack pulls him back. Bait Shield Vault before you commit.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are where you stabilize — you trade around his Q spear cooldown, and your bulk lets you bank the wave back without dying to his poke. Don't over-respect his level 6: All Out gives you a duelist profile but it strips your tankiness, and Pantheon's W-stun-into-combo can still out-burst you in that window, so R is for peel and side-skirmishes, not a blind 1v1. Watch for his global R roaming bot or mid — ping it the second he backs off.","late":"Once you hit your first tank item, Pantheon falls off a cliff and you take over — his early poke does nothing through your armor and HP, and Iceborn plus your W-charge let you walk him down and pull him into your team with R. This is a normal tank scaling pattern: his damage is front-loaded, yours compounds. Just don't let his early lead snowball so hard that he ends before you come online. Close on your mid-to-item windows.","whys":["He opens with a point-click Shield Vault stun into an empowered Comet Spear, and you have only Q with no way to answer the all-in yet.","You pick up W or E and become safer, but his W-stun trade still edges you before your combo is whole — soak XP and don't force it.","Your combo is online: charge W through his stun, wall-stun him, pull with a second Q — you finally trade back evenly.","You bank small leads trading around his Q spear cooldown, but his poke still chips you between your trades — it stays a coin-flip on cooldowns.","All Out strips your tankiness and his W-stun-into-combo can still out-burst you in that window, so it's a roam ping, not a free 1v1.","Your first tank item plus Iceborn lets you walk through his faded poke and force the all-in he can no longer answer.","He's outscaled but his front-loaded burst still punishes mistakes — it's even, decided by who banked the earlier lead, not by raw scaling."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"poppy","win":["Skill","Poppy","Poppy","Skill","Skill","Poppy","Poppy"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Poppy's passive shield-throw and W-block on your E mean she pokes you off the wave while you have only Q and no Path Maker safety yet."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once your Q-W combo is online you trade back, but her E pins you to a wall for a stun if you dash carelessly with your own E."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out flips the duel — your R range + duelist conversion lets you win the straight 1v1 before her items, your one clean kill window."},{"when":"1st item / Late","text":"Her Heartsteel + steadfast bulk and her R to cancel your engage reclaim the lane; she trades evenly and out-grinds your stacking armor."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 6 and use All Out to convert into your duelist profile and win the straight 1v1 before she items up","Land Path Maker's stun and your second-stack Q pull while her 20s W is down","Bank small leads at Levels 4-5 and force side-lane fights before her Heartsteel scaling kicks in"],"foe":["Use Steadfast Presence to stop your W, E and R dashes, grounding you where you stand","Pin you to a wall with Heroic Charge for the stun, then drop Hammer Shock and grind","Stack Heartsteel HP and trade evenly all lane, denying you any snowball window"]},"early":"Level 1 belongs to Poppy — you only have Q with no engage, and Iron Ambassador lets her throw a buckler, pick it up for a shield, and poke you off the wave. Don't step into Hammer Shock's slow zone for a stack you can't finish yet. By Levels 2-3 you get Path Maker and the full combo, so the lane levels out, but respect Steadfast Presence: it stops your W, E and R dashes outright and grounds you, and Heroic Charge pins you to a wall for a stun. Farm at the tip of Q and wait for your spike.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a grind — she trades evenly because her steadfast bulk eats your armour pressure and Heroic Charge answers your W charge. Don't dash in with E into her wall setups. Your real window is Level 6: All Out converts you out of tank stats into a duelist with bonus range and penetration, and that profile wins the straight 1v1. Bait Steadfast Presence with a throwaway Footwork dash — it is 20s at rank 1 — then R her and run it down. This is your one clean kill window before she items up.","late":"This is where Poppy reclaims it. Her Heartsteel stacking and steadfast HP grow faster than your armour matters, and her R counters your whole pattern — Steadfast Presence stops your engage dash and Keeper's Verdict flings your team away the moment you commit. But Verdict is a channel: hold Path Maker's stun or a Q stack for the wind-up and you cancel it outright. You still can't out-scale her bulk-for-bulk, so use your earlier-to-mid windows and first-item disruption to side-lane and close the game.","whys":["You have only Q and no engage threat, while her passive shield and poke let her win the level-1 last-hit war.","You pick up Path Maker so the lane evens out, but her W still blocks your only dash and her trade pattern matches yours.","Your full combo is online and the second Q stack pulls her in, but she trades evenly with Steadfast Presence bulk so neither commits.","She edges the 4-5 grind — her E pins you to a wall for a stun and her bulk shrugs off your stacking-armor pressure.","All Out converts you into a duelist with extra range and penetration and wins the straight 1v1 she can't escape — your one clean window.","Her Heartsteel and steadfast HP scale past your armor, and her W blocks the engage your first item is built around.","She out-grinds you late and her R cancels your R peel — W blocks your E in, ult flings your carry out, so your lockdown does nothing."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"quinn","win":["Quinn","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Quinn","K'Sante","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Quinn owns it — Blinding Assault plus Harrier poke chunks you while you have only Q and no way to close."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your combo comes online: a charged Path Maker takes reduced damage and stuns, your first real punish if she steps up while Vault is on its 12s."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out flips the duel — R's dash + range converts you to a duelist profile that can run her down once her E vault is on cooldown."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet + your tank durability is your peak: the IBG slow plus Q stacks pin her so her Harrier kite can't reset distance."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her Vault (E), then charge Path Maker through the gap and pull her into terrain with your Q","Build durability so her Harrier poke and E burst can't chunk you out of last-hits","Hit Level 6 and your first item, then collapse with R before she out-roams the lane"],"foe":["Vault away the instant you charge W, then blind your follow-up autos with Q","Kite with Harrier move speed and poke you below trading thresholds between cooldowns","Roam with her speed to snowball other lanes while you're stuck farming"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are hers — Blinding Assault blanks your autos from 1025 range and Vault leaps her back out, while Harrier procs poke you and you have no way to close. Don't step up for a Q stack you can't finish; she just Vaults off and resets with move speed. Last-hit at max Q range, eat the poke, and wait for Level 3. Once your combo is online you have an answer: Path Maker's charge cuts the damage and stuns her if you read the vault.","mid":"This is where the lane turns. Bait her E vault — the moment she blows it to disengage, you've got a window with no escape on her: charge W to stun her against a wall and Q3 to pull her in. At 6, All Out is your kill button: it gives you the range and dash to catch her after the vault is down, and the duelist stats burst her before Harrier can kite you. Track her roams; if she leaves, take plates and ping the map.","late":"With your first item you're durable enough that her poke and Vault burst stop mattering — Iceborn's slow plus your Q stacks glue her in place so she can't kite. From 2+ items you're a teamfight monster: she's a squishy roamer with no escape once you commit, and All Out knocks her back through a wall into your team. She has no percent-HP or true damage to punish your armour, so unlike Vayne or Fiora she never reclaims this — just don't facecheck her roams.","whys":["Quinn owns Level 1: Blinding Assault blanks your autos and Harrier poke chunks you while you have only Q and no way to answer.","Even at Level 2 — you pick up W or E and get safer, but she still kites your single-target Q with Harrier move speed.","Skill: your full Q-W combo is online, but landing charged W through her E vault is a read — guess right and you punish, guess wrong and she resets.","Levels 4-5 swing to you: this is your tank lane-control peak where your bulk eats her poke and you trade around her E cooldown.","All Out's dash and bonus range let you run her down once her E vault is spent — the duelist profile bursts her before she kites away.","Iceborn Gauntlet's slow plus your Q stacks and tank durability pin her Harrier kite so she can't poke you safely anymore.","From 2+ items you're a peel/teamfight monster and she has no percent-HP or true damage to punish your armor — she never reclaims this lane."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"renekton","win":["Skill","Renekton","Renekton","Skill","Skill","Renekton","Renekton"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Renekton's W stun into a fury-empowered Q is his hardest point-click window — you only have Q and no engage, so don't contest his last hits in melee."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full combo comes online: bait Slice and Dice (E), charge Path Maker through the trade, then pull with a second Q."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out turns the duel — but his empowered W destroys your Footwork shield, so fight once the fury bar is spent, never into it."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Renekton falls off a cliff into items while your tank-into-duelist scaling and R peel only grow — this is where you reclaim the lane and the map."}],"wants":{"you":["Concede levels 1-2 and farm safely until your Q-W combo is online at 3","Bait his 16s W stun, then charge Path Maker into the gap and pull him with your second Q stack","Drag the game past his item fall-off where your scaling and R peel take over"],"foe":["Hit level 2 first and W-stun you off CS for an early fury-empowered all-in","Snowball levels 1-5 with point-click Q damage before you out-scale","Burn his lead into towers and sidelane pressure before items neuter him"]},"early":"Renekton owns the first two levels outright — he has a point-click W stun and a fury-empowered Q while you have only Ntofo Strikes and no engage at level 1, so don't walk into melee range to last-hit or he'll stun you and dump the combo. Soak XP from the tip of Q and give up a little CS. From level 3 your full combo flips it: charge Path Maker to cut the damage of his all-in, stun him back, and pull with your second Q stack. His W is 16s at rank 1 — that gap is your trade.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a knife-fight around fury. When he dashes in with Slice and Dice expecting a free stun, start charging Path Maker — the charge cuts the damage and the release knocks him into a wall, then your second Q stack pulls him back for a trade your bulk wins. At 6, All Out survives his fading burst and out-damages a Renekton who has spent his fury. Never commit into a full rage bar: empowered Ruthless Predator stuns 1.5s and destroys your Footwork shield outright. Ult after his empower is gone.","late":"This is all yours. Renekton has no sustained threat once his early fury combos are survived, and he falls off hard into items while your armor stacking, first tank piece, and R peel only get stronger. Don't let him cash his early lead into a sidelane snowball before then — match his waves, and in teamfights save All Out to dash through and recall his carry out, not to fight him. If he didn't kill you in the first six levels, he can't.","whys":["You have only Q and no engage at level 1 while Renekton is a point-click bully — concede the level and farm from max Q range.","He spikes hard at 2 with W stun into a fury-empowered Q combo; you don't get a real trading tool until 3, so don't contest CS in melee.","Your full kit arrives — Path Maker's charge cuts his burst, then a second Q stack pulls him in and neutralises his dominance.","You trade around his fury bar: bait the 16s W stun, step in after it, pull with Q, and your bulk wins the exchange.","All Out beats a Renekton whose fury is spent — but it strips resists, so commit only once his empowered W is gone.","Your first tank-engage item makes you durable and disruptive while his point-click damage is starting to fall off — slight edge to you.","Renekton has no sustained threat and falls off hard into items, while your armor stacking and R peel reclaim the matchup outright."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"riven","win":["Riven","Riven","Skill","Riven","K'Sante","Skill","Riven"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Riven's first Q dash and W stun give her a 2-spell all-in before your Q-W combo exists — she can chunk you off cooldown and you have no answer but to farm."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your combo comes online: bait the third Broken Wings cast, then charge W through the trade and pull her with a second Q."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is your one clean window — pop R to survive her full Q-E-W-AA burst combo, then duel her down as a temporary skirmisher before her items scale."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Riven's Conqueror plus first-item spike out-damages your tank stats; her three Q dashes kite your short W and R, and she sidesteps to reset, reclaiming the lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive her combo behind Path Maker's damage-reduction charge, then stun and pull her in to flip the trade","Reach Level 6 and pop R All Out to win the one duel where you out-survive her burst","Bank cs safely at Levels 1-2, accept poke, and avoid feeding her Q-W all-in before your combo exists"],"foe":["Use her three Q dashes and E shield-dash to sidestep your short Q3 and W wall-smash entirely","All-in inside her Q-E-W combo window before your W charge or R is up","Snowball the early lead and scale into a first-item duel that ignores your armor stacking"]},"early":"Riven owns the first two levels: her Broken Wings triple-cast and Ki Burst stun give her a real all-in before you have anything but Q, so don't walk up to last-hit into her combo range — take cs with the edge of Q and eat a little poke. The lane equalizes at 3 when your full kit is online. The trick is patience: bait out her Q dashes and her 10s E shield, because once those are down she has no mobility, and that is when you charge W in and pull with a second Q stack.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are hers — she trades around your W cooldown and her 10s E shield resets faster than your bulk can punish, so play around cs and don't over-extend without W up. At 6 the lane flips to you for one window: All Out converts you to a duelist and lets you survive her burst, so charge W for the damage reduction, R her through a wall away from her dashes, and duel her down before she back-times into items. Track when her E is down — that's your only opening to commit.","late":"This is where she reclaims it. Riven's first-item spike with Conqueror out-damages your tank stats, and her three Q dashes plus E let her sidestep your short W wall-smash and R completely, then reset the combo on you. Her ultimate is 60s at rank 3 against your 80s, so she gets a Wind Slash cycle you cannot answer. You don't win the straight 1v1 once she has items — armour does nothing against flat-AD burst. Peel her off your carries with All Out instead of duelling her solo.","whys":["Riven has a 2-spell Q-dash and W-stun all-in at Level 1-2 while you have only Q and no engage — she chunks you off cooldown.","Her W stun plus Q dashes still beat your kit before your combo exists; just farm the edge of Q and concede the level.","At 3 your kit is online — bait her Q dashes and E, then charge W and pull her with a second Q to even the trade.","Levels 4-5 are hers: her E shield resets faster than your bulk can punish and she trades around your W cooldown.","All Out lets you survive her Q-E-W burst and turn duelist — R her through a wall, then charge W and win the one clean 1v1.","Her first-item Conqueror spike and your fading bulk roughly cancel — she sidesteps your short W with dashes, you trade off her shield timing.","Her items out-scale you: flat-AD burst ignores your armor stacking and three Q dashes kite your W and R, so peel with R instead of dueling."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"rumble","win":["Skill","Rumble","Rumble","Skill","Skill","Rumble","Rumble"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full combo comes online — charge Path Maker into a committed Rumble, stun him, then pull with a second Q while Flamespitter is down."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your lane-control peak: trade around his Flamespitter cooldown with your Path Maker damage resistance and bank small leads before he overheats reliably."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is a coin flip here — it gives you a duelist 1v1 but strips your bulk, so only commit R when his Equalizer and Flamespitter heat are down."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Rumble's takeover: full-build AP DPS and Equalizer zoning out-burn your armor stacking, which does nothing against his magic damage — close before this."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3, charge Path Maker through Flamespitter, then stun and pull a committed Rumble","Trade in the Level 4-5 window around his Flamespitter cooldown where your Path Maker damage resist eats his DPS","Bait his E harpoon slow and his Equalizer placement, then all-in on R while his overheat and ult are down"],"foe":["Chip you with Danger Zone Flamespitter in extended melee while you're stuck in Q range","Land E harpoon to slow you out of your short W and Q range and kite your cooldown-reliant pattern","Drop Equalizer to zone your wave and scale to 2+ items where his magic DPS ignores your armor"]},"early":"Rumble has no mana, so Flamespitter is always available to chip you at level 1 — farm and don't stand in the cone for free. His early DPS still can't out-trade your bulk if you pick the window. By level 3 you have the full kit: charge Path Maker for the damage reduction, push through the burn, stun him on the release, and pull him back with your second Q stack. Watch his heat bar — at 100% he Overheats and cannot cast at all, and that is the window you commit into.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your window. Trade around Flamespitter's 10s cooldown: charge Path Maker to blunt the burn, pull him in with your second Q, and let your tank stats bank a small lead. Dodge Electro Harpoon — he carries two charges at 850 range and each one shreds your magic resist as well as slowing you out of your own reach. At 6 it's a genuine coin flip: All Out gives you the 1v1 but strips your resists right when The Equalizer can melt a squishier you, so ult only once his R is spent.","late":"This is where Rumble takes it back. Armour stacking does literally nothing against his magic damage, and every Electro Harpoon shreds the magic resist you did buy, so a full-build Rumble out-burns you the second your windows close. Don't bet on the very late 1v1 — he scales against your profile. Bank your Level 3-to-first-item leads, then pivot to teamfights where your R peels his carries and Path Maker's charge soaks the Equalizer line, instead of solo-duelling a champion your defences are blank against.","whys":["Rumble's Flamespitter has no mana cost so he chips you at level 1, but his early DPS can't out-trade your tank bulk — just farm and pick your window.","He picks up his W shield and move speed, but you get W or E to become safer too — neither of you has a real all-in yet, so it's even.","Your full combo is online — Path Maker's charge eats the Flamespitter burn and its release stuns, then a second Q stack pulls a committed Rumble in.","Your lane-control peak: you trade around his Flamespitter cooldown and your Path Maker bulk banks small leads against his melee-range DPS.","All Out gives you a duelist 1v1 but strips your tankiness right as his Equalizer can melt you — it's a coin flip on whether his heat and ult are down.","Your first tank-engage item makes you durable and disruptive, but his first AP item lets his overheat burn keep pace — roughly even forcing side fights.","Full-build Rumble's magic DPS and Equalizer zoning ignore your armor stacking entirely — he out-scales your profile, so close earlier or pivot to peeling in teamfights."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"ryze","win":["Skill","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Full Q-W combo online — W a committed Ryze and Q3 knock-up to punish him while Rune Prison sits on its 11s cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out converts your tank stats to a duelist profile and dashes through him — you survive his Flux-into-Rune Prison root and run him down before Realm Warp escapes."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet + your Q slow lock him in melee range where his 615-range Flux-root combo can't kite you out."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Ryze's threat window — Archangel's-stacked spell spam and realm warp turn lane pressure into a raid-boss; your armor does nothing into his AP."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and W a committed Ryze into your Q3 knock-up before his root resets chain","Use Path Maker's damage-reduced charge to eat his Flux-root burst, then All Out him on the spot","Close the lane on your first-item durability before his Archangel's stacks turn him into a raid-boss"],"foe":["Land Spell Flux then Rune Prison to root you, then kite you with Overload resets","Stack Tear/Archangel's and farm safely until his 2+ item spell spam outdamages your tank stats","Use Realm Warp (R) to escape your All Out dash or roam when you over-commit"]},"early":"Ryze has no real Level 1 damage threat and no escape but Flash, so don't panic at his 1000-range Overload poke — just farm with the tip of your Q (Ntofo Strikes) and stack your passive marks. The danger is the root: Spell Flux (E) first, then Rune Prison (W) roots instead of slowing, so don't stand in his 615 range with your W on cooldown. Once you hit Level 3 your full Q-W is online and the lane flips — he's squishy and immobile.","mid":"This is your window. Path Maker (W) charges through his Flux-root burst taking reduced damage, then knocks back and stuns him if you pin him to a wall — and his only answer is to blow his root and pray. At 6, R throws him through the wall and All Out dashes after him; you survive his combo and chunk him before he can realm-warp out. Force every all-in here while his single 10s root is his whole defense and your bulk plus first-item Iceborn keeps him pinned in melee.","late":"Ryze is a hard scaler and this is where he reclaims it — once his Tear stacks into Archangel's and he has 2+ items, his Q-E spell spam outdamages everything your armor stacking gives you, because none of it touches his AP. Don't try to 1v1 a fed Ryze in the open; your job becomes peeling. Use R to launch him through a wall away from your carry, and lean on the lead you should have built before ~25 minutes — if the game goes long on his terms, his Realm Warp and reset chains win.","whys":["Ryze has no Level 1 burst, but neither do you with only Q — farm marks and respect his E-into-W root if you over-extend.","You pick up W or E and become safe; his single root can't punish a tank who can charge through it.","Your full Q-W combo lands — W an over-committed Ryze and Q3 knock-up him before his reset chain comes back.","You out-trade a pre-item Ryze: Path Maker eats his Overload-Flux burst and your bulk shrugs his poke.","R launches him through the wall and All Out dashes after — you eat Rune Prison (11s) and kill him before Realm Warp.","Iceborn Gauntlet plus your Q slow pins him in melee where his short-range root combo can't kite you out.","He out-scales hard: Archangel's-stacked spell spam ignores your armor entirely — peel with All Out's recall, don't 1v1 him."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"sejuani","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","K'Sante","Sejuani"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo is online — W into a committed Sejuani and Q3 pull for the only clean burst in this slow tank mirror."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your lane-control peak: bank leads while Permafrost has no Frost stacks to fire on and she has no reset to punish you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out duels her but strips your tank stats — only commit if you can avoid her R Glacial Prison flip mid-dash."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Fury of the North's resists and her 1300-range Glacial Prison out-utility you — she brings AoE lockdown where your R only peels one target."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and W a committed Sejuani into Q3 for the only real burst window in the mirror","Trade at 4-5 before Winter's Wrath stacks Frost — you have a reset and she does not","Build small CS and plate leads early since neither tank kills the other outright"],"foe":["Land Arctic Assault (Q) knockup into a Permafrost (E) stun to hold you for a gank","Stack Frost with Winter's Wrath so Permafrost can stun you on demand","Scale to teamfights where her R Glacial Prison flip out-utilities your single-target R peel"]},"early":"Two slow tanks poking — neither of you dies at Level 1, so just farm and respect Frost Armor: out of combat it hands her resists and slow immunity, so your Q slow does nothing until you break it. Once you hit Level 3 you have the only real combo: W into her when she commits to a trade, then Q3 to pull her in. Her escape is Arctic Assault (Q), down 18 seconds at rank 1, so a clean W stun into a wall is your best early lead. Do not waste W on that dash — bait it first.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your peak: Permafrost only stuns once Winter's Wrath has stacked Frost on you, and unlike her you have E Footwork as a reset to disengage and reposition. Bank plates and small CS leads here because neither of you can outright kill the other. At 6, All Out gives you a duelist 1v1, but it strips your tankiness right as her R Glacial Prison can flip you mid-dash — only ult-commit when her R is down, or you trade your bulk for nothing.","late":"This is where she edges you. Winter's Wrath comes back every 5 seconds at rank 5 and Fury of the North keeps handing her free resists, so your armor stacking buys less against her than against a normal bruiser. In teamfights her R Glacial Prison is a 1300-range AOE flip while your R only peels one target — she brings more lockdown to a 5v5. Close the game on your mid-game side-lane pressure; do not bet on out-scaling a fellow tank.","whys":["Both of you are tanks at Level 1 with no kill threat — Frost Armor makes her immune to your Q slow until you damage it off.","Your W or E unlocks first and makes you safer; you get a combo piece while she still only has poke and her E.","Full Q-W online: you W a committed Sejuani and Q3 pull her in — bait Arctic Assault first, it is down 18s.","Your lane-control peak — Permafrost only stuns at max Frost stacks, so trade before her W has stacked you.","All Out duels her but strips your bulk into her R Glacial Prison flip, so the window is genuinely even — only commit with her R down.","Your first tank item is durable but Winter's Wrath re-stacks Frost every 7s, so neither side spikes clearly here.","Frost Armor's free resists and her 1300-range Glacial Prison out-scale you: she brings AoE lockdown where your R peels one target."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"sett","win":["Sett","Sett","Sett","Skill","Skill","Sett","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Sett owns the early grit: his passive double-punch and W true-damage smash out-trade you before your Q-W combo is online, so just farm and don't auto-walk into his haymakers."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W comes up but Facebreaker into a charged Haymaker still wins the stat-check — and his W shield eats whatever burst you answer with, so bait it out before you commit Q3."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"The Show Stopper vs your All Out: a coinflip on who commits first — his R grounds you, so Path Maker, Footwork and the All Out dash are all shut off if he lands it before you charge W."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"This is your window: with tank items stacked you survive his stored Haymaker and R, then peel with Footwork and the R wall-knockback — Sett's grit trades fall off and you out-last him."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach 2+ tank items where you survive his stored W smash and R suppress, then out-sustain his grit","Use W's damage-reduced charge to soak his Facebreaker into Haymaker instead of eating it raw","Bank farm safely early and bait his W stacks empty before you commit your Q3 knock-up"],"foe":["Land E grab-stun into a fully-stored W true-damage smash before your W unstoppable is up","Win the early grit trades with passive double-punch while you lack your Q-W combo","All-in at 6 with The Show Stopper, grounding you so none of your three dashes work"]},"early":"Sett owns the first three levels outright — his passive double-punch and his W, which stores the damage you deal him and fires it back as a true-damage smash plus a shield, beat your Q-W combo before it's even online at Level 3. Don't feed his W by trading into it; last-hit at the edge of your Q cleave and accept some chip. The trap is Facebreaker: if he yanks you in while his W is charged, you eat the smash with no answer until your own W charge is back up. Just farm and survive — this lane is about reaching your items, not the slap-fight.","mid":"Levels 4-6 even out into a skill matchup. Your W Path Maker is the key: the charge takes reduced damage, so it soaks his Facebreaker into Haymaker, and you knock him back and Q3 to lock him. But mistime it and his combo still kills you, so the trade is a read on who commits first. At 6 your All Out gives you a real 1v1, but The Show Stopper grounds you — W, E and the All Out dash all go dead — so don't ult into a fresh E-W with his Grit full.","late":"This is where you reclaim the lane. By 2+ tank items his stored Haymaker and his slam stop one-shotting you, and your sustained tank DPS plus the Footwork disengage let you out-last every grit trade he picks. Sett has no scaling answer to a healthy tank — he's an early-game bully whose true damage and all-in lose value the bulkier you get. Drag the game past your second item, then win teamfights by W-ing onto his carry or launching him off yours.","whys":["Knuckle Down's max-health punches and Haymaker's stored true damage out-trade you at 1, when you have only Q and no engage.","He still owns Level 2 — his W true-damage smash and grit beat you before your Q-W combo comes online.","Even with your full Q3 pull at 3, Facebreaker (16s) into a charged Haymaker wins the stat-check trade.","Levels 4-5 are a coinflip — W's charge soaks his stored Haymaker, but mistime it and his combo still kills you.","At 6 it's even: All Out gives a 1v1 but strips your bulk when The Show Stopper grounds you and kills your dashes.","With his first item Sett's grit and stored W smash still out-trade your single-item tank profile before your bulk piles up.","By 2+ items you survive Haymaker and his R, out-sustain his trades, and peel with Footwork and your wall-knockback."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"shen","win":["Skill","Shen","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Shen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once your Q-W combo is online you W a committed Shen into Q3's knockup-pull — your first real punish window before his taunt CDs are reliable."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out converts your tank stats into a duelist profile and dashes through him; on his taunt cooldown you win the straight 1v1 and can R-recast to peel."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With your first tank-engage piece (Iceborn) you out-durable a pre-item Shen and force side-lane fights where his global R does nothing for the duel."},{"when":"Mid-Late","text":"Shen's biggest threat isn't the duel — it's his global R saving a fed teammate; the one answer is CC on him mid-channel, so hold your W stun for that cast."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q3's pull on a Shen who used Shadow Dash aggressively, then W-stun him into the wall","Hit Level 6 and All Out him on his taunt cooldown so your duelist profile wins the 1v1","Force side-lane all-ins at your first item so his global R is spent saving someone else, not him"],"foe":["Block your Q3 and AA strings with W (Spirit's Refuge) so your Passive marks deal nothing","Land E taunt mid-W so your charge finishes facing nothing and you walk into his spirit blade","Stay even in lane and scale, then swing the map with global R to a winning teammate"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — you only have Q and no engage, and Shen is a slow tank with just his Q empower, so you both farm. The thing to respect is his W, Spirit's Refuge: while it is up it blocks attacks, not abilities, so your spells still land but your Passive-marked auto hits nothing — keep casting through the zone and hold the auto. His E taunt is his only real threat early, and at 18 seconds a missed or traded Shadow Dash hands you a clean window to step up. Last-hit, stack Q marks, and wait for Level 3.","mid":"This is your lane-control peak. With the full Q-W combo you bait his E taunt, and the moment it is on cooldown you W a committed Shen, charging through his damage, then Q3 him for the pull — Shadow Dash is his only escape from your range. Your sustained tank DPS off Passive move-speed stacks beats his trade unless Spirit's Refuge (16s) is up blocking your autos, so time your all-ins around his W and taunt windows. At 6 your All Out is the real spike: it sheds bulk for a duelist profile and dashes through him, and on his taunt cooldown you win that straight 1v1 outright.","late":"Honest truth: the lane is even and Shen makes his money off the map, not the duel. You out-bulk and out-trade him in a pure 1v1 at most points, but his global R can shield a fed teammate and win a fight you are not even in. There is one answer: Stand United is a channel, so a Q pull or a W stun on him cancels it outright — hold one for the moment he starts casting. Close on your earlier windows — bank a side-lane lead at first item and group with R as a peeler before his global picks the map apart.","whys":["Level 1 you have only Q and no engage, and Shen is an immobile tank with just his Q empower — neither of you can commit, so you both just farm.","At 2 Shen's E taunt and W block give him a safer kit than your half-combo; his W can shut off your Passive marks before your Q3 is online.","With the full Q-W combo up you W a committed Shen and Q3 him into the pull — Shadow Dash is his only exit and it is down 18s at rank 1.","These are your tank lane-control levels: you bait his E taunt, trade on its cooldown, and your Passive move-speed DPS out-sustains his Q empower.","All Out converts your stats to a duelist and dashes through him — on his taunt cooldown you win the straight 1v1, your last clean solo-kill window.","Your first tank-engage item out-durables a pre-item Shen and forces side-lane fights, but his W block keeps the even lane honest — it is a coin-flip, not a stomp.","Two items in, Shen's global R swings fights across the map that your armor stacking can't touch — he out-scales you in teamfight impact, not in the duel."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"singed","win":["Skill","Singed","Singed","Singed","Skill","Singed","Singed"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Best window to land Q3's pull before he buys boots and starts proxying out of your range entirely."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"R launches him through a wall into All Out — your only real catch, though his R's Grievous Wounds halves your healing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Singed's Rylai's + boots make his fling-and-kite untouchable, and he proxies your wave so you fall behind in farm."},{"when":"Late","text":"He runs your team down with Fling (E) and poison, and Insanity Potion's Grievous Wounds cuts All Out's healing while your armor does nothing."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q3's knockup-and-pull while he is still in your range before he out-speeds you","Use W's wall-stun to pin him against terrain, the one CC his move speed cannot shrug","Catch him with R's wall-launch into All Out when he dives your backline"],"foe":["Build move speed and proxy your wave so you can never trade him","Fling you (E) into Mega Adhesive, grounding you so no dash gets you out","Scale as a drain-tank and become an uncatchable splitpush and dive threat"]},"early":"Singed barely contests Level 1, so this is your one even window, but you have to land Q3's pull while he is still standing in your range. The second he gets boots and his poison trail going, he starts proxying behind your tower and your short Q and W can never reach him. Never stand in Mega Adhesive (W): it grounds, so Path Maker, Footwork and All Out all stop working, and Fling (E) exists to put you exactly there. Farm safely and accept you cannot pin him down once he is rolling.","mid":"By Levels 4-6 Singed is a proxy machine, and your W stun is the only CC he cannot simply out-speed, so position to knock him into your tower or terrain when he overstays on your wave. At 6 your R launches him through a wall into All Out, but it strips your tank stats and Insanity Potion's Grievous Wounds halves the healing All Out gives back. The real trap is Mega Adhesive: stand in the glue and your W, E and All Out dashes are all grounded, so step out of it before you commit. If he farms your wave from behind your tower, play for cross-map pressure instead.","late":"This is where the lane is genuinely lost on a straight 1v1. Singed is a drain-tank whose Insanity Potion puts Grievous Wounds on your All Out healing, and your armor stacking means nothing against a champ whose gameplan is move speed and sustain. He flings your carries with E and runs your entire team down, and a single CC like your Q3 or W never catches him. Group with your team, use R purely to peel his flips off your backline, and let numbers solve what your lockdown never will.","whys":["Singed concedes Level 1 with no real threat and so do you, so it is even — last-hit and look for an early Q3 before he gets rolling.","Once he has boots and starts his poison trail he out-speeds your short Q and W and begins proxying out of reach.","His move speed plus Fling (E, 10s) means he kites every trade you try and your full Q-W combo cannot land.","He proxies your wave behind tower where your Q3 and W stun simply cannot reach, and you bleed farm and tempo.","R launches him through the wall into All Out — a duelist 1v1 and the one tool that catches him, so this is your even window.","His Rylai's plus boots make his fling-and-kite untouchable, and proxying your wave snowballs his lead while you fall behind.","Insanity Potion's Grievous Wounds guts All Out's healing while he runs your team down; armor does nothing to a move-speed sustain champ."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"sion","win":["Sion","Sion","Skill","Skill","K'Sante","Skill","Sion"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Roar of the Slayer pokes from 800 range and shreds your armour while your Q-W combo is still offline — his cleanest early window."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo arrives — W a committed Sion and Q3 to knock him up; this is your first window to trade back into his poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out converts you to a duelist, and a fully-charged Decimating Smash is slow enough to walk out of, giving you a clean 1v1 over an immobile target."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Glory in Death heals him off max-health attacks and Soul Furnace grows on kills — buy Grievous Wounds, not more armour, or he wins every extended tank fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive his E poke to Level 3, then W a committed Sion and Q3 to land your knock-up trade","Use Level 6 All Out to dash through his charged Q and win the one clean duelist 1v1","Punish him while he is charging Decimating Smash — the charge pins him in place for your combo"],"foe":["Poke you with Roar of the Slayer from 800 range, shredding your armour","Land a fully-charged Q knockup to chain into his W AOE and a kill setup","Drag it to a tank war his max-health damage and Glory in Death healing win"]},"early":"Sion owns the first two levels here — Roar of the Slayer pokes from 800 range and shreds your armour while you have no engage at Level 1 with only Q, so just farm and eat a little chip. Do NOT walk in to throw a single Q stack into that poke; you lose the exchange every time. The lane turns at Level 3 when your full Q-W combo comes online: if he steps up or starts charging a Q, W into him and Q3 to pull him back into your range.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a genuine coinflip tank standoff — you trade around his charged Q and his W shield, banking small leads with your bulk, but he out-pokes you with E so don't over-extend on his wave. Level 6 is your window: All Out strips your tankiness, but a fully-charged Decimating Smash is slow and telegraphed, and against an immobile Sion you get a clean duelist 1v1 he can't escape. Bait the charge, then commit — and count 3 seconds off his Soul Furnace shield, because that is when the reactivate detonates.","late":"This is where the lane slips away. Sion scales on raw HP, and both Glory in Death and Soul Furnace deal max-health damage, so armour is the wrong answer and Grievous Wounds is the right one. Two items deep he out-bulks you, out-utilities you in teamfights with his charged Q engage, and refuses to die. Your R lets you peel a carry, but in a straight tank-vs-tank attrition fight he wins. Close on your Level 3-and-6 windows; do not bet on out-scaling him late.","whys":["Roar of the Slayer shreds your armour from 800 range and you have no engage with only Q — you concede the level and farm.","He keeps poking with E from range while your Q-W combo is still offline; you can't punish him yet.","Your full Q-W combo arrives — you can W a committed Sion to eat his knockup and Q3 him back, evening the trade.","It's a tank standoff: you trade around his charged Q and W shield, but his E poke keeps it a coinflip, not a win.","Decimating Smash telegraphs its full charge, so you step out of it and an immobile Sion cannot escape your 1v1 — your one clear spike.","Your first tank-engage item makes you durable and disruptive, but his HP scaling and E poke keep the lane even.","Glory in Death and Soul Furnace both hit for max health and heal him, so armour is the wrong buy — bring Grievous Wounds or he out-lasts you."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"swain","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","K'Sante","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo is online — clear Nevermove's return so the root whiffs, then W in, Q3-pull, and walk him down."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out trades your tankiness for a duelist profile — strong, but it makes you eat his W bomb and R drain harder, so only ult to peel/dash out, not to facetank his combo."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet keeps you sticky and bulky — you survive his rooted combo and chunk him every time he steps up to Q."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two-item Swain in a teamfight is his peak — Demonic Ascension drains your whole team and Ravenous Flock banks it as permanent health, so bring Grievous Wounds."}],"wants":{"you":["Hold W (Path Maker) for his E pull — unstoppable means the root whiffs and you keep marching in","Reach Level 3 and Q3 knock-up him after closing the gap his slows can't stop","Build Iceborn first so you stay sticky and bulky through his bomb and drain poke"],"foe":["Root you with Nevermove's return so his W bomb and Q line connect free","Poke you down with Q and W before you close, banking soul stacks on his passive","Drag the lane into a long AOE drain fight where his R out-sustains your trades"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — he pokes with Q and you just farm with Q tip, eating a little chip you can shrug off as a tank. The key from Level 2 onward is reading Nevermove: the wave only roots on the way BACK, so walk through the outgoing cast and be out of the return line. Don't blow E (Footwork) to dodge his bomb early; save it to close the gap his slows leave on you, then Q3 to pull him in.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your peak. He has no dash and no escape, so once you W into him and Q3-pull, he's stuck eating your full combo and you out-trade his poke as a tank. At 6 be careful with All Out — it strips your bulk, and his W bomb plus R drain punish a squishier you, so ult to dash through and peel out, not to stand and facetank his AOE. Bait Nevermove's return, then commit while it is down 12 seconds.","late":"This is the window Swain wants. A two-item drain mage heals off your whole team with Demonic Ascension, and Ravenous Flock turns those Soul Fragments into permanent max health, so Grievous Wounds is not optional. You're still a strong peeler — R launches him off your carry — but don't let him start a sustained teamfight on his terms. Use your mid-game lead and your W to lock him down before the drain out-paces you.","whys":["Level 1 he only has Q poke and you only have Q — you both just farm, so it's a wash you can tank either way.","At 2 you pick up W or E; Nevermove only roots on its return pass, so step in and clear the second hit.","Full Q-W combo online — sidestep Nevermove's return, then W and Q3-pull him; Swain has no dash to leave with.","Your tank lane-control peak: you out-trade his Q/W poke and bank leads since his slows can't keep you off him.","All Out wins many 1v1s but strips your bulk, so against his W bomb and R drain it's a double-edged spike, not a free win.","Iceborn Gauntlet keeps you sticky and durable — you survive his rooted combo and punish every Q step-up.","Two-item Swain reclaims it: Demonic Ascension drains straight through your trades unless Grievous Wounds is already on him."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"sylas","win":["Skill","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Sylas"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online — W him the moment Abscond commits, then Q3-pull before Kingslayer heals the trade back."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Lane-control peak: trade on his Abscond cooldown (13s at rank 1) with your bulk and bank leads while he is squishy."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Danger window — Hijack steals YOUR All Out and comes back in 80s at rank 1, so hold your ultimate until you have watched him spend his."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Sylas hits his AP bruiser scaling and Kingslayer out-heals your tank damage — buy Grievous Wounds or close before this."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and W him as Abscond commits, then Q3-pull a Sylas with no dash left","Trade around his E and Q cooldowns at 4-5 while your bulk eats his AP poke","Bank an early lead and avoid ulting when his R can steal your All Out"],"foe":["Chain to you with the Abduct recast, then Q-W to heal the whole trade back","Steal your All Out with R at 6 and turn your own duelist shred on you","Sustain through lane with Q-W heal and scale into his AP bruiser item spike"]},"early":"Sylas wants to Abscond in, chain to you with the Abduct recast and drain with Q-W to heal off the trade — but at Levels 1-2 he is squishy and that dash is his only safety. Farm with Q range and don't trade into his full mana. Once you hit Level 3 you flip it: W him the instant he commits the dash, then Q3 to pull an immobile Sylas who has already spent his escape.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are yours — your bulk eats his AP poke and you out-trade him around Abscond (13s) and Kingslayer, banking small leads before he can scale. At 6 respect his R: Hijack STEALS your All Out, so if you ult into him he gains your own duelist shred and burst back. Force trades when his E is down, but keep your ultimate pocketed until his R has been spent.","late":"This is where Sylas reclaims it. Kingslayer out-sustains your tank damage and his AP bruiser items mean he heals through everything your armour stacking cannot stop, so Grievous Wounds is the only real answer. You are a teamfight peeler now, not a duelist — launch him off your carries with R rather than 1v1ing him, and lean on the side-lane lead you banked at 3-5.","whys":["Sylas has only E for safety at level 1 and you have just Q — neither threatens, so farm and set up.","He picks up his W drain or second E charge and can poke-heal, but you are equally safe with W or E — even skirmish.","Your full Q-W combo lands: W the moment he commits Abscond, then Q3-pull a Sylas who has already spent his only dash.","Your bulk out-trades a squishy pre-item Sylas around his E and Q-W cooldowns — bank leads here.","His R steals your All Out, neutralizing your 6 spike — even window, don't ult into a stolen-ult threat.","Your first tank-engage item keeps you durable, but his AP item lets his Q-W drain start matching your damage.","Kingslayer's healing beats your tank damage without Grievous Wounds — peel with R, don't duel him late."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"tahmkench","win":["Skill","Tahm Kench","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once your Q-W combo is online you W a Tahm who steps up to Tongue Lash and Q3-pull him for a real trade, before Thick Skin converts it to a shield."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out converts you to a duelist and runs down a slow, low-mobility Tahm — your single best 1v1 window, and it lands before his sustain items arrive."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Tahm's threat peak: with his first tank item Devour and a three-stack Tongue Lash stun set up the kill, and Iceborn alone cannot out-damage Thick Skin's shield."},{"when":"Late","text":"An Acquired Taste turns his health into damage and Thick Skin out-lasts your armour, while Devour on an ally saves the fights you cannot reach."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his Q tongue, then W-charge into Q3 to land a knockup trade his grey-health can't fully heal","Hit Level 6 and use All Out to run his slow body down for a clean duelist kill before items","Use E Footwork to a minion to break the Tongue Lash line and deny his third stack"],"foe":["Stack An Acquired Taste to three, then Tongue Lash for the stun","Soak your Q-W trades into Thick Skin and cash them as a shield on the recommit","Reach the tank items where his health-scaling damage and Devour saves out-scale you"]},"early":"Tahm Kench's whole early threat is Tongue Lash — 900 range, it heals him and stacks An Acquired Taste, and only the third stack stuns, so count his hits. Keep E Footwork ready to dash to a minion and break the lash line. At Level 1 you only have Q with no engage, so just farm outside tongue range. The catch: Thick Skin banks the chip your Q poke deals and cashes it as a shield, so you are not winning a poke war — wait for the Level 3 combo and take one real trade.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are your lane-control window. With Q-W online you bait Tongue Lash, then W an overcommitted Tahm for the knockback-stun and Q3-pull him, doing real damage before Thick Skin converts it — this is where you bank small leads as a tank. At 6, All Out is your best shot: it strips your bulk but turns you into a duelist who runs his slow body down, since Abyssal Dive is 21 seconds and it is his only exit. Don't commit into a full Thick Skin bar — force the shield out first, then go.","late":"This is where Tahm reclaims it and the 47.5% shows. His W devour does percent-HP and his grey-health passive out-lasts every bit of damage my armor-stacked tank profile can output, so my late-game scaling does nothing against him — I can't burst through regen and I can't out-sustain a drain tank. Worse, his R map roams snowball other lanes while I'm stuck top. My only path is to have already banked a lead on my 3-6 windows, then group and use R to peel him off my carries in teamfights rather than trying to solo-duel a percent-HP sustain monster.","whys":["You both have weak level 1s — you only have Q with no engage and he can only Q-tongue you, so farm safe and set up the lane.","Tongue Lash only stuns at three An Acquired Taste stacks, but it heals him and Thick Skin banks whatever chip you land.","Your full Q-W combo lands — W a committed Tahm for the knockback-stun and Q3-pull him, faster than Thick Skin can convert it.","This is your tank lane-control peak — you trade around his cooldowns and bank small leads while his only answer is to soak and regen.","All Out converts you to a duelist and runs down a Tahm whose only exit is Abyssal Dive (21s) — your cleanest kill window.","His first tank item makes Devour and the three-stack Tongue Lash stun lethal, and Iceborn alone can't out-damage Thick Skin.","An Acquired Taste scales his damage off his own health and Thick Skin out-lasts your armour without Grievous Wounds — group and peel instead."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"teemo","win":["Teemo","Teemo","Skill","Skill","K'Sante","Skill","Teemo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Teemo blinds your Q autos and kites with passive move speed before you have W or E — you just farm and eat poison."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W combo comes online: W through his kite, then Q3's pull — your first window to actually touch him at all."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out shreds his squishy frame: R launches him through a wall and dashes after him, and he has no dash to escape it."},{"when":"Late","text":"Teemo's shroom walls and splitpush take over — your armor stacking does nothing to his on-hit poison and he zones you off the map."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Blinding Dart, then W through his kite into Q3's pull inside the 7s window","Reach Level 6 and launch him through a wall with R — his squishy frame folds and he has no dash back","Use E over a wall or to a wave to close the gap his poke can't punish, then commit your full combo"],"foe":["Blind your Q autos with his Q every trade so your passive mark and DPS go dark","Kite with passive move speed and E poison, keeping you at auto range you can't W-close","Survive to 2+ items and zone you with R shroom walls into a free splitpush"]},"early":"Teemo owns Levels 1-2 outright — Blinding Dart shuts off your autos and with them your passive mark, and Move Quick lets him kite the moment you step up, so last-hit at the tip of Q and accept the poison chip. Do not chase a Q into auto range he can simply blind; you have no W or E yet to close the gap. At Level 3 your Q-W combo finally comes online — bait the blind, W to eat the distance, then Q3 for the pull — but Toxic Shot keeps ticking as he walks, so it stays a coinflip skirmish.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a genuine even fight: you can W through his kite and stick a Q3, but Toxic Shot ticks for four seconds and the blind chips you back to neutral, so neither of you fully owns it. Level 6 is your one clean spike — All Out converts your tank stats into a duelist profile, and Teemo's squishy frame has no dash out of an R that launches him through a wall. Blinding Dart is a flat 7 seconds, so hold the all-in for that gap — blinding your empowered autos is the only thing that saves him.","late":"This is where you lose the matchup back. Your armor stacking is worthless against his on-hit poison and his shroom walls zone every choke, so he splitpushes a side lane and forces you to facecheck mushrooms to catch him. Once he has 2+ items his DPS through the blind out-races your sustain, and your R peel matters less when he's a map problem you can't pin down. You needed to bank a lead on your Level 6 window; if the lane went even, the late game tilts to him.","whys":["His Q blind cancels your Q autos and passive mark while you have no W or E to close — he kites you with passive move speed and you can only farm.","Still no combo online and he out-ranges you; his blind plus poison chip means every step up costs you health for nothing.","Your Q-W combo lands — W through his kite into a Q3 pull — but Toxic Shot ticks for 4 seconds while he walks, so it is an even skirmish.","You can W-close and Q3, but his E poison and blind reset the trade to neutral — neither side owns the window.","All Out shreds his squishy frame: R launches him through the wall, he has no dash back, and Blinding Dart is a flat 7 seconds.","Your first tank-engage item keeps you durable, but his blind plus poison off-cooldown trades it back — the all-in is a coinflip, not a free kill.","Armor does nothing to his on-hit poison; his shroom walls zone you and he splitpushes — his scaling and map pressure reclaim the lane."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"trundle","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full Q-W combo comes online — W an over-committed Trundle for the stun and Q3's two-stack pull, before Chomp drains enough of your AD to matter."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out turns the duel: R launches him through any wall in the way, his own Pillar of Ice included, and the damage boost burns down a drain-tank with no burst to punish your stripped bulk."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet online — your slow-field plus Q chain-slow pins him so he can't use W move-speed zone to reposition, and you out-disrupt his sustain in extended trades."},{"when":"Lvl 6 (his)","text":"Subjugate steals a chunk of your resistances and doubles the theft over 4 seconds — if he lands it mid-fight he flips a losing duel, so never all-in below half."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and W a committed Trundle for the stun, then Q3's two-stack pull before Chomp drains your AD","Use All Out's damage boost and healing to burn a drain-tank with no burst to exploit your lost resists","Pin him with Iceborn slow + Q chain-slow so his W move-speed zone can't kite or reset the fight"],"foe":["Open with Chomp — it resets his auto, so the wind-up is the tell — and steal your AD","Drop Pillar of Ice (21s) to wall off your W dash angle and block your path","Hold R for the all-in to steal your resistances and heal, flipping the duel when you commit low"]},"early":"Level 1 is a coin-flip farm window — you only have Q and no engage, and Chomp steals your attack damage, so don't trade autos you don't need. The lane swings your way at 3: once W and Q are both up you can W a Trundle who walks in for a pillar or a bite, stun him with the knockback, and Q3-pull at two stacks before his drain matters. Respect Pillar of Ice — 21 seconds at rank 1, and he drops it to block your W path, so bait it or angle your dash around it.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your control peak. You out-trade him around cooldowns: he's a sustain-grind drain-tank with no burst, so your bulk lets you sit in his face and your Passive move-speed keeps you on him. At 6, All Out is the swing — R launches him through any wall, his own pillar included, and though it strips your tankiness Trundle has no burst to punish the lost armour while your damage boost eats him down. The one thing to fear is Subjugate: it steals YOUR resistances and heals him, so never commit while you're low.","late":"This is the only place Trundle reclaims footing — he's a drain-tank built to out-sustain bruisers in long fights, and Frozen Domain raises his healing from every source while he stands on it, so fighting inside it is the mistake. Grievous Wounds, not more armour, is the answer to King's Tribute and Subjugate. Close it on your earlier windows: take side-lane fights at 6 and first item where your All Out and Iceborn disruption win, and don't bet on a 25-minute drain duel.","whys":["You have only Q with no engage and his Q-bite steals your AD — last-hit safely and don't feed him free drain stacks.","With W or E added you're safe, but you can't reliably lock him yet — set up the level-3 spike rather than over-extend.","Full Q-W online: W a committed Trundle for the knockback stun, then Q3's pull at two stacks, before Chomp drains your AD.","Your tank bulk lets you sit on him around cooldowns and your Passive move-speed keeps you in range his sustain can't kite.","All Out's damage boost burns down a drain-tank with no burst to punish your stripped resists — win the side-lane 1v1.","Iceborn slow plus Q chain-slow pins him so his W move-speed zone can't reset, and your disruption out-trades his sustain.","He out-sustains the very late game — Subjugate steals your resists and King's Tribute heals him, so bring Grievous Wounds or don't duel."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"tryndamere","win":["Tryndamere","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Tryndamere"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Tryndamere spins to last-hit and pokes with crit autos while you only have Q — concede the level and farm at max Q range."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W combo is online — W him as Spinning Slash (12s) commits, then Q3-pull for your first punish window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out can win the duel, but it strips your tank stats right as his Undying Rage makes him unkillable for 5s — don't ult into a full Fury bar."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two crit items in, Tryndamere spin-kites your short Q/W and R Undying Rage outlasts your burst — peel for your team instead of dueling him."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach your Level 3 Q-W combo and bank small leads while he must walk into Q range to fight","Use W's damage-reduced charge to punish his Spinning Slash, then Q3-pull him back in","Use R to recall him off your carry in fights rather than betting on a late 1v1 against Undying Rage"],"foe":["Spin in with Spinning Slash (E) to last-hit safely and stack crit autos on you","Bait your W and E, then spin in for a Fury-fuelled all-in once both are down","Pop R Undying Rage to survive your All Out burst and spin-kite you out once he has crit items"]},"early":"Level 1 belongs to him — he spins to last-hit and chips you with crit autos while you only have Q and no engage. Don't step up to throw a Q he can just walk through; farm at the tip of Q and eat a little poke. Once you hit 3 your Q-W combo flips it: bait Spinning Slash, W him for the knockback stun as he lands, then Q3-pull him back in. His Fury bar is the tell — if it's full, he wants you to commit so he can spin in and crit you down, so trade when it's low.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are yours. He has to walk into your range to do damage, so you trade around Spinning Slash's 12-second cooldown — W his dash, Q3-pull him back, and bank the bulk lead as a tank. Level 6 is a trap: All Out gives you a duelist profile but strips your armour right when Undying Rage makes him immortal for 5 seconds, so a full-commit ult into a topped-up Tryndamere just feeds him a free spin-down. Ult to peel or to finish him at low Fury, not to out-DPS a fresh R.","late":"This is where he reclaims it. Two crit items in, Tryndamere spin-kites your short-range Q and W, and Undying Rage simply outlasts any burst All Out can muster — you can't kill a man who survives at 1 HP for 5 seconds, and Bloodlust heals the rest unless Grievous Wounds is on him. Stop trying to win the side-lane 1v1. Your value is R: launch him through a wall away from your carry, then let your team collapse. Win on your earlier mid-game windows.","whys":["He spins to last-hit and pokes with crit autos while you have only Q and no engage — concede the level and farm at range.","He picks up W slow + dropback but you get W or E for safety — neither can punish the other yet, so it's a wash.","Your full Q-W combo lands: W stuns him as Spinning Slash commits, then Q3's pull drags him back in.","You trade around his E cooldown and your bulk banks small leads — he must walk into Q range to fight you.","All Out can win the duel but strips your tank stats right as his R Undying Rage turns him immortal for 5s — it's a coin flip.","Your first tank-engage item makes you durable and disruptive, but his crit start lets him spin-kite trades even — neither stomps.","Two crit items in he spin-kites your short Q/W and Undying Rage outlasts your burst without Grievous Wounds — peel, don't duel."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"urgot","win":["Urgot","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Corrosive Charge (Q) outranges Ntofo Strikes 800 to 450 and chunks you while you have no engage — concede the level and last-hit at max range."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W is online: W-charge through his slow into terrain for the stun, then the 2-stack Ntofo pull — your first real window to punch back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Fear Beyond Death is the kill threat, 100s at rank 1; All Out makes you a duelist but strips resists, so only flip the 1v1 when his R is down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After Iceborn/first tank piece you out-sustain his shotgun chip in a drawn-out sidelane fight — he can't burst through your stacking armor and your peel."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and W-charge into him so the wall-stun lands, then Q3 knock-up before his Q legs reset","Bait out Disdain (E) — 16s at rank 1 — then land W's stun and the Ntofo pull while it is down","Grind a long sustained fight where your tank stacking out-lasts his shotgun chip rather than trading single Qs"],"foe":["Poke you down with Q shotgun legs at range before you can close, abusing his Level 1 lead","Land Disdain (E), shielded as he charges, to dump you in Purge range where percent-HP shreds you","Hit the R fear-execute when you're low — his percent-max-HP and execute punish your big health bar"]},"early":"Urgot owns Level 1 — Corrosive Charge (Q) reaches 800 to your Ntofo Strikes' 450 and Echoing Flames autos chunk you while you have zero engage, so last-hit at the tip of Q and eat a little chip. Do NOT walk up to trade single Qs; he wins that exchange every time. It flips at Level 3 once Q-W is online: W-charge him into the wall for the stun, then the 2-stack Ntofo shockwave pulls him back in. W's charge also cuts the damage of his return trade — bank two clean ones and the lane is yours.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your control window — trade around Corrosive Charge's 10s cooldown and your bulk eats his chip better than he eats your sustained DPS. The danger is Disdain (E), 16s at rank 1: it shields him as he charges and hurls you into Purge range, where percent-max-HP melts your health bar. Bait it, then commit — your W stun and the Ntofo pull both land while it is down. At 6 respect Fear Beyond Death, 100s at rank 1; All Out wins the straight duel but strips your resists, so only flip the 1v1 when his R is down or you're topped up.","late":"This stays a coinflip-EVEN sidelane all game — neither of you hard-outscales the other. He's a tanky, immobile sustained-DPS bruiser whose percent-HP genuinely hurts your stacked armor, but your first item turns you durable and disruptive enough to out-last his shotgun chip in a long fight. Don't bet on bursting him; bet on grinding him down while you peel his execute window. Carry grievous-wounds value if his team has healing, and remember your R can pull a flipped carry out of his fear range in a teamfight — that peel, not the 1v1, is where you tilt this even lane your way.","whys":["Corrosive Charge (Q) outranges Ntofo Strikes 800 to 450 and chips you while you have no Level 1 engage — concede and farm.","He still pokes with Q legs but you pick up W or E for safety; the trade is closer but neither side commits — genuinely even.","Your Q-W lands: W stuns him into terrain and the 2-stack Ntofo pull follows before his 10s Corrosive Charge resets — your first window.","You trade around Corrosive Charge's 10s and your bulk out-lasts Purge chip — he must stand at 490 range to use it.","Fear Beyond Death executes you under the threshold, but All Out flips the 1v1 — whoever commits on the other's cooldown takes it.","Your first tank item makes you durable enough to out-sustain his shotgun chip, but his E-flip-into-Q-W can still punish a mistake — even.","Neither outscales: his percent-HP hurts your armor but your peel and sustain answer it — the lane stays a coinflip into a teamfight skirmish."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"vayne","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Vayne"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W is online — W her into a wall for the stun, then the 2-stack Ntofo pull, before Condemn (E) can peel you off."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out makes you a duelist and dashes you after Tumble, which she resets only every 6s at rank 1 — your cleanest window pre-items."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Iceborn Gauntlet the slow stops her kiting your 450-range Q, but three consecutive hits proc Silver Bolts as true damage through all your armour."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Two items in, Silver Bolts' true damage ignores all your tank stats and Condemn stuns you into terrain — she kites your W and out-DPSes any long fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Path Maker (W) against a wall to stun her, then the 2-stack Ntofo pull before Condemn answers","Hit Level 3 and force melee range while she still has no kiting buffer and your combo out-trades her tumble","Close the game on your tank-item spike — don't let it reach the 2+ item window where her true damage rules"],"foe":["Kite with Tumble, invisible while Final Hour is up, so your 450-range Q whiffs","Stack W Silver Bolts on you so her percent-max-HP true damage ignores every point of armor you build","Use Condemn to knock you into terrain the instant you W in, stunning you, then run you down"]},"early":"Vayne is one of the safest level 1s into me but she's also fragile and immobile until she gets attack speed, so I just farm with Q at level 1 and don't feed her free tumble resets. The instant I hit Level 3 I have my real threat: W Path Maker charged into a wall is a long stun, and if I catch her tumbling toward terrain I follow with Q3 to knock her up and pull her in. Bait her E condemn before I commit my W charge — if she burns condemn to peel an early step-up, my next all-in lands clean.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are yours: she has to walk up to last-hit and your Q on 3.5s out-pokes Tumble while your bulk eats her early autos. At 6 All Out is your best window all game — the dash range chases her Tumble and the duelist damage kills her before Silver Bolts ramp. The trick is Condemn: it knocks you back, and only stuns if you hit terrain, so start the fight off the wall and keep Footwork (E) to re-stick after she tumbles. Every fight you win here is one her items have not happened for yet.","late":"This is where it flips: once Vayne has Botrk and Shieldbow, Silver Bolts deals percent-max-HP true damage on every third consecutive hit, so the armour your passive and items stack does nothing against her. She kites your 450-range Q and your W charge with Tumble and Condemn, and in a long fight she out-DPSes you even through All Out's duelist stats. Your late plan is not to duel her — use R to launch her through a wall, off your carries and into your team, never to 1v1. If the game got here you missed your windows; close it on the earlier spikes.","whys":["She is safe at level 1 and so are you with only Q — neither side threatens a kill, so farm and deny her Tumble resets.","You pick up Path Maker and gain a real step-up threat while she has no attack speed to punish it.","Your W wall-stun and the 2-stack Ntofo shockwave pull land before she has the buffer to kite — you own melee range.","She must walk up to farm and your bulk eats her autos while Q on 3.5s out-trades Tumble poke through Levels 4-5.","All Out gives you dash range to chase her Tumble and damage to kill her before Final Hour and Silver Bolts ramp.","Iceborn's slow stops her kiting your 450-range Q, but Silver Bolts' third hit is true damage — genuinely even.","Silver Bolts' true damage ignores every point of armour you build and she kites your whole kit — peel with R, never duel her."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"vladimir","win":["Skill","Vladimir","Skill","Skill","K'Sante","Vladimir","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Tides of Blood pokes and Transfusion heals it straight back through your only Q — you have no engage threat, so farm."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W is online: bait the pool — 28s at rank 1 — then W him into terrain for the stun and the 2-stack Ntofo pull."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is your one clean kill window — R him before Sanguine Pool is up, and carry Grievous Wounds so Transfusion cannot undo it."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Sanguine Pool is 2s untargetable on 16s maxed — it blanks your R and your pull, and he out-heals the rest. His window, not yours."}],"wants":{"you":["Land W Path Maker against terrain while he is mid E-charge so the stun and knockback connect before he pools","Hit Level 6 and R All Out him before Sanguine Pool is up — your duelist stats burst his low resists","Force side-lane all-ins on your first tank item so the game ends before his AP items come online"],"foe":["Bait the Ntofo pull and W, then Sanguine Pool for 2s untargetable to waste your cooldown-reliant combo","Poke you down with E and heal it back with Q so you never bank a lane lead","Survive to 2+ AP items where Rylai-slow plus pool kiting makes him unkillable into your tank stats"]},"early":"Vladimir has no escape until W Sanguine Pool comes online, but you have no engage threat at Level 1 with just Q, so neither of you wins the opening — last-hit at the tip of Q and accept his E-charge poke without walking into auto range. The danger is his Q drain healing back every bit of chip you land, so don't waste your short cooldowns trading into a target that just sustains it off. By Level 3 your Q-W combo is up: this is your first real window, but his pool can blank it, so make him spend it on minions or bait it before you commit W into terrain.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are even — you out-position a pre-Rylai Vlad and bank small leads with your bulk, but any all-in can be blanked by Sanguine Pool's 2 seconds of untargetability, so force him to burn it first; it is 28s at rank 1 and only 16s maxed. Level 6 is your one clean window: All Out strips your tank stats but gives you a duelist 1v1, and Vlad's low base resists fold to your R burst IF you catch him before pool. Buy Grievous Wounds early, or Transfusion simply undoes the trade — this is the last point the matchup is yours.","late":"This is Vlad's game and you cannot win it late. He is a hard AP scaler whose Sanguine Pool makes him untargetable on command — it dodges your R All Out, your W charge, and your Q3 pull — while Rylai's slow and Liandry burn kite your move-speed-stacking passive and melt you regardless of how much armor you stack, because his damage is magic and percent-based. Don't bet on the late teamfight against him; close the side lane on your Level 6 and first-item windows, or accept that your job becomes peeling him off your carries rather than killing him.","whys":["Vlad is one of the weakest level-1s, but so are you — with only Q and no engage you just farm and deny his Q drain last-hits.","He charges Tides of Blood and heals it straight back with Transfusion while you lack a combo — his chip edges this level.","Your Q-W lands a terrain stun, but Sanguine Pool's 2s of untargetability blanks it — a coin-flip on whether his 28s pool is up.","You out-trade a pre-Rylai Vlad with your bulk, but he pools out of the Ntofo pull and W — neither reliably wins, so it is skill.","All Out converts you to a duelist and his low base resists fold to your R burst if you catch him before Sanguine Pool comes up.","Your first tank item is durable, but his AP item plus Transfusion healing out-sustains armour that does nothing to his magic.","He out-scales hard — untargetable pool dodges your R, and Rylai-slow plus Liandry magic damage ignores your armor and melts you."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"volibear","win":["Skill","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Volibear"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W lands: W-charge a committed Voli for the stun, then the 2-stack Ntofo pull while he is mid-bite — his own stun is 12s at rank 1."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is a coin-flip — it wins the raw 1v1 but strips your armour, so ult only once Thundering Smash is down and Grievous Wounds is up, or Frenzied Maul heals him through it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet makes you durable and sticky; you out-disrupt his dive and can W-knock him off your jungler at scuttle/grubs."},{"when":"Late","text":"Volibear's biggest window — full-build he out-brawls your stripped R form, Frenzied Maul heals through your damage, and Stormbringer's tower disable wins the dive."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 3 and W-stun a committed Voli, then pull with the 2-stack Ntofo while his Q sits on 12s","Bank a small lead Levels 4-5 with Q stacks and your bulk, trading around his W bite cooldown","Use R only as a peel/reposition tool late — recast to yank Voli off a carry rather than dueling his sustain"],"foe":["Land Thundering Smash's stun mid-combo and start the brawl on his terms, off a 12s cooldown","Land a second Frenzied Maul on you to heal through your damage and win the long fight","Reach 2+ items and his R to out-dive and out-brawl your armor-stripped All Out form"]},"early":"Level 1 you both just farm — you only have Q and no engage, and Thundering Smash stuns the first thing he attacks, so don't facecheck a trade before your combo is up. At Level 3 it swings your way: bait the dash, W-charge for your own stun, then pull him in with the 2-stack Ntofo. Watch his auto wind-up, not the cast — his Q is an attack reset. Respect Frenzied Maul: the second bite on the same target heals him, so never start a trade you cannot finish.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your control window: you out-position his 300-range Q dash, bank Ntofo stacks, and your bulk shrugs off chip he can only heal back with a second Frenzied Maul. At 6 the trap is Sky Splitter — 16s flat, it slows you and shields him if he stands in the blast, which is his cue to commit. Fight outside that circle, buy Grievous Wounds, and commit All Out only once his Q stun is down, because the moment you ult you give up the armour that keeps you alive in his brawl.","late":"This is where Voli reclaims it. Full-build a repeat Frenzied Maul heals straight through your tank damage and out-grinds your stripped All Out form, while Stormbringer's bonus health and tower disable win any dive around objectives. Stop trying to solo him — carry Grievous Wounds, flip R into a peel tool, and use it to launch him off your carry rather than betting on a 1v1 his sustain wins. Bank your mid-game lead into objectives before his scaling takes over.","whys":["You only have Q and no engage, and Thundering Smash stuns the first thing he hits — just farm and concede the level.","He picks up either bite or dash and so do you; neither can commit a clean all-in yet, so it stays a wash.","Your Q-W lands before Sky Splitter's shield is online — W-stun through the bite, then the Ntofo pull, and you win.","You out-position his short Q dash and bank Q stacks with your bulk, trading on his W-bite cooldown.","All Out wins the raw duel but strips your armour, while Sky Splitter's shield and repeat Frenzied Maul bites out-DPS it — a coin-flip.","Iceborn keeps you durable and sticky and you out-disrupt his dive, but his W sustain matches your damage so neither stomps lane.","Full-build Frenzied Maul heals through your damage and Stormbringer's bonus health plus tower disable out-dives your stripped R form."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"warwick","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W is online — W a committed Warwick into terrain for the stun, then the 2-stack Ntofo pull, and win the trade before Jaws heals it back."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your tank lane-control peak: bank small leads by trading around his Q heal cooldown while his W gives him no burst to punish you back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress is the threat window — 1.5s of suppression on 110s at rank 1, and nothing in your kit shortens it, so hold E's shield and dash for the moment it ends."},{"when":"Late","text":"From 2+ items Eternal Hunger heals triple under 25% HP and Jaws of the Beast bites for percent max health — armour is the wrong answer to a fed drain bruiser, so close earlier."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach your Level 3 Q-W combo and punish him before his Q drain can sustain the trade back","Bank small Level 4-5 leads with your bulk while his W gives him no way to burst you","Bait Infinite Duress, then punish the 110s cooldown with your full Q-W pattern"],"foe":["Drag the lane long so his passive lifesteal and Q heal grind you down in sustained fights","Land Infinite Duress while your dashes are down, or Primal Howl to fear you out of your combo","Scale into the late game where his chase (W move speed) and low-HP healing ignore your armor"]},"early":"Warwick is a non-threat at Level 1 — his early is Jaws of the Beast last-hits and he has no engage, so poke at the tip of Q and set up your lane. It flips your way at Level 3 when Q-W comes online: W him into the wall for the longer stun, then pull him back in with the 2-stack Ntofo. The key is timing — burst the trade fast, because if it drags, Jaws' heal and Eternal Hunger claw the HP straight back.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your peak as a tank — you out-trade a pre-item Warwick because his W only gives him move speed, no burst, so he can't punish your bulk. Trade around his Q drain cooldown and bank small leads. At 6 it evens out: his R is a full-channel suppress that holds you in place for the rest of his combo, so do NOT all-in with W down. Save W's unstoppable charge specifically to break the suppress and walk out of his commit.","late":"This is where Warwick reclaims the lane and you must respect it. His passive heals harder the lower your HP, and your entire identity — armor stacking — does nothing against a fed drain bruiser who chases with W move speed and sustains through your damage. R All Out makes you a duelist but strips your bulk, which is exactly what his sustained DPS punishes. Close the game on your 3-to-first-item windows; never let a fed Warwick catch you isolated in the side lane late.","whys":["Warwick has no engage at Level 1 and you have only Q — both of you just farm, so this is a genuine wash neither owns.","You pick up W or E and become safer while his W only grants move speed, giving you the cleaner level-2 trade.","Your Q-W lands — W into terrain for the stun, then the Ntofo pull — and you burst him before Jaws of the Beast heals it back.","Your tank lane-control peak: you out-trade around his Q cooldown and his burst-less W can't punish your bulk.","At 6 Infinite Duress suppresses you for 1.5s through everything, but it is 110s at rank 1 — bait it and the all-in is yours.","His first drain-tank item restores his sustain just as your first tank piece comes online — neither pulls clearly ahead.","Warwick out-scales you: Eternal Hunger triples its healing under 25% and Jaws is percent max health, so armour lies."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"wukong","win":["Skill","Wukong","Wukong","Wukong","K'Sante","Skill","Wukong"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W comes online — the one trading window where you charge W into him and land the 2-stack Ntofo pull before he Nimbus Strikes out."},{"when":"Lvl 2-5","text":"Wukong's threat window: Warrior Trickster's clone plus Crushing Blow's shred and Nimbus Strike's gap-close out-trade your early, worst when your Q is down."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is your equalizer — your duelist profile and R knockback can survive his E-Q-W-R combo and flip the 1v1 if you bait his ultimate spin first."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Wukong reclaims it: Crushing Blow's shred beats your armour stacking and Cyclone's AoE knockup makes him the bigger fight threat — peel, never duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach Level 3 and charge W into a committed Wukong, then Q3 to lock him before he E's out","Bait his clone (W) and his R spin, then All Out the real Wukong while his combo is down","Use R All Out to peel him off your carry when his ult knocks up your team"],"foe":["Drop the Warrior Trickster clone to bait your W charge, then Nimbus Strike in","Stack Q armor-shred so your tank itemization does nothing in the extended trade","Hit multiple targets with R's spin knockup in skirmishes where your peel is split"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — you only have Q with no engage, and he cannot commit without Nimbus Strike, so farm at the tip of Q. The problem starts at 2-3: Crushing Blow shreds your armour and Warrior Trickster's clone hides which body is real before you blow the W charge. Watch his auto wind-up, not the cast — Crushing Blow is an attack reset. Never spend W or the Ntofo pull on a decoy; whiff and he lands on you clean.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still his — he trades around your Q cooldown and Nimbus Strike's gap-close means you cannot punish him on the back foot the way you do an immobile bruiser. Your spike is 6: All Out gives you a duelist profile and R launches him out of Cyclone's spin, so bait the clone and the ultimate first, then dash onto the real Wukong while his lockdown is down. Win it here on a good R or you do not win it.","late":"This is where he reclaims it. His Q armor-shred ignores the exact thing you build into — armor stacking does nothing against a Wukong who melts it, and his R spin is a bigger teamfight tool than your single-target peel when fights are spread. Stop trying to 1v1 him with two items down; use R All Out to recall him off your carry instead of dueling, and let your team punish the windows after his ult is committed.","whys":["Neither of you has a real engage at 1 — you have only Q, he can't commit without E — so it is a farm standoff.","Crushing Blow shreds your armour and Warrior Trickster's clone baits your cooldowns before your full combo exists.","He out-trades around your Q using Nimbus Strike to gap-close faster than your 600-range W charge can answer.","His E dash means you cannot punish him the way you punish immobile bruisers, so he banks the lane-control window.","All Out makes you a duelist and your R launches him out of Cyclone — bait the clone and the spin, then dash onto the real him.","Your first tank-engage item is durable but his Q shred and E mobility keep the side-lane fight even.","Crushing Blow's shred beats armour stacking and Cyclone's AoE knockup out-scales single-target peel — launch him with R, never duel."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"yasuo","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Yasuo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Ntofo Strikes plus Path Maker is online — W a committed Yasuo for the stun, then the 2-stack pull, before his crit pattern is dangerous."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your lane-control peak: bank leads in melee, where Wind Wall's 4 seconds block nothing and Sweeping Blade needs a target to dash off."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is double-edged — it wins the 1v1 but strips your tankiness, so commit R only once his 2-stack Steel Tempest is spent and his shield is popped."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Yasuo's takeover: crit items plus Wind Wall, 17s maxed and 4 seconds long, blank your Q entirely — armour stacking does nothing. His window, not yours."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach the level-3 combo: W a committed Yasuo, then the 2-stack Ntofo pull, before his crit scales","Fight in melee where Windwall blocks nothing, banking small tank leads at levels 4-5","Close the game on your mid-game item windows before his crit build out-duels your stripped-down R profile"],"foe":["Hold Wind Wall's 4 seconds to eat your Q poke, then Sweeping Blade through minions to reset distance","Stack crit items and flow past two items where he shreds your armor and out-DPSes your All Out duelist form","Bait your W charge and E-dash out, then re-engage with Steel Tempest knockup into his own R when you're on cooldown"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you only have Q, so farm and stay out of his Steel Tempest pokes while he stacks the tornado. The shift is level 3: with Path Maker and Ntofo Strikes online you can W a Yasuo who steps up to last-hit and pull him in before his crit pattern means anything. Wind Wall does nothing if you engage in melee — it only eats a Q thrown from range, so close first, then poke. Don't burn W early: bait the dash, and note his passive shield builds while he walks, so pop it before you commit.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are yours as a tank — you trade around Sweeping Blade, soak his crit autos with your bulk, and bank small leads because he cannot kite a champion who walks him down. At 6 All Out is a trap if misused: the duelist conversion wins a straight 1v1 but strips your armour exactly when a 2-stack Steel Tempest knockup hands him free Last Breath, so commit R only once that is spent. Fake a Q to bait Wind Wall — 25s at rank 1 — then fight in melee where it is worthless.","late":"This is where it slips. Yasuo is a hard scaler — once crit items land, Wind Wall blanks every ranged poke you own and your tank identity falls apart against crit DPS that does not care about armour stacking. All Out gives you damage but takes your bulk, and a full-build Yasuo out-DPSes that stripped profile. Cash your mid-game leads before two items: end the game, or pivot to peeling him off your carries with R's knockback rather than solo-duelling a champion whose passive shield eats your opener.","whys":["Level 1 you only have Ntofo Strikes and no engage threat, but so does a tornado-stacking Yasuo — farm, dodge his Steel Tempest pokes, and concede nothing.","You pick up Path Maker or Footwork and become safe enough to trade — step on him when his E-dash is on cooldown and he can't reset distance.","Your Q-W is online: W a committed Yasuo, then pull with the 2-stack Ntofo — his crit pattern cannot punish it yet, and Wind Wall is dead weight in melee.","Levels 4-5 are your tank lane-control peak — you trade around his E cooldown and out-position his short crit range, banking small leads with your bulk.","All Out is double-edged: it wins the 1v1 but strips your tankiness, so commit only once his 2-stack Steel Tempest is spent — Last Breath needs that knockup.","Your first tank-engage item keeps you durable and disruptive, but a pre-crit Yasuo trades back enough that this window is genuinely contested, not owned.","He out-scales hard: crit items plus Wind Wall — 4 seconds blocking every Q you throw — beat armour stacking, so peel him, never duel him."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"yone","win":["Skill","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Yone"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W comes online — bait the 2-stack Mortal Steel dash, then W-charge him into a wall for the stun and the Ntofo pull. Force Spirit Cleave first."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is a coin-flip spike: it gives you a duelist 1v1 but strips your bulk, and Soul Unbound — 22s at rank 1 — rewinds him out of your engage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet makes you durable and disruptive — your Q slow plus W stun forces side-lane fights before his crit items come online."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Yone's threat window: two crit items make his knockup into Fate Sealed lethal, and Soul Unbound plus a Spirit Cleave shield out-DPS your stripped body."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait the 2-stack Mortal Steel dash, then W-charge him into a wall and pull with the Ntofo shockwave","Lock in your Levels 3-5 tank control window and bank small leads before his crit items spike","Save R All Out to peel him off your carry, not to greedily 1v1 his mobile late-game build"],"foe":["Weave Mortal Steel and Soul Unbound to dodge your 450-range Q, then poke from spirit form","Land his Q3 knock-up into R for the all-in once he has two crit items","Stall lane even and scale into a mobile carry your armor stacking does nothing against"]},"early":"Level 1 you have only Q and no engage, so farm at Ntofo Strikes range — Mortal Steel matches it and Spirit Cleave beats you if you step up early. Level 2 makes you safer, and at Level 3 the full kit is online: your first real window. Bait the 2-stack Mortal Steel dash — when he commits it, W-charge him into a wall for the stun, then pull him in. Force Spirit Cleave out first; it shields him on 14s and eats your opener. Never throw a raw Q at a Yone holding Soul Unbound; he rewinds out of the pull.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your lane-control peak as a tank — trade around Mortal Steel's 4s and Spirit Cleave's 14s, eat the cleave on your armour, and bank small leads while he must walk into Q range to farm. At 6 it goes even: All Out gives you a duelist profile that wins the straight 1v1, but it strips your bulk, and Soul Unbound — 22s at rank 1, 10s maxed — snaps him back to his body and repeats his damage. So never burn R on a full-health Yone: bait E and W first, then commit when he has nothing left to rewind to.","late":"This is where Yone reclaims it. With two crit or lethality items the 2-stack Mortal Steel knockup into Fate Sealed is real burst, and Soul Unbound plus a stacked Spirit Cleave shield out-DPS your All Out body once your tank stats are converted away — armour stacking means nothing against a fed mobile carry. Don't bet on the very late 1v1: close on your Levels 3-5 and first-item windows, where Iceborn and the W stun force fights he cannot kite. Past two items, stop duelling in the side lane and play for fights — survive the burst, then R to launch him off your carry.","whys":["Neither of you threatens at Level 1 — Mortal Steel matches your Ntofo Strikes at 450 range and no one has a dash yet, so just farm.","You are safer with W or E up, but Mortal Steel and Spirit Cleave match your chip — an even stretch until your combo lands.","Your Q-W lands: bait the 2-stack Mortal Steel dash, W-charge him into a wall for the stun, then the Ntofo pull — your first real trade.","Levels 4-5 are your tank control peak — trade around his cooldowns and bank leads with bulk while he walks into Q range to farm.","All Out is a coin-flip: it wins the duelist 1v1 but strips your bulk, and Soul Unbound — 22s at rank 1 — rewinds him out of your engage.","Iceborn keeps you durable and disruptive, but his first crit item holds the lane even — your Q slow and W stun force fights before he spikes.","Two crit items let his knockup-into-Fate Sealed burst and Soul Unbound kiting out-DPS your stripped All Out body — armour does nothing, so peel, never duel."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"yorick","win":["Skill","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W lands — W-charge through Mourning Mist's slow to stun him, then the Ntofo pull: your clean melee window before Maiden."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out lets you dash through him and survive the ghoul swarm, but it strips your bulk right as Maiden adds sustained DPS — commit only with Dark Procession down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet makes you durable enough to dive his wave and reset his Maiden cooldown by forcing the all-in."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick's threat window: Maiden, ghouls and a 12s Dark Procession wall box you in the side lane, and he 1v1s or splits faster than you answer."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Mourning Mist, then W-charge through the slow so the stun lands and the Ntofo pull follows","Fight when Maiden is dead or on cooldown so you face Yorick alone, not the whole swarm","Use R All Out to dash past the ghoul wall and isolate Yorick, then end the game on your mid-game item windows"],"foe":["Box you in with Dark Procession's wall while ghouls and Maiden chunk you down","Drop W wall to box you off the wave or wall you in for a free ghoul-stacked trade","Avoid the Ntofo pull and W stun, summon Maiden, and grind the side lane until his split outpaces you"]},"early":"Level 1 you have only Q, no engage, and walking into ghoul range just lets him stack Mourning Mist on you for free — last-hit at the tip of your Q and concede the level. The lane flips at 3 once your kit is online: bait Mourning Mist, 12s at rank 1, then W-charge through the slow for the stun and pull him in with the 2-stack Ntofo. Watch his auto wind-up — Last Rites is an attack reset that heals him, so carry Grievous Wounds.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are yours as a tank — you out-trade a Yorick who has to walk past his own ghouls to reach you, and you bank small leads on Mourning Mist's 12s cooldown. At 6 your R is a real 1v1: launch him, eat the ghoul burst your W charge already reduced, and your duelist profile beats him before Maiden is stacked — but it sheds your bulk, so never pop it into a fresh Maiden. Force the all-in while Dark Procession is down; that is when he is a melee with no wall.","late":"This is where you lose the bet. Yorick is a hard scaler — full Maiden, a permanent ghoul swarm, and his W wall mean that in a side lane he traps you and 1v1s through your armor, which does nothing against four ghouls plus Maiden DPS. Your R peels for a teamfight, but he just splits the other side and takes towers faster than you answer. Close the game on your Levels 3-6 windows; never let it become a side-lane scaling race you can't win.","whys":["He has only Last Rites at level 1 too, but Mist Walkers and Mourning Mist poke free — last-hit at Q tip, out of ghoul range.","He picks up W wall or E cage; you pick up W or E to become safer, but neither side has a clean kill yet, so it stays even.","Your Q-W is online — W-charge through Mourning Mist's slow for the stun, then the Ntofo pull, before Maiden exists.","You out-trade a Yorick who must path past his own ghouls, banking leads on Mourning Mist's 12s cooldown.","All Out dashes you through him and survives the ghoul-swarm burst to win the 1v1 before he stacks a full Maiden.","Iceborn makes you durable enough to dive his wave, but Maiden's sustained DPS answers it — genuinely contested.","Maiden, ghouls and Dark Procession's wall let him 1v1 through your armour and split faster than your team answers."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"zac","win":["K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Zac"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Your Q comes back every 3.5s while Stretching Strikes sits on 14s — chip him at 450 range and step on every blob he sheds."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W is online — W-stun a committed Zac, then the 2-stack Ntofo pull, and punish him before he eats his blobs."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out is a coinflip: it out-duels a blob-less Zac but strips your bulk, so ult only with Grievous Wounds up and Elastic Slingshot's 21s spent."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Zac's biggest window — Unstable Matter chews percent max health every 5s, and the Cell Division revive means you rarely get a clean kill."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 3, W-stun a committed Zac, then Ntofo-pull him before the blobs sustain the trade back","Bait his E sling and Q/W CC, then all-in on the cooldowns while he can't re-engage or peel","Use R All Out to peel his E-sling engage off your carry in mid-game teamfights rather than for the 1v1"],"foe":["Sling in with E, land Q/W CC, and grind an even trade his passive blobs heal back","Reabsorb Cell Division blobs to out-sustain your Q poke and dodge your W charge","Scale to 2+ items where his teamfight engage and blob revive outlast your tank shred"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours in small doses — Ntofo Strikes is up every 3.5 seconds and his only ability, Stretching Strikes, is a 14-second grab, so chip him at 450 and deny the blobs. The lane opens at Level 3 when Q-W comes online: if he slings in or walks up to last-hit, W-stun the committed Zac, then pull him back with the 2-stack Ntofo. Watch his auto wind-up — Stretching Strikes resets it. Keep stepping on blobs, or every trade you win gets healed back.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your peak: you out-position Elastic Slingshot, 21 seconds at rank 1, bank small leads with your bulk, and trade around Unstable Matter's 5s. Bait the sling, then commit W and the Ntofo pull while it is down and he cannot re-engage. At 6, All Out is a genuine coinflip — it beats a Zac with no blobs up, but it strips your bulk, so ult only with Grievous Wounds bought and no blob pile behind him to heal on.","late":"This is where Zac reclaims it. At 2+ items Unstable Matter takes a percentage of your max health every 5 seconds, so stacking armour is the wrong answer, and the Cell Division revive means a kill you earned stands back up. Don't bet on solo-killing him late — your value is R, launching his sling engage off your carry and out of the fight. Close on your Level 1-5 windows; the longer it goes, the more his sustain and pick threat outscale your lockdown.","whys":["Level 1 you chip with Ntofo Strikes every 3.5s while Stretching Strikes sits on 14s — his one ability whiffs and you win.","He picks up W or you pick up E — it stays even because his passive blobs sustain any poke you land before your combo is online.","Your Q-W lands: W-stun the committed Zac, then the Ntofo pull, and out-trade him before Cell Division heals it.","Your tank lane-control peak — you out-position Elastic Slingshot, 21s at rank 1, and trade around Unstable Matter's 5s.","All Out can win the duel but strips your tankiness, and Zac just slings to a blob pile to reset — it's a coinflip, not a free spike.","Your first item is durable, but Cell Division's blobs match your shred unless you step on them — even, not favoured.","At 2+ items Unstable Matter's percent-HP and the Cell Division revive beat armour stacking — peel with R, never solo him."]},
  {"a":"ksante","b":"ziggs","win":["Ziggs","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","K'Sante","Ziggs"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your Q-W is online — if Ziggs steps up to shove, W-stun him and Ntofo-pull him in for a real chunk while Satchel is on 20s."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"All Out gives you a duelist 1v1 and the gap-close to reach Ziggs, but it strips your tankiness — commit only with Satchel Charge's 20s and Flash down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Iceborn Gauntlet plus your E over the wall lets you finally stick to him and force a side-lane fight he can't kite out of."},{"when":"Late","text":"From two items Ziggs out-ranges your whole kit — 850-range bombs and a 5000-range Mega Inferno Bomb chunk you before you reach, and armour does nothing."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his W Satchel and E minefield, then E over a wall or W-charge in to close the gap before they're back up","Reach Level 3 and use your Q-W lockdown the moment he over-extends to shove the wave","Get Iceborn Gauntlet so the slow lets you stick through his kite and end the lane in the side"],"foe":["Bomb you with Q from max range every wave so you eat poke walking up to CS","Zone you off the wave with Hexplosive Minefield's 16s slow and deny you farm","Save W Satchel to knock you out of your W-charge or All Out gap-close and reset the poke war"]},"early":"Ziggs out-ranges everything you have at Levels 1-2 — Bouncing Bomb is 850 to your 450 — so take the safe CS at the tip of your Q and accept some chip. The lane turns at Level 3: the second he steps forward to shove, W-charge in for the stun, then pull him with the 2-stack Ntofo and make him pay for the poke he was free-casting. Watch his auto wind-up too: Short Fuse is an attack reset. He has zero escape once you reach him — reaching him is the whole problem.","mid":"This is your best stretch of lane. Bait Satchel Charge — 20s at rank 1, and his only knockback to break your engage — then E over a wall or W-charge in and pull him; without it he cannot peel your lockdown. At 6, All Out lets you dash through him and win the straight 1v1, but it converts your tank stats to duelist, so ult only when Satchel and Flash are down. Iceborn Gauntlet is the real unlock: the slow finally lets you stick through his kite instead of watching him walk backward casting bombs.","late":"Past two items this flips to him and you have to respect it — Ziggs is pure artillery and your armor stacking does literally nothing against his AP. On Baron and Dragon he chunks your whole team from a screen away with Q bombs and his R before you can ever W-charge in, and your job shrinks to flanking with E and R to pull him out, not winning a poke war you can't win. Close the map on your Level 3-to-first-item windows; if it goes long and even, his range owns the objective fights.","whys":["Ziggs out-ranges you with Q bombs and you only have Q — you can't trade, so just farm at max range and concede the level.","He still pokes you walking up to CS, but you pick up Path Maker and get safer — a wash, neither side kills.","Your Q-W is online — W-stun him and Ntofo-pull the instant he steps up to shove, while Satchel Charge sits on 20s.","You out-trade him at melee range with your bulk and lockdown — every time he over-extends to push, you punish.","All Out wins the 1v1 and gap-closes, but it strips your tankiness — a coinflip if Satchel Charge is up to knock you away.","Iceborn Gauntlet's slow lets you finally stick through his kite and force a side fight he can't escape.","He out-scales hard — 850-range bombs and a 5000-range R out-range your whole kit, and armour does nothing to AP."]}
